var scenariolist = [
["Tutorial Scenarios"],
["tutorial.xml", "Tutorial — Khalkhin Gol", "Tutorial — Khalkhin Gol<br>3 July 1939<br>Japanese forces have crossed the Khalkhin Gol and occupied positions around the Bain-Tsagan heights. The first three turns are an AI-controlled demonstration of objectives, unit information, transport, reconnaissance, artillery preparation, support fire, reinforcement, resupply, and OverRun. At the start of turn 4, full control of the Soviet-Mongolian detachment passes to you. Capture the Khaylastyn Crossing and the Hamar-Daba Command Post; the Bain-Tsagan Observation Point is optional.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [20, 24]}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["Red Army Campaign (1936-1945)"],
["bn9s00.xml", "Battle of Sesena", "BATTLE OF SESENA - 29 OCT 1936<br><br>South of Madrid, Spain<br><br>Comrade, here is your order - Move west with your armored forces and occupy the towns of Esquivias and Illescas! Support this move with your air force. Your infantry occupied Sesena and defend the town against enemy attacks. Good luck!<br><br>ORDERS<br>After 8 turns control 3/2/1 VH for a BV/V/TV.", [{"id": 1, "country": 28}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [26]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s01.xml", "Battle of Lake Khasan", "BATTLE OF LAKE KHASAN - 2 AUG 1938<br><br>Lake Khasan, Far East of Soviet Union<br><br>The sneaky Japanese attacked and beaten our border troops on the Bezymyannaya and Zaozyornaya hills. Attack the Japanese with superior power and recapture the territories we deserve!<br><br>ORDERS<br>After 9 turns control 7/6/5 VH for a BV/V/TV.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank (+1)<br>2x Infantry (+2)<br>1x Reconnaissance<br>1x Artillery (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s02.xml", "Khalkhin Gol", "KHALKHIN GOL - 3 JUL 1939<br><br>Khalkhin Gol River, Mongolian People's Republic<br><br>The Japanese crossed the Khalkhin Gol river in the north, occupied the Baintsagan hills and tried to surround our troops with a two-pronged assault. Carry out a vigorous counterattack, thwart the enemy intentions and occupy the Japanese positions west and east of the river!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>3x Infantry (+1)<br>1x Reconnaissance<br>1x Artillery<br>1x Fighter Aircraft (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [23]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s03.xml", "Battle of Grodno", "BATTLE OF GRODNO - 20 SEP 1939<br><br>Southeast of Grodno, East Poland<br><br>Move your units across the city of Grodno to the Lithuanian border. Occupy the city and vicinity and break any resistance!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Capture all VH!<br>b. Prevent that more than 2 enemy ground units cross the Polish-Lithuanian border (Exit Points).<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>4x Infantry (+1)<br>2x Reconnaissance (+1)<br>2x Artillery (+1)<br>1x Fighter Aircraft<br>1x Tactical Bomber (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [60]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s04.xml", "Raate Road", "RAATE ROAD - 2 JAN 1940<br><br>Raate-Suomussalmi Road, Eastern Finland<br><br>Our comrades from the 163rd division in Suomussalmi are cut off and need help. Break through the enemy encirclement and restore the supply route!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Reach the Exit Point (Road to Suomussalmi) with at least 5 of your ground units.<br>b. Prevent that the enemy destroy more than 4 of your units.<br><br>NOTES<br>a. The Finns will try to surprise you. Be aware!<br>b. Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>4x Infantry<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>2x Artillery<br>2x Fighter Aircraft (+1)<br>1x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s05.xml", "Vyborg Bay", "VYBORG BAY - 5 MAR 1940<br><br>Karelian Isthmus, Finland<br><br>The Finns asked for a ceasefire because their front is collapsing. But before peace comes, we have to capture the west bank of Vyborg Bay and the city itself! <br><br>ORDERS<br>After 10 turns control 10/8/6 VH for a BV/V/TV.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>4x Infantry<br>1x Anti-Tank (+1)<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>3x Artillery (+1)<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>1x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s06.xml", "Battle of Bialystok-Minsk", "BATTLE OF BIALYSTOK-MINSK - 27 JUN 1941<br><br>West of Minsk, Belarus<br><br>The treacherous Germans have launched a general attack on our homeland. The western front has collapsed and most of our troops are threatened to be encircled west of Minsk. Escape before the pocket closes! Make your way through the mess to the east!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Reach the Exit Points in time with at least 10 of your ground units before the enemy capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>a. You can't deploy your air force.<br>b. All friendly auxiliary troops are controlled by the AI - you only command your core units.<br>c. Save your core units! Reach the Exit Points as soon as possible - don't get into a fight you can't win. There should also be useful attachments to make your units faster!<br>d. Attention - summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>2x Tank<br>4x Infantry<br>1x Anti-Tank<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>3x Artillery<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>1x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}, {"id": 2, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s07.xml", "Yelnya Offensive", "YELNYA OFFENSIVE - 2 SEP 1941<br><br>Yelnya, Southeast of Smolensk<br><br>You'll lead the attack against the semi-circular Yelnya salient which the Germans had extended 50 kilometres south-east of Smolensk, forming a staging area for an offensive towards Vyazma and eventually Moscow. Eliminate the threat and win the much-needed victory for us, Comrade!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Capture all VH!<br>b. Prevent that more than 9 enemy ground units reach the Exit Points.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>3x Tank (+1)<br>4x Infantry<br>1x Anti-Tank<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>1x Flak (+1)<br>3x Artillery<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>2x Tactical Bomber (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s08.xml", "Battle of Moscow", "BATTLE OF MOSCOW - 9 DEC 1941<br><br>Dmitrow, North of Moscow<br><br>The German offensives against our capital were halted and our strategic counter-offensive started. Your goal is to cross the Moscow-Leningrad railway line and to liberate the city of Klin.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>3x Tank<br>4x Infantry<br>1x Anti-Tank<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>1x Flak<br>4x Artillery (+1)<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>2x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s09.xml", "Second Battle of Kharkov", "SECOND BATTLE OF KHARKOV - 12 MAY 1942<br><br>Volchansk, Northeast of Kharkov<br><br>We'll start an offensive to liberate Kharkov. With a dual pincer movement from the Volchansk and Barvenkovo salients, we'll surround and free the city. The main attack takes place in the south, your job is to lead the northern attack.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Kill 64 enemy units and prevent that the enemy destroy more than 15 of your units.<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement, if wanted.<br><br>CORE (recommended) <br>4x Tank (+1)<br>5x Infantry (+1)<br>2x Anti-Tank (+1)<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>1x Flak<br>4x Artillery<br>2x Fighter Aircraft<br>2x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 37, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s10.xml", "Battle of Voronezh", "BATTLE OF VORONEZH - 28 JUN 1942<br><br>Volovo, Northwest of Voronezh<br><br>The Germans launch an offensive towards Voronezh. Strong forces are trying to break through our defensive positions. Delay the advance of the fascists until we bring up reserves to defense the city!<br><br>ORDERS<br>After 10 turns control 8/7/5 VH for a BV/V/TV.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>4x Tank<br>5x Infantry<br>2x Anti-Tank<br>2x Reconnaissance<br>2x Flak (+1)<br>4x Artillery<br>3x Fighter Aircraft (+1)<br>2x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 41]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s11.xml", "Tatsinskaya Raid", "TATSINSKAYA RAID - 22 DEC 1942<br><br>Bol'shinka, 200km west of Stalingrad<br><br>You'll lead a raid deep into the German rear - the target is the enemy airfield at Tatsinskaya, the primary operating base for the German airlift efforts to Stalingrad. Inflict significant losses on enemy Air Force by destroying as many planes as possible and force the Germans to divert forces attempting to relieve their forces encircled in Stalingrad!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Reach the Exit Point with at least 8 of your ground units.<br><br>NOTES<br>a. You don't have to control all VH! You just have to ensure that you keep at least one VH occupied so that the enemy can't win.<br>b. Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>4x Tank<br>5x Infantry<br>2x Anti-Tank<br>3x Reconnaissance (+1)<br>2x Flak<br>4x Artillery<br>3x Fighter Aircraft<br>2x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s12.xml", "Third Battle of Kharkov", "THIRD BATTLE OF KHARKOV - 7 MAR 1943<br><br>South of Kharkov, Ukraine<br><br>We expect a German attack on Kharkov again. Stop the attack and inflict maximum losses on the enemy!<br><br>ORDERS<br>After 10 turns control 6/4/3 VH for a BV/V/TV.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>4x Tank<br>5x Infantry<br>2x Anti-Tank<br>3x Reconnaissance<br>2x Flak<br>4x Artillery<br>3x Fighter Aircraft<br>3x Tactical Bomber (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s13.xml", "Battle of Kursk", "BATTLE OF KURSK - 11 JUL 1943<br><br>South of Kursk, Russia<br><br>Despite our prepared defensive positions the Germans continue their advance on Kursk. You will counterattack at Prokhorovka and throw back the Germans before they break through the last lines of defense towards Kursk.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement, if wanted.<br><br>CORE (recommended)<br>4x Tank<br>5x Infantry<br>3x Anti-Tank (+1)<br>3x Reconnaissance<br>2x Flak<br>4x Artillery<br>4x Fighter Aircraft (+1)<br>4x Tactical Bomber (+1)", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn9s14.xml", "Zhitomir-Berdichev Offensive", "ZHITOMIR-BERDICHEV OFFENSIVE - 27 DEC 1943<br><br>East of Zhitomir, Ukraine<br><br>You task is to defeat the opposing German 4th Panzer Army of Army Group South and the liberation of the Zhytomyr Oblast region, including the cities of Zhitomir and Berdichev.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.<br><br>CORE (recommended - Core build phase completed)<br>5x Tank (+1)<br>6x Infantry (+1)<br>3x Anti-Tank<br>3x Reconnaissance<br>2x Flak<br>5x Artillery (+1)<br>4x Fighter Aircraft <br>4x Tactical Bomber", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [17, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [47]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s15.xml", "Crimean Offensive", "CRIMEAN OFFENSIVE - 7 MAY 1944<br><br>East of Sevastopol, Crimea peninsula<br><br>You're honored to liberate our beloved Sevastopol. The Germans and Romanians have already started evacuation by sea. Don't let a single man escape across the sea!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Capture all VH!<br>b. Prevent that more than 4 enemy ground (naval) units reach the Exit Points.<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement, if wanted.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s16.xml", "Jassy-Kishinev Offensive", "JASSY-KISHINEV OFFENSIVE - 20 AUG 1944<br><br>North of Jassy, Eastern Romania<br><br>In our major offensive on Romania you and your troops will be deployed on the right wing of the attack front. The goal is to encircle and destroy the enemy's 6th Army.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s17.xml", "Belgrade Offensive", "BELGRADE OFFENSIVE - 12 OCT 1944<br><br>West of Belgrade, Serbia<br><br>The time has come to liberate the Serbian capital from the fascist bondage! With the support of the  Yugoslav Partisans and the Bulgarian Army, it should not be difficult to drive out the Germans and their collaborators.<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}, {"id": 2, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s18.xml", "Lake Balaton Counterattack", "LAKE BALATON COUNTERATTACK - 16 MAR 1945<br><br>East of Lake Balaton, Hungary<br><br>The German offensive flagged - the enemy isn't be able to break through to the Danube. Time for us to attack. Advance to Lake Balaton and crush the enemy formations!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention - winter conditions! If possible, equip your troops with tracked movement. Check if you can switch between wheeled and tracked movement for free.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s19.xml", "Road to Vienna", "ROAD TO VIENNA - 3 APR 1945<br><br>East of Vienna, Austria<br><br>The Germans are on the run - withdrawing towards Vienna. Chase the enemy and destroy as many units as possible so that the enemy cannot establish an effective line of defense in front of Vienna!<br><br>ORDERS<br>a. Capture all VH!<br>b. Prevent that more than 44 enemy ground units reach the Exit Points.<br><br>NOTES<br>Attention summer conditions! Don't forget to switch back to wheeled movement, if wanted.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn9s20.xml", "Manchurian Offensive", "MANCHURIAN OFFENSIVE - 9 AUG 1945<br><br>Khabarovsk, Far Eastern Russia<br><br>At the Tehran and Yalta Conference, the Soviet Union has promised to enter the Pacific Theater within three months after the end of the war in Europe. So we are going to smash the Japanese puppet state of Manchukuo with a powerful operation. Your task is to overcome the border rivers near Khabarovsk and quickly advance westward into the interior!<br><br>ORDERS<br>Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Stay Alive - Red Partisans (1941-1945)"],
["bn5s01.xml", "RP Guerrilla Hunter", "GUERRILLA HUNTER - 2 JUL 1941<br><br>HQ 8th NKVD Rife Brigade, Estonia<br>CO General Kuznetsov<br><br>It does not look good for us, Comrade! The Germans stand at the Estonian border and all over crawled Bandits out of their holes. Minutes ago, I was informed about a upcoming guerrilla attack. It seems the Estonian Forest Brothers try to free some of their guerrilla fighters from her imprisonment. A Estonian commando, flown in from Finland lead the operation.<br><br>Order: Protect our prison building, search & destroy the ERNA commando and all Bandits!", [{"id": 1, "country": 58}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn5s02.xml", "RP German Blitz", "BLITZ - 10 JUL 1941<br><br>HQ 8th NKVD Rife Brigade, Estonia<br>CO General Kuznetsov<br><br>The Nazi war machine stand at our gates, Comrade! And your fate is the defense of Dorpat. Hold the city as long as you can, a train with important war goods must pass your position before the city falls.<br><br>Note: Buy cheap Militia to block the German advance. <br><br>Order: Protect the train, resist the German attack for 10 rounds and hold as much VH as possible!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [58]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s09.xml", "RP Sink the Tirpitz", "SINK THE TIRPITZ - 5 OCT 1941<br><br>HQ Soviet Partisans, Estonia<br>CO General Karotamm<br><br>The largest German battleship, the Tirpitz, flagship of a fleet, which has supported the German landings on the Baltic islands, anchored off the coast and poses a serious threat for our Baltic fleet.<br>Maritime forces are not available that could match with this ship. The Harbor defense prevent submarine attacks and air attacks are useless against the strong armour. Therefore, the Germans believe their battleship is safe.<br>But an daring Guerrilla - Commando attack could succeed. The high command subordinate 3 Naval-Commandos to your forces. Find a way to sink the Tirpitz!<br><br>Order: Sink the Battleship! Use the air-, sea- and land-transport capability of the Commandos. Use your Partisan and Saboteur units to slow down the German advance by blow up ports, roads and bridges or lay mines.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [58]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [361]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s03.xml", "RP Hit & Run", "HIT & RUN - 28 APR 1942<br><br>HQ Soviet Partisans, Lithuania<br>CO General Karotamm<br><br>Comrade, its time to strike the invaders where it hurts. You'll attack a weak defended German supply depot and raise the Red Banner on its ruins! The Germans did not expect large partisan forces in this area and need some time to react. Take advantage of surprise, but be fast! It's a dangerous mission, speed is everything here!<br><br>Order: Reach the EH (red-border hex) and retreat 3 units.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [60]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s08.xml", "RP Revenge", "REVENGE - 8 OCT 1942<br><br>HQ Soviet Partisans, Latvia<br>CO General Karotamm<br><br>Parts of an SS-Division were moved in our area for rest and refreshing. It is a unit well-known as Anti-Partisan combat formation and has spread terror among the Soviet population.<br>This is our chance for revenge! Your force should be strong enough to enclose and wipe out this devils. Especially the leaders of this bunch should receive no mercy.<br><br>Order: Search & destroy three enemy unit. The units can be identified by an extra frame around their unit strength.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [59, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s06.xml", "RP Gypsy Baron", "OPERATION GYBSY BARON - 15 JUN 1943<br><br>HQ Soviet Partisans, Belarus<br>CO General Karotamm<br><br>That we have interrupted the supply routes for their offensive at Kursk, has not pleased the Germans. They'll try to force us out of this area. Resist their attack, and hold the railways unusable.<br><br>Order: Resist the German attack for 16 turns and hold as much VH as possible!", [{"id": 1, "country": 359, "support": [7, 59]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s04.xml", "RP Rescue Mission", "RESCUE MISSION - 12 SEP 1943<br><br>HQ Soviet Partisans, Estonia<br>CO General Karotamm<br><br>A plane loaded with a important U.S. politician, on his way to Moscow, was forced to make an emergency landing in our area. This gentleman must be saved, and Moscow has developed an daring plan, just right for you!<br>A British submarine, ready to take our guest is waiting off the coast. You must carry the VIP by air or by sea to the rendezvous-point, a little island lying off the coast.<br>But first you have to conquer the port or airfield of Kuressaare in a coup. Split you force in two groups. With the southern group perform a mock attack against the German positions, while the second group together with the VIP, past the busy Germans in the north and perform an fast attack against Kuressaare. Capture a plane or a vessel and carry this sporty Cowboy to the rendezvous-point. Good luck, Comrade!<br><br>Order: Reach the EH (red-border hex) and retreat the VIP MSU unit.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [58]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19, "support": [9, 22, 361]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s07.xml", "RP Kill Bruno", "KILL BRUNO - 28 JAN 1944<br><br>HQ Soviet Partisans, Estonia<br>CO General Karotamm<br><br>The Germans hide a rail gun in a our operation area. This gun must be destroyed. The German Luftwaffe is very active in this area and makes an air strike impossible. So, here is our plan.<br><br>The Germans consider their rail gun safe, because any direct attack is smashed by the Luftwaffe. So we first switch off the German airfields.<br>There are two airfields that must be made unusable. The eastern airfield is to seize with your troops. A reinforcing Smersh team, which is subordinate to you for this operation, attack the western airfield.<br>Start similar the central attack on the rail gun! If the rail gun destroyed, block the railway line as long as possible before you retreat your troops. The Germans will soon bring in reinforcements. Good luck, and leave a pile of rubble behind you!<br><br>Note: You can use a Smersh commando or a Partisan unit to make a airfield unusable. Move the unit on the airfield hex and press key 1 for \"blow\". Remember that an airfield sometimes consist of several airfield hexes. Then you have to \"blow\" each airfield hex.<br><br>Order: Resist the German attack for 16 turns and hold as much VH as possible!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn5s05.xml", "RP Narva", "NARVA - 24 JUL 1944<br><br>HQ 2nd Shock Army<br>CO General Fedyuninsky<br><br>Comrade, we want to break the German defense at Narva in an all out attack. Our objective is to seize Narva, break through the Tannenberg Line, and occupy all enemy ports, airfields, and key cities. Give her best, Stalin look at us!<br><br>Order: Capture all VH or destroy all enemy units!<br><br>Original Title & Design: Retreat to the Tannenberg Line by Stephen deJong", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [17, 35, 40]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn5s10.xml", "RP August Storm", "AUGUST STORM - 12 AUG 1945<br><br>HQ Transbaikal Front, Manchuria<br>CO General Malinovsky<br><br>Comrade, the liberation of Manchuria from Japanese occupation making good progress on all fronts. Outstanding work, but now the heavily defended area around Solon is our next target. A breakthrough in this area is necessary for our further advance! The high command is expecting a quick victory!<br><br>Order: Capture all VH or destroy all enemy units!", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Yugoslav Front (1941-1945)"],
["bn8s00.xml", "Uprising in Serbia", "UPRISING IN SERBIA - 25 Aug 1941<br><br>North of Bela Crkva, Macva Region, Serbia<br>CO Commander Misa Pantic<br><br>Our time has come, Comrade! The uprising in Serbia is under way and we must dare the open struggle against the fascist occupiers. You will lead the attack to liberate the provincial capital Krupanj! But first we need the arms depots of the Gendarmerie in the surrounding villages and as many men as possible before we can dare to attack.<br><br>Capture all VH! Use awarded prestige to recruit new partisans.<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>5 x Partisan<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>Hitler believed that with occupation of Yugoslavia, the country was liquidated as independent state. The Kingdom of Yugoslavia was divided between Germany, Italy, Hungary and Bulgaria, while in the territory of present-day Croatia and Bosnia and Herzegovina was proclaimed Independent State of Croatia. Occupiers plundered possessions and took some 350,000 Yugoslav soldiers into captivity. The largest part of Serbia was organized into Territory of the Military Commander in Serbia and as such it was the only example of the military regime in occupied Europe. Germans chose Milan Acimovic for head of quisling Commissary Government.<br><br>Preparations for the uprising by the Communist Party began after the May consultation held in Zagreb on 4 May 1941. The Military Committee of the Provincial Committee of the Communist Party for Serbia was formed in mid-May. On 13 May 1941, Josip Broz Tito sent a message to the Comintern stating that the Yugoslav communists were preparing for an uprising that would commence when Germany attacked the Soviet Union. The Central Committee of the Communist Party of Yugoslavia arrived in Belgrade in late May, and this was of great importance for the development of the resistance. After their arrival, the Central Committee held conferences with local party officials.<br><br>Western Serbia was chosen for base of the uprising, due to forests and hilly terrain and due to its population who provided strong resistance to invading Austrian forces in World War One. First partisan and chetnik detachments were formed in Valjevo area.<br><br>For the beginning of the uprising is taken armed action of Radevina partisan detachment on 7 July 1941 in Bela Crkva near Krupanj. In Bela Crkva was held the traditional Ivanjdan midsummer village fair. There came a group of fifteen partisans, led by commander Misa Pantic and political commissar Zikica Jovanovic Spanac. Partisans gathered people and called them to join in fight against the German invaders. Speech was given by Pantic, a doctor from Valjevo, and Jovanovic, a journalist from Valjevo and combatant from Spanish Civil War. Gendarmes Bogdan Loncar and Milenko Brakovic tried to break up the gathering, forbidden under conditions of military occupation. The partisans opened fire and killed both gendarmes.<br><br>Eight weeks later after three days of fighting, Krupanj was liberated on September 3, 1941 by Valjevo partisan detachment and chetniks led by Orthodox priest Vlada Zecevic and lieutenant Ratko Martinovic. Zecevic, Martinovic and bulk of their chetniks later joined to partisans.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [66]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s01.xml", "Battle of Sabac", "BATTLE OF SABAC - 18 Sep 1941<br><br>North of Sabac, Macva Region, Serbia<br>CO Commander Nebojsa Jerkovic<br><br>We will take advantage of our success of the last weeks and extend the free territories fast. You will perform a attack against the strong German garrison of Sabac and free the city from fascism. The royalist Chetniks have promised their support, unfortunately we are still dependent on it. Carry the operation to success! Long live the Republic of Uzice, long live our leader Comrade Tito! <br><br>Capture all VH and hold it for 15 turns!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>5 x Partisan<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>1 x 81mm 81/14, Mules<br>1 x Light Cavalry (in scenario)<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>The uprising in Serbia was successful and secured a defensible, self-sustained, independent region, the first of many \"free territories\" to be established by the Partisans during the course of the war, and was commonly called the \"Uzice Republic\".<br><br>Mid-September 1941 Nebojsa Jerkovic, a commander of Macva partisan detachment, visited Chetnik captain Dragoslav Racic, a commander of Cer Corp in order to reach agreement on joint attack on Sabac. Battle of Sabac lasted from September 22 until September 24, when 342nd German Division came in aid to besieged Germans and broke rebel encirclement. German soldiers retaliated and killed some 1,000 men from Sabac and Macva. Number of soldiers in Macva partisan detachment drop to half on initial troops. Deployment of 342nd German Division marked beginning of big German counter-offensive on liberated territory.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [66]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s02.xml", "Betrayal", "BETRAYAL - 1 Nov 1941<br><br>East of Uzice, Zlatibor Region, Serbia<br>CO Commander Koca Popovic<br><br>We have information about an imminent attack of the treacherous Chetniks on our headquarters in Uzice. March with your comrades as soon as possible to Uzice and beat back the attackers! <br><br>Hold and retake all VH and make sure, that you lost no more than one of your HQ MSU.<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>5 x Partisan<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>2 x 81mm 81/14, Mules<br>1 x Light Cavalry<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>After more than a month of disagreements and minor collisions, the events culminated on November 1 in a massed Chetnik attack in and around the town of Uzice where the Partisans had their headquarters. Apparently underestimating the Partisans numbers, the Chetnik forces were quickly beaten back. Captain Duane Hudson, British liaison officer in Yugoslavia, then advised the Allied command in Cairo to stop supplying the Chetniks so the British arms would not be used for civil warfare. The Chetniks, who had already received one shipment of weapons sent by parachute, then waited in vain for a second one, even though the British later resumed helping them. Both Tito and Mihailovic, however, were still willing to reach a truce, although both were pressed by some of their officers to attack the other as soon as possible; ceasefires alternated with ultimatums, as bloody reprisals between the two resistance movements affected both sides' morals and alienated civilians. At one point, Mihailovic's forces, after mounting a surprise attack on the Partisans, found themselves surrounded. The Partisans allowed them to go free, which political observers have attributed to military foresight, as the Chetniks would continue to attack German forces.", [{"id": 1, "country": 66}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn8s03.xml", "Retreat to Montenegro", "RETREAT TO MONTENEGRO - 2 Dec 1941<br><br>Southwest of Nova Varos, Zlatibor Region, Serbia<br>CO Commander Koca Popovic<br><br>After a surprisingly strong German counterattack, our positions in Serbia have become untenable. All partisan detachments are on retreat into Italian occupied Montenegro. Lead your comrades over the Lim River and cross the border at Dobrakovo. But hurry up, the Germans are at your heels!<br><br>Reach the Exit Point at Dobrakovo and retreat three of your units!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>5 x Partisan<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>2 x 81mm 81/14, Mules<br>1 x Light Cavalry<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>To clear the territory of the \"Uzice Republic\", the German Army employed its 113th Infantry Division and 342nd Infantry Division, and parts of 704, 714, 717 and 718 Infantry Divisions. They were assisted by Dimitrije Ljotics Serbian Volunteer Corps and Kosta Pecanacs personal Chetnik faction. As German forces entered the territory they faced significant resistance, especially on Rudnik Mountain and in Kraljevo. On September 29, the offensive officially started when the 342nd Infantry Division attacked Partisans on the road between Sabac and Loznica.<br><br>German forces and their Allies advanced from the north and east towards Uzice, and by the 2nd half of November the Partisan forces were in full retreat. On November 25, the final phase of the German offensive against both rebel groups began. Tito and Mihailovic had one last phone conversation : Tito announced that he would defend his positions, while Mihailovic said that he would disperse. Ultimately, on November 29, the Partisans, including their headquarters which were stationed there, left Uzice.<br><br>After leaving Uzice, the Partisans headed for Sandzak, into Italian-occupied territory. Some detachments failed to retreat on time and were dispersed or destroyed. After the main Partisan forces left for Sandzak, only parts of 5 Partisan detachments were present in Serbia.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7, 12]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s04.xml", "Rail Raid", "RAIL RAID - 8 Feb 1942<br><br>Railway between Mostar and Sarajevo, Bosnia<br>CO Commander Koca Popovic<br><br>Some German armored trains are on their way from Mostar to Belgrade. We will intercept and destroy two of them! Our plan is to isolate these two trains in an outlying area by blowing up the tracks and cut them off from help. Then it should be possible to destroy these trains by a concentrated attack of your forces.<br><br>Find and destroy 4 of 6 enemy MSU and prevent the escape of any MSU via exit point. Isolate the enemy trains by blowing up the tracks before and behind them! <br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>3 x Partisan<br>3 x Regular<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>2 x 75mm 75/13, Mules<br>1 x Light Cavalry<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>During the April war against Royal Yugoslav Army, Armored trains No. 23 and No. 24 were used. After capitulation both trains stayed and have participated in destruction of Partisan movement in Serbia during winter 1941/42. After destruction of Partisan uprising in Serbia main battleground of German Armored trains becomes railway Zagreb-Belgrade. Each year number of armored trains was increased and at during winter 1944/45 nearly half of all German armored trains participated in fightings. Railway Zagreb-Belgrade-Salonika, used by German troops retreating from Greece, Bulgaria, Romania and parts of Yugoslavia was protected by Armored Railway Trains (Eisenbahn-Panzerzüge): No. 4, 6, 23, 64, 65, 73; Heavy Recon Trains (schweren Spahzüge): 201, 202, 203, 204; all Light Recon Trains (leichte Spahzüge): 301, 302, 303, 304; Command Train (Kommandozüge) No. I; Track Protection Trains (Streckenschützzüge) 'Max' and 'Werner' and Protection cars No. 30, 31, 32, 33, 34, 35 and 38.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s05.xml", "Operation Trio", "OPERATION TRIO - 10 May 1942<br><br>Foca, Srpska Region, Bosnia<br>CO Commander Koca Popovic<br><br>Italians, Croats and Chetniks have launched a large-scale operation against our liberated territory. We are surrounded by superior enemy forces and must retreat immediately. Cover the retreat of the 1st Proletarian Brigade, especially the Brigade HQ! <br><br>Reach one of the Exit Points with your HQ MSU! <br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>6 x Regular<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>2 x 75mm 75/13, Mules<br>1 x Light Cavalry<br><br>ATTENTION! In second and third turn, you will receive reinforcements in HQ! You will not be informed. You have to go to HQ in order to open the Deploy window. This bug is reported, but I do not know when it will be fixed.<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>During Operation Southeast Croatia, Josip Broz Tito, his Supreme Staff and the 1st Proletarian Brigade commanded by Spanish Civil War veteran Konstantin \"Koca\" Popovic, had withdrawn south to Foca, on the boundary between eastern Bosnia and Herzegovina. With the help of Montenegrin Partisans, they established a liberated area around Foca and Gorazde. This area, known as the \"Foca Republic\", was expanded by subsequent military operations. By late March, People's Liberation Councils had been established to govern 10 towns and 92 villages in the liberated area, but communist organisation in the area was limited and of poor quality.<br><br>Operation Trio was the first large-scale joint German-Italian counter-insurgency operation of World War II conducted in the Independent State of Croatia (NDH), which included modern-day Bosnia and Herzegovina. It was carried out in two phases within eastern Bosnia from 20 April to 13 May 1942, with Ustase militia and Croatian Home Guard forces taking part on the Axis side. The aim of the operation was to target all insurgents between Sarajevo and the Drina river in eastern Bosnia. These included groups led by communists and Serb-chauvinist Chetniks. Differentiating between the rank and file of the two insurgent factions was difficult, as even the communist-led insurgent groups consisted mainly of Serb peasants who had little understanding of the political aims of their leaders.<br><br>During Operation Trio, the Partisan leader Josip Broz Tito, his Supreme Staff and the Partisan main force, consisting of the 1st and 2nd Proletarian Brigades, withdrew from their base of operations around Foca. After briefly reorganising around Zelengora mountain south-east of Foca, they moved their operations to western Bosnia for the remainder of 1942.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [12, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s06.xml", "Counterattack on Kljuc", "COUNTERATTACK ON KLIJUC - 7 Oct 1942<br><br>West of Kljuc, Una-Sana Region, Bosnia<br>CO Commander Koca Popovic<br><br>Few days ago the fascists managed to capture the city Kljuc. Meanwhile, we was able to stop the attack and are going to start our counterattack. Attack Kljuc, liberate the city and cut off the withdrawal Fascists and destroy them!<br><br>Capture all VH and prevent the escape of more than 4 enemy units via Exit Point!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>6 x Regular<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>3 x 75mm 75/13, Mules<br>2 x Light Cavalry<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>Operation Jajce: Started on 28 September with homocentric attack from areas Sanski Most - Banja Luka and Donji Vakuf - Travnik and by October 6th took control of Kljuc, Mrkonjic-Grad and Jajce.<br><br>Combat Group 'Sanski Most' reinforced with tanks, artillery and local Chetniks after two days combat against parts of 6th Krajina partisan detachment captured Kljuc on September 29th. On October 2nd with encirclement maneuver across Lisina mountain, German Combat Group 'Vedel' pushed back 2nd Proletarian Brigade towards village Jezero and captured Mrkonjic-Grad.<br><br>Surprised Operational Staff NOP i DV for Bosnian Krajina with six brigades and two detachments in that sector, because of bad communications lines failed to make stronger resistance, but managed to withdraw its units under assault of much stronger enemy and on October 6th launched counter-attack with 5 brigades and parts of 2 detachments in upper part of Sana river. During three day combat Kljuc has been taken back and several garrison eliminated between Sitinica and Vrhpolja but advance towards Sanski Most was stopped by attack of German Regimental Combat Group 'Vedel' from Sitinica.<br><br>On October 7th 1st Proletarian Brigade and parts of 6th Krajina partisan detachment broke reinforced 2nd Battalion of the Domobran 10th Infantry Regiment and captured Kljuc.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s07.xml", "Case White", "CASE WHITE - 30 Feb 1943<br><br>Vicinity of the Neretva River, Herzegovina<br>CO Commander Koca Popovic<br><br>After the hard fighting of the past days, the Fascists are still on our heels! We must retreat as quickly as possible to Montenegro and our only remaining option is to reach and cross the Neretva River. But the passage is only possible at one point! Scouts reported that Chetniks has occupied this area, so we have to fight our way. We are in real danger, but in any case, we will not leave our wounded comrades!<br><br>Cover the retreat of the Partisan hospital and High Command HQ! Reach one of the Exit Points and retreat 3 of 5 of your MSU! So make sure, that you lost no more than two of your MSU.<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>6 x Regular<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>3 x 75mm 75/13, Mules<br>2 x Light Cavalry<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>Battle of the Neretva<br><br>During the battle, the Partisans were caught in a pocket with their backs to the Neretva river. On their western side, were German forces, including several elite units and supported by panzer brigades. The eastern side (opposite the Partisan pocket) was guarded only by Chetnik formations, who were acting in coordination with the Germans. To reach this side the Partisans would have to cross one or more of the five bridges on the Neretva river. If the Partisans could cross the river they would be relatively safe; however, they had insufficient time to cross as the Axis forces were preparing for their final push.<br><br>In order to counter this strategic \"checkmate\", the Partisan commander, Josip Broz Tito, prepared an elaborate deception. He ordered his sappers to actually blow up all the bridges on the river. When air reconnaissance brought this information to the German command, they concluded that the Partisans must be preparing a final dash north of their current position (along the western shore of the Neretva), and had blown up the bridge to prevent desertion as well as attack by Chetnik forces from the other side of the river. They thus began a redeployment of troops in the area to block the anticipated movement.<br><br>This redeployment gave the Partisan engineers precious time needed to sufficiently repair the bridge and to eliminate the Chetnik troops defending its far side. The Germans, characteristically, quickly caught on, but were unable to correct their mistake and prepare a serious attack in time, because of their previous redeployment orders. With their rearguard fighting off an increasingly powerful German advance, the Partisans crossed the river under intense air bombardment (the Axis deployed large Luftwaffe formations), but the mountainous landscape prevented accurate destruction of the makeshift bridge. After the escape was complete, the weak bridge was finally rendered useless to prevent pursuit. The humiliating strategic defeat was amplified by Tito being able to keep his well known pledge not to leave the wounded behind, as they faced certain execution at the hands of the Axis (which later actually happened in the aftermath of the Battle of the Sutjeska).", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 12, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s08.xml", "Case Black", "CASE BLACK - 4 Jun 1943<br><br>Vicinity of the Sutjeska River, Southeastern Bosnia<br>CO Marshal Josip Broz Tito<br><br>We could speak of a kind of déjà vu - as in the last winter at the Neretva River, today we are facing the same challenge at the Sutjeska River! Strong enemy forces have encircled us and try to block our way into eastern Bosnia. We must fight our way through the enemy lines or perish! Find a suitable crossing point at the Sutjeska River and lead our troops to victory!<br><br>Reach one of the Exit Points and retreat at last 6 of your units!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>6 x Regular<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>3 x 75mm 75/13, Mules<br>2 x Light Cavalry<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>The Axis rallied 127,000 land troops for the offensive, including German, Italian, NDH, Bulgarian, Greek forces under Georgios Poulos (officially SS) and Cossack units, and over 300 airplanes. The Yugoslav National Liberation Army had 22,148 soldiers in 16 brigades. After a period of troop concentration, the offensive started on 15 May 1943. The Axis troops used the advantage of better starting positions to encircle and isolate the partisans on the Durmitor mountain area, located between the Tara and Piva rivers in the mountainous areas of northern Montenegro and forced them to engage in a fierce month-long battle on waste territory.<br><br>On June 9, Tito was nearly killed, as a bomb fell near the leading group and wounded him in the arm. The popular post-war report of the event credited Tito's German shepherd dog Luks, for sacrificing his life to save Tito's. Captain William F. Stuart, a Special Operations Executive operative who was parachuted into Tito's headquarters alongside Captain William Deakin during May, was killed by the explosion, as well.<br><br>Facing almost exclusively German troops, the Yugoslav National Liberation Army (YNLA) finally succeeded in breaking out across the Sutjeska river through the lines of the German 118th and 104th Jäger and 369th (Croatian) Infantry divisions in the northwestern direction, towards eastern Bosnia. Three brigades and the central hospital with over 2000 wounded were surrounded. Following Hitler's instructions, German commander in chief Generaloberst Alexander Löhr ordered their annihilation, including the wounded and the unarmed medical personnel. In addition, YNLA troops suffered from severe lack of food and medical supplies, and many were struck down by typhoid.<br><br>In total there were 7,543 partisan casualties, more than a third of the initial force. The German field commander, General Rudolf Lüters in his final report described the so-called \"communist rebels\" as \"well organized, skillfully led and with combat morale unbelievably high\".<br><br>The successful Partisan breakout helped their reputation as a viable fighting force with the local populace. Consequently they were able to replenish their losses with new recruits, regroup, and mount a series of counterattacks in eastern Bosnia, clearing Axis garrisons of Vlasenica, Srebrenica, Olovo, Kladanj and Zvornik in the following 20 days.<br><br>The battle marked a turning point toward Partisan control of Yugoslavia, and became an integral part of the Yugoslav post-war mythology, celebrating the self-sacrifice, extreme suffering and moral firmness of the partisans.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 8, 12]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s09.xml", "Operation Istria", "OPERATION ISTRIA - 25 Sep 1943<br><br>Vicinity of Petrinja, Central Croatia<br>CO Commander Koca Popovic<br><br>Italy has capitulated and in whole former Italian occupied territory of Yugoslavia rebellion have broken out! The Germans try to disarm the Italians and to gain control over these abandoned areas. Unfortunately the fascists has occupied the most important cities such as Trieste, Rijeka and Zadar before we could intervene. However, many new ad hoc Partisan units were formed and they besiege these cities now, but they are too weak and inexperienced to expel the Germans. Help our comrades in the liberation of our all homeland! But hurry, the reaction of the Germans will not long be stay out. They gather strong armored elite units and prepare a counterattack!<br><br>Capture all VH and hold it for 15 turns!<br><br>Numerous Italian military equipment has fallen into our hands, also some heavy weapons. It's time to motorize a part of your Corps and also to add some fast armored units.<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>2 x Guards, Trucks<br>2 x AB 41<br>1 x 105mm 105/28, Trucks<br><br>4 x Regular<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>2 x 75mm 75/13, Mules<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>After capitulation of Italy in September 1943 open uprising begun in Slovenian littoral, Istria, Croatian Littoral, Gorski Kotar, Notranjsko and Dolenjsko with disarming of the Italian units and formation of large liberated territory and several new Partisan brigades as well as 18th, 30th and 31st Slovenian division of NOVJ. German communication line between Italy and Sava valley was cut or severally disrupted.<br><br>German 194th Grenadier Regiment managed to secure major ports of Trieste, Pula (Pola) on 13 September and Rijeka (Fiume) and Susak on 15 September before Partisans could move in, but both Pula and Rijeka become effectively surrounded with neither side able to do anything.<br><br>On 19 September German High command give order to commander of Army Group B, Field-Marshal Erwin Rommel to suppress uprising and eliminate NOV i POJ forces in Gorski Kotar, east Slovenia, Slovenian littoral, Istra, Croatian Littoral and secure Adriatic coast in that area.<br><br>Task was given to 2. SS Panzer Corps under Paul Hausser which massed huge force for the operation over 40000 soldiers, 95 tanks, 41 assault guns, 23 tank hunters, 6 heavy self-propelled guns and around 300 half-tracks versus around 15000 Partisans.<br><br>Such massive superiority in armor allowed Germans to quickly achieve their goals against Partisans who had only few captured Italian tankettes and anti-tank guns which makes entire operation waste of resources at the time when Germany was hard pressed on Eastern front and in southern Italy.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [62]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s10.xml", "Banja Luka Strike", "BANJA LUKA STRIKE - 18 Dec 1943<br><br>North of Banja Luka, Bosnia<br>CO Commander Slavko Rodic<br><br>Your Corps will start a surprise attack on the largest town in the region of Srpska. Liberate the citizens of Banja Luka from the fascist bondage! Apart from some German armored trains, resistance is only expected by some Croatian NDH troops.<br><br>Capture all VH!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>2 x Guards, Trucks<br>2 x AB 41<br>2 x 105mm 105/28, Trucks<br><br>4 x Regular<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>1 x 75mm 75/13, Mules<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>The first Banja Luka operation started on 12 December 1943 at 10.00 pm with attack of units of 5th Corps of NOVJ on Banja Luka, airfield in Zaluzani and Bosanska Gradiska, lasted until 1 January 1944. Purpose of operation was easing the German pressure on NOVJ forces in east Bosnia.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s11.xml", "Knight's Move", "KNIGHT'S MOVE - 25 May 1944<br><br>Drvar Region, Western Bosnia<br>CO Marshal Josip Broz Tito<br><br>Our HQ's in Drvar are surprisingly attacked by enemy airborne troops! Moreover, strong enemy columns move on Drvar from all sides. Beat back the attacks and ensure that our HQ's and the Allies military missions in Drvar do not come to harm!<br><br>Hold as much VH as possible for 10 turns! 10 of 12 VH are needed for a BV and at last 6 VH are needed in order not to lose the battle. Furthermore you must ensure that at least one of your 6 MSU survive the enemy attacks!<br><br>In this scenario, the AI has the first turn!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>3 x Guards, Trucks<br>2 x AB 41<br>2 x 105mm 105/28, Trucks<br><br>3 x Regular<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Mules<br>1 x 75mm 75/13, Mules<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>The offensive began at 5am with the advance of ground forces from their assembly areas surrounding the areas of operations. About 6.35am, five squadrons of Luftwaffe bombers, including Junkers Ju 87 dive bombers, began bombing targets within Drvar and Bosanski Petrovac. A total of 440 sorties were flown on 25 May 1944.<br><br>Airborne assault and initial response<br><br>500th SS Parachute Battalion began to parachute and glide onto their objectives at 7am, with most parachutists and glider pilots able to land relatively close to their targets despite the smoke and dust from the bombing. Some gliders landed significantly off course, including one that landed in front of the Bastasi cave seven kilometres to the west of Drvar, and several that landed in Vrtoc(e. The occupants of the glider that landed in Bastasi were immediately killed by members of Tito's escort battalion guarding the cave, and the occupants of the gliders at Vrtoce had to fight their way toward Drvar. After landing, the first wave of the 500th SS Parachute Battalion quickly gained control of Drvar.<br><br>Panther Group supported by Red Group overcame minimal resistance at the cemetery and Captain Rybka established his headquarters behind the cemetery walls. However, there was no sign of Tito or his headquarters. Greifer Group and Brecher Group were also unsuccessful as the British and American groups had moved following the aerial reconnaissance on 23 May. Parts of Stürmer Group landed their gliders in a field immediately south of the Drvar cave and came under fire from members of Tito's escort battalion on the high ground in the area of the cave. The Draufgänger Group landed their gliders at the \"Western Cross\", then assaulted a building they believed was the Partisan communications centre. However, the building was actually the office of the Communist Party of Yugoslavia Central Committee, who resisted fanatically until the building was levelled using satchel charges. Both Blue Group and Green Group, consisting of parachute troops that landed in the eastern part of Drvar where most of the population lived, were also engaged in heavy fighting. The Young Communist League of Yugoslavia had just finished a conference in Drvar, and many of the delegates were still staying in the town. Many youths took up whatever arms they could obtain and commenced fighting the parachutists who were attempting to establish a cordon on the eastern side of the town.<br><br>Two kilometres further east on the road to Mokronoge was a Partisan officer training school with about 130 students. On hearing the fighting from the direction of Drvar, the students marched west initially armed with pistols and a few rifles. They split into two groups, a smaller group which crossed the Unac and advanced west along the railway line on the ridge leading toward Tito's cave, and a larger group which collected arms and ammunition from several stray canisters of German equipment dropped by parachute. The larger group of students attacked Green and Blue Groups from the east around 8am, suffering severe casualties but maintained continuous pressure on the German flank. About 9am, the Germans had largely secured Drvar, and the available troops went from house to house, armed with photographs of Tito, brutally questioning the civilians they could find. Soon after this commenced, Rybka realised that Partisan resistance was concentrated to the north in the vicinity of the cave. He therefore fired the red signal flare to rally his troops for an assault in that direction.<br><br>Assault on Tito's cave and the Partisan counterattack<br><br>About 10.30am, Rybka launched a frontal attack across the Unac supported by at least one MG42 machine gun firing into the mouth of the cave. The Germans reached the base of the hill, fifty metres from the cave, but suffered severe casualties in the assault. They were also running low on water. Prior to this attack, Tito and around 20 staff had taken refuge in the cave.<br><br>While Rybka was assembling his troops for this attack, surrounding Partisan forces were rushed toward Drvar. Three battalions of the 3rd Proletarian Brigade of the 1st Proletarian Division approached from the southeast. One battalion attacked the German position at the cemetery while the other two swung around to strike the Germans from the west.<br><br>Tito makes his escape<br><br>At about 11.15am, after Rybka's first attack had been defeated, Tito and the small group gathered with him escaped from the cave. There was a platform at the mouth of the cave, and they climbed down a rope through a trapdoor in the platform, although the hysteria displayed by Tito's mistress Davorjanka Paunovic (codenamed \"Zdenka\") and his dog \"Tiger\" caused some delays. The party split up and following a creek leading to the Unac, the small groups climbed the heights to the east and withdrew toward the village of Potoci.<br><br>Second German attack and withdrawal<br><br>About midday, the second wave of parachute troops were dropped in two groups to the west of the cemetery. The drop zone was within fields of fire of the Partisans to the west of Drvar, and they suffered many casualties during the drop. Collecting the remainder, Rybka mounted a second attack, but the pressure on his flanks was too heavy, and the assault again failed. Fighting continued throughout the afternoon with both sides taking heavy casualties.<br><br>In the late afternoon, Rybka ordered a withdrawal of all his forces to the area of the cemetery and formed a defensive perimeter. During the withdrawal, at least one group of troops was cutoff and killed. About 6pm, Rybka was wounded by a grenade blast and was later evacuated with other casualties in the light aircraft intended to carry away Tito after his capture. By 9.30pm, the Germans had consolidated their position in the cemetery, although they were now completely surrounded by the Partisans. During the night the 3rd Proletarian Brigade attacked the cemetery, with elements of the 9th Dalmatia Division reinforcing the assault. At 3.30am on 26 May, the final Partisan attack was launched against the cemetery, breaching the walls in several places, but the paratroopers held on.<br><br>Ground force assault and Partisan withdrawal<br><br>Throughout 25 May, the ground forces of XV Mountain Corps had not been able to advance as quickly as expected. There had been unexpected resistance from the Partisan 1st, 5th and 8th Corps along their axes of advance, and there was very poor communication between the various elements which resulted in lack of coordination of their movements. They were also subjected to several Allied air attacks.<br><br>Escorted by elements of the 3rd Krajina Brigade, Tito made his way to Potoci, where he was met by a battalion of the 1st Proletarian Brigade. At Potoci they were met by the allied mission staff and groups of Partisans. Fortunately the British mission signals officer had brought the only surviving radio. After the final night attack had failed to overrun the Germans in Drvar, and realising that the ground forces would eventually fight their way to the town and relieve the paratroopers, Tito ordered the withdrawal of Partisan forces from the town. About 5am on 26 May, a Luftwaffe fighter-bomber formation engaged the withdrawing Partisan troops. After German troops were observed in the area of Potoci, Tito, his staff and his escort continued toward Kupres, travelling on foot and by horseback, as well as on the wagons of a narrow-gauge logging railway. During this trek, one of the members of the Soviet mission was wounded by shellfire.<br><br>Relief of the paratroopers<br><br>About 7am on 26 May, the 500th SS Parachute Battalion established radio contact with reconnaissance elements of Battle Group Willam, but it was not until 12.45pm that the 92nd Motorised Grenadier Regiment reached Drvar and relieved the paratroopers.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [41]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [9, 19, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s12.xml", "Operation Ratweek", "OPERATION RATWEEK - 3 Sep 1944<br><br>West of Zagreb, Croatia<br>CO Commander Peko Dapcevic<br><br>This is a Hit & Run-operation! In recent days, the USAAF bombed all enemy airfields in Zagreb east of the Sava River. Your task is the capture and destruction of the remaining enemy airfields west of the Sava River! If all airfields are unusable, Zagreb is without fighter protection and the USAAF is able to bomb important factories and railway facilities without significant losses. Act quickly and retreat in time, before the enemy can react!<br><br>Find and destroy 5 of 5 enemy MSU (Factories and trains in Zagreb) with your bombers (Reinforcement) and don't lose any of your own MSU bombers! To ensure this, all enemy airfields east of the Sava River must be destroyed by your ground forces, otherwise the Luftwaffe shoot down your bombers soon!<br><br>The time of hiding in the mountains is over! Now comes the time to fight the enemy in open field. The British have given us some modern heavy weapons, upgrade your Corps into a powerful full-motorized force, in order to perform your future tasks! A fighter squadron, trained and equipped by our British Allies, is also subject to your command. Congratulations!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>2 x Stuart V<br>6 x Guards, Trucks<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Trucks<br>2 x AEC III<br>3 x 105mm 105/28, Trucks<br>1 x Spitfire V<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>Simply refereed to by Partisan Supreme Headquarters as Destruction of communications on Yugoslav front from 1 to 7 September 1944, operation Ratweek was major joint effort of Allied air forces and Yugoslav partisans.<br><br>Plan probably originated from ULTRA decrypts revealing planed withdrawal of German Army from Adriatic coastline and Army Group E from Greece where over 350.000 German soldiers were used for occupation and coastal defense duties. Disrupting German withdrawal schedule would have serious consequences as subsequent events showed.<br><br>Agreement was made during talks between Josip Broz Tito, Winston Churchill and Henry Maitland Wilson from 6 to 14 August 1944 in Caserta and Naples. Goal was to destroy communication network (road and railway) in entire Yugoslavia simultaneously by using eight Partisan Corps (24 division and one operational group with 79 brigades, totaling 120.000 soldiers), four Partisan operational zone and units of regional staffs supported by Allied Balkan Air Force and 15th United States Army Air Force.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [9]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s13.xml", "Belgrade Offensive", "BELGRADE OFFENSIVE - 12 Oct 1944<br><br>West of Belgrade, Serbia<br>CO General Peko Dapcevic<br><br>The time has come to liberate the Serbian capital from the fascist bondage! With the support of the victorious Red Army, it should not be difficult to drive out the Germans and their collaborators. Long live our leader Comrade Tito, long live the Communist Party!<br><br>Capture all VH!<br><br>A fighter-bomber squadron, trained and equipped by our British Allies, is subject to your command. Congratulations!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>2 x Stuart V<br>6 x Guards, Trucks<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Trucks<br>2 x AEC III<br>3 x 105mm 105/28, Trucks<br>1 x Spitfire V<br>1 x Hurricane IV<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>The 4th Guards Mechanized Corps of the Red Army and the Yugoslav 12th Corps broke through the enemy resistance south of Belgrade on 14 October, approaching the city. The Yugoslavs advanced along the roads in the direction of Belgrade south of the Sava River, while the Red Army engaged in fighting on the northern bank outskirts. The assault on the city was delayed due to the diversion of forces for the elimination of thousands of enemy troops surrounded between Belgrade and Smederevo (to the south-east). On 20 October, Belgrade had been completely overrun by joint Soviet and Yugoslav forces.<br><br>The Yugoslav 13th Corps, in cooperation with the Bulgarian 2nd Army, advanced from the south-east. They were responsible for the area of Nis and Leskovac. The forces were also responsible for cutting off the main for the evacuation of Army Group E, along the rivers of South Morava and Morava. Army Group E had, therefore, been forced to retreat through the mountains of Montenegro and Bosnia and was unable to strengthen the German forces in Hungary.<br><br>The next day, elements of the 3rd Ukrainian Front stormed Kraljevo and finally cut Thessaloniki highway to Belgrade.<br><br>The Soviet 10th Guards Rifle Corps of the 46th Army (2nd Ukrainian Front), together with units of the Yugoslav Partisans moving via the Danube - provided more offensive strength from the north-east against the Wehrmacht's position in Belgrade. They cleared the left bank of the Tisa and Danube (in Yugoslavia) and took the town of Pancevo.", [{"id": 1, "country": 67, "support": [7, 361]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [19]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s14.xml", "Knin", "KNIN - 26 Nov 1944<br><br>South of Knin, Herzegovina<br>CO Commander Pavle Ilic<br><br>Enemy troops in strength of two to three divisions entrenches in Knin to keep the Balkans retreat routes open. Through a quick victory in Knin, we would be able to prevent the withdrawal of considerable Wehrmacht contingents and cause a heavy defeat to the fascists!<br><br>Capture all VH!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>2 x Stuart V<br>6 x Guards, Trucks<br>2 x MG-Infantry, Trucks<br>2 x AEC III<br>3 x 105mm 105/28, Trucks<br>1 x Spitfire V<br>1 x Hurricane IV<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>Main battle begun by frontal assault of the 26th Division backed by artillery and armor against German 891st and 892nd Regiments but failed to breach it.<br><br>On 28 November Army Group E allowed 15th Mountain Corps to begun retreat from Knin to more defensible position north Knin which were to be held during the winter. Two days later Germans begun shortening their front by pulling back from Ostra Glavica, Bulajusi and Lisnik, also fresh 847th Regiment from 392nd Division arrived in area of Padene to boost German defenses in that sector.<br><br>On 1 December new assault breaks Germans lines, successful morthen outflanking maneuver by 8th Brigade of the 20th Division attacks German forces in Padene area while 26th Division ties down most of Germans to the southern sector. Next day 14th Brigade of the 19th Division reaches Knin - Padene road and connects with 20th Division completing encirclement of German forces in Knin. 1st Dalmatian Brigade breaches German lines in the south advances towards Knin itself.<br><br>Between 2 and 3am on 3 December, 1st and 12 Dalmatian brigade arrived into Knin across demolished brigade over Krka river and by 4am linked up with 9th Brigade of the 20th Division liberating Knin. Most of German forces were cut off in several pockets, smaller one southeast of Knin was eliminated by 26th Division capturing 1200 German soldiers. Most of 264th Division was surrounded near Stara Straza with only small group lead by division commander Alois Windisch managed to breakthrough during the night of 3/4 November. As a last act of desperation to prevent it from falling into Partisan hands Germans set fire to their ammunition and fuel depot stored in Stara Straza railway tunnel killing around 600 of their wounded which were also located inside.<br><br>By 4 December most organized resistance ceased with Germans attempting to reach their lines in small groups, amongst captured was Konrad Wild, commander of the 383rd Regiment of the 373rd Division.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s15.xml", "Liberation of Mostar", "LIBERATION OF MOSTAR - 6 Feb 1945<br><br>Sibenik, Croatia<br>CO General Petar Drapsin<br><br>Your Corps is selected for the liberation of Mostar! However, the Germans have already started to retreat inland. Advance with a task force as soon as possible on Visoko and with a second along the coast on Dubrovnik. This way we can surround and destroy the retreating Germans! The British have pledged support from sea and want to eliminate some German bases on the islands. This is your chance for revenge for the 'Battle of the Neretva River' in winter '43!<br><br>Capture all VH and prevent the escape of more then three enemy units via Exit Point!<br><br>The Soviet Union supported our fight for liberation extensive with weapons and ammunition. You are now able to provide you Corps with the most modern equipment!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>1 x T-34/85<br>1 x Stuart V<br>6 x Guards, Trucks<br>1 x SU-85<br>1 x MG-Infantry, Trucks<br>2 x AEC III<br>1 x 152mm D-1, Trucks<br>2 x 105mm 105/28, Trucks<br>1 x Spitfire V<br>1 x Hurricane IV<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>The Mostar Operation was a series of Yugoslav Partisan military operations in Herzegovina from February 6-15, 1945.<br><br>Mostar guarded left flank for troops of German South-East Command and Army Group E retreating from Serbia and Montenegro through Sarajevo North along Bosna river to Slavonski Brod.<br><br>Most of central Herzegovina was part of the District of Hum in the Independent State of Croatia. Mostar was also home to an air field of the Air Force of the Independent State of Croatia.<br><br>Partisans took Siroki Brijeg on February 6 and Mostar without resistance on February 14.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 34, 66]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s16.xml", "Battle of Sarajevo", "BATTLE OF SARAJEVO - 1 Apr 1945<br><br>Vicinity of Sarajevo, Bosnia<br>CO Commander Kosta Nad<br><br>The encirclement and destruction of the German-Croat forces in the area of Sarajevo is our next planned step. For this we need the motorized and armored units of your Elite-Corps. Advance in the rear of the enemy quickly at Podlugovi and cut the Germans off! The rest should like a walk in the park.<br><br>Capture all VH and prevent the escape of more then three enemy units via Exit Point!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>1 x T-34/85<br>1 x Stuart V<br>6 x Guards, Trucks<br>2 x SU-85<br>2 x AEC III<br>3 x 152mm D-1, Trucks<br>1 x Spitfire V<br>1 x Hurricane IV<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>Surrounding actions of Yugoslav army from 28 March to 10 April 1945 for purpose of liberating Sarajevo and its wider area. Under command of Operative HQ for liberation of Sarajevo were 2nd, 3rd and 5th Corps of Yugoslav army, 11th and 13th Krajina and 18th Central Bosnian Brigade, Artillery Brigade and Tank Company. Sarajevo and surrounding areas was defended by strong German and NDH forces under command of German 21st Mountain Corps.<br><br>German defense plan of 22 February named Sarajevo as fortified city which could only be abandoned on permission from Adolf Hitler. This plan was stolen by Sarajevo operatives lead by Vladimir Peric Valter what caused mass arrests including 25 German and 150 NDH soldiers and suicide of LtColonel Vedel, German chief of staff, who kept it in a locked vault. By 20 March failure of German offensive in Hungary and opening offensive of Yugoslav 4th Army in Lika made holding Sarajevo pointless and retreat was ordered with 3000 wounded German soldiers from Sarajevo hospital going first.<br><br>Interception of Yugoslav wireless communications revealed to Germans that general attack was planed for 28 March and in order to secure their retreat routes several operations were planed and carried out BERGGEIST, MAIGEWITTER and OSTERGLOCKE.<br><br>After heavy fighting's Sarajevo was liberated on 6 April. During pursuit of enemy, units of JA liberated Visoko, Kakanj and 10 April Busovaca concluding Sarajevo operation.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 34, 67]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s17.xml", "Advance on Trieste", "ADVANCE ON TRIESTE - 14 Apr 1945<br><br>Vicinity of Drnis, Croatia<br>CO Commander Pavle Ilic<br><br>The last chapter of the liberation of our homeland is opened. Advance with your Corps to Trieste, liberate the city and link up with the from Italy coming Allied troops!<br><br>Capture all VH!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>1 x T-34/85<br>1 x Stuart V<br>6 x Guards, Trucks<br>2 x SU-85<br>2 x AEC III<br>3 x 152mm D-1, Trucks<br>1 x Spitfire V<br>1 x Hurricane IV<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>Fought from 16 April to 7 May 1945 between the units of the 4th Yugoslav Army and the German 97th Army Corps in wider area of mountains Sneznik-Rijeka-Ilirska Bistrica. As part of the Yugoslav Army (JA) closing operations, from 14 April 4th Army advance from the line Crikvenica-Lic-Fuzine-Delnice in direction of Rijeka (Fiume) and Trst (Trieste) and in heavy fighting's which lasted 22 days liberated Crikvenica, Kraljevica, Bakar, Opatija, Labin, Buzet, Rijeka (Fiume), Pula (Pola), Pazin, Umag, Ilirska Bistrica, islands of Cres, Losinj and Krk. Finally was liberated Croatian coast and Istra. The German 97th Corps was surrounded in area of Ilirska Bistrica where it capitulated on 7 May. 16,000 solider and officers including three generals have been taken prisoners together with entire corps equipment.<br><br>The area of Ilirska Bistrica-Klana-Rijeka was defended by 6 German, 4 Italian and 2 NDH battalions, regiment of SVC and parts of Chetnik Dinara Division, in the area of Postojna-Milje(Muggia)-Trieste-Monfalcone-St.Peter (Pivka) was German 188th Mountain Division with some German and Italian garrisons, two regiments of SVC and around 150 coastal and anti-aircraft guns.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [7, 34, 359]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [6, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["bn8s18.xml", "Battle of Poljana", "BATTLE OF POLJANA - 14 May 1945<br><br>Poljana Region, Slovenia<br>CO General Kosta Nad<br><br>Marauding Axis troops, not willing to surrender to us and want to go to British occupied Austria, move toward your positions. Prevent that these units reach the Austrian border. Show no mercy, if they do not want to give up!<br><br>Find and destroy 58 of 62 enemy units. So make sure that no more than 4 enemy units reach one of the Exit Points!<br><br>Recommended Core:<br><br>1 x T-34/85<br>1 x Stuart V<br>6 x Guards, Trucks<br>2 x SU-85<br>2 x AEC III<br>3 x 152mm D-1, Trucks<br>1 x Spitfire V<br>1 x Hurricane IV<br><br>THE STORY<br><br>Just before 9 am on May 14, a significant force of mostly NDH units with some Montenegrin People's Army and Slovenian Home Guard troops approached Partisan positions at the Surnik farm near Poljana demanding free passage west. This was refused, and firing commenced on both sides. NDH attacks, including artillery fire support, intensified in the afternoon, evening and overnight, finally ceasing on the morning of 15 May with the arrival of around 20 British tanks. Tense negotiations followed, during which British officers made it abundantly clear that they would not offer protection to the collaborators and that unconditional surrender to the Partisans was the only option. White flags of surrender were finally raised around 4 pm on 15 May.<br><br>The surrender of this last area of Axis resistance 8 days after the official end of World War II in Europe, the surrender of the Germans on Monday 7 May 1945, was the last major battle of World War II in Europe.", [{"id": 1, "country": 41, "support": [4, 7, 34]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 43, "support": [22, 361]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["Red Destiny (1946-1954)"],
["rd01.xml", "RD Bialystok Insurrection", "Ah, welcome comrade General!  Allow me to brief you on the tactical situation, and the reasons for which you were called here:<br><br>The citizens of Bialystok are agitating for the return of Polish independence.  Unfortunately, it seems that some units of the former Polish Army were able to evade our men during our brief campaign through Poland, and these units have quickly seized the area from our local garrision.<br><br>This rebellion forces us to divert your forces from the front in Germany, comrade General.  You must crush the insurrection quickly and with force.  Paratroopers will be arriving shortly to assist your men.<br><br>Show no mercy, Comrade.   Stalin himself has ordered that the villages be razed to the ground.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd02.xml", "RD Road To Berlin", "Comrade General, the final approach to Berlin has begun.  The foolish Germans have left the approach through the Seelow Heights minimally guarded by their lightest units.  This is an excellent opportunity for you to further become experienced in mobile warfare, comrade General.  Drive to the eastern edge of Berlin, and crush all those who would oppose the wave of Soviet revolution.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 86}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd03.xml", "RD Siege Of Berlin", "Comrade General, here lies the German capital of Berlin.  You have been selected by party officials to lead the attack.  <br><br>A British volunteer corps has arrived to assist the defenders of the city, and we suspect that the Germans are well-entrenched. The 5th Division will assist your forces.  Make mother Russia proud, comrade.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 86, "support": [22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd04a.xml", "RD Border Clash At Ulan-Ude", "Comrade General, due to your exceptional performance in Berlin, the Party has asked you take a transfer to the Far East.  Here, China has been ravaged by an internal war for well over a decade.  Comrade Stalin is indignant at how far north their troops have been able to travel  Now is the time to strike.  Your forces must push over the border demarcation at Ulan-Ude, and retake as much land as possible from the invaders.  However, comrade General, do not underestimate the Chinese Army.  Although they are in a weakened state, they use some of the same purchased American equipment as the European Allies.  They may attempt to counter-attack.  Good luck, comrade General.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd05a.xml", "RD Liberation In Almaty", "There has been a perpetual state of warfare along the Kazakh front for the past five months.  The decadent Chinese recently launched an attack on the city of Almaty and took it from our brave conscripts.  You are to take your corps, positioned north of Almaty, and liberate the area.  The more quickly you can drive the Chinese out of the area, the better.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd04b.xml", "RD Beachhead At Taranto", "Comrade General, have you ever been to Italy? Nyet? Well, you will soon be taking a, how shall we say, tour of the country, da?  The Party has selected you to begin the attack on Italy due to your performance in the battle for Berlin.  The initial strike will be here, at Taranto.  Your forces will be landing against fierce Allied resistance, since the cowardly Italians have pleaded for Allied help against our unstoppable onslaught.  Allied ships pose a major threat to the invasion, so we have sent you a small fleet of our mighty Soviet submarines to sink the badly made Allied tin cans.  Good luck, comrade General.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd05b.xml", "RD Advance On Salerno", "The fight for Italy still continues, comrade General.  However, the party believes the Italian government is on the verge of surrender.  They do not wish to see their beautiful countryside pockmarked by the craters of war, da?  You must bring the conflict to an end, comrade General.  Finish off the last major vestige of Allied power in Italy, at Salerno.  More of our fine submarines are on their way to assist you, should more Allied surface ships be encountered.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd04c.xml", "RD Evacuation In Thermopylae", "Comrade General, the Party has selected you for tactical operations in the invasion of Greece due to your performance in Berlin.  The Allied dogs have holed up in the area of Thermopylae.  I'm sure you know already that the Western nations believe they can hold us off until they can evacuate the country, da?  They think they can do what the Spartans did to the Persians here, in times long ago.  <br><br>Comrade General, you must show them that it is foolish to resist the tides of revolution.  Wipe out the Allied forces and take the area for mother Russia.  Intelligence reports the annoying Allied Navy may try to shell you if you go along the coast, comrade, so beware.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [11, 39, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd05c.xml", "RD Landing At Maleme", "Comrade General, the Allies are using the Greek island of Crete as a last bastion.  With the Greek government officially out of the picture, this island is the last obstacle to our rightful rule of the Aegean Sea.  Your forces will land at a predesignated point on the island, in the area of the city of Maleme.  Paratroopers have landed to the west of your landing zone.  <br><br>You will not be pleased to know that the Royal Navy has positioned a significant flotilla here. Our superior submarines, crafted by the loyal workers, will be dispatched to your command to remove the Allied naval threat.  Good luck, comrade General.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd06.xml", "RD Drive on Antwerp", "Our glorious Red Army of workers and peasants has begun the invasion of the Low Countries.  Holland fell quickly to our armored forces, but I am most displeased to inform you that the Allied pigs have managed to set up significant defenses around the Belgian port of Antwerp. Your veteran army, having served mother Russia well in the past, has been tasked with securing this vital and important city.  Crush the Allied dogs, comrade General.  The party will not be kind if you fail here.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [6, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd07.xml", "RD Frostbite in the Ardennes", "The Allies have laid a trap in the Ardennes, and Russia's brave soldiers are now bogged down in a hellish forest.  Your job, comrade General, is to lead them out of this pocket into the beautiful French countryside.  Drive the Allies back with everything you have at your disposal.  Do not let your fate become the same as the general who came before you.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 6, "support": [22, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd08.xml", "RD Push To Dunkirk", "The Allied cowards think they can escape socialist justice.  The pathetic remnants of the French army are attempting to escape at Dunkirk, with assistance from German and British troops.  You must show them the futility of their situation, comrade.  <br><br>Comrade Stalin has placed his trust in you and expects you to complete this operation as quickly as possible.  Do not disappoint him, Comrade General...", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 6, "support": [22, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd09a.xml", "RD Storming Dover '51", "Comrade General, the time has finally come.  Over a year has passed since the Allies fled Europe from the city of Dunkirk, and now our carefully made plans are going into action.  <br><br>Your decorated forces have been specially chosen by comrade Stalin himself to land on the British mainland and secure the beaches at Dover. While the British troops outnumber us almost two-to-one, the majority of them are inexperienced recruits.  The Free French and German troops we expect you to encounter are more experienced but far fewer in number.  <br><br>Submarines have been sent to neutralize the British ships in the area, an assigment of which I am sure they shall have no trouble with. <br><br>Task Force Bear is landing to the west of your position, in order to secure one of the airfields located along the shore. <br><br>There is a rumor that an experienced British force is being sent to reinforce the area within several days.  It would be in your best interest to secure the coast of Dover as quickly as possible.  Good luck, comrade General.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd10a.xml", "RD The Sack Of London '52", "Are you not excited? This is the last battle, comrade General! The British capital of London lies before our glorious Red Army of workers and peasants.  <br><br>However, as I am sure you know, this is not going to be an easy task, da? The pitiful Allied dogs have rallied what remains of their armies inside of London.  Though the British troops would be some threat to us alone, our intelligence reports that veteran Free German and French troops are supplementing the Allied defense force.  No matter.  With you in command, comrade General, the Allies do not stand a chance.  Go, forward! Destroy the Allies! For comrade Stalin, and mother Russia!", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd09b.xml", "RD Passage To Madrid", "Comrade General, we have finally rid France of the Allied scum.  Unfortunately, the French armies to the south were able to retreat into the mountains of Spain and Andorra, supported by a weak pro-Allied Spanish government.<br><br>Stalin has personally chosen you for the honor of leading the assault on Madrid.  This road is the fastest route to the Spanish capital, comrade General.  Intelligence reports indicate that you can expect heavy Allied resistance and attacks from several directions on this road.  End the resistance of the feeble Spanish government, comrade General.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd10b.xml", "RD Fortress at Gibraltar", "Here at the port of Gibraltar, the Allied dogs have made their final stand in continental Europe. It is up to you, comrade General, to expel them from their hiding spot.  <br><br>The Allies have sent their best troops to hold their fortress, and are heavily dug in. Additionally, the Royal Navy is patrolling the narrow waters around Gibraltar.<br><br>Intelligence has intercepted an Allied radio transmission; it is possible the Allies may try to send troops from their North African colonies in desperation, in an effort to reinforce their garrison on Gibraltar.  <br><br>The party is relying on a victory from you here comrade; show the Allies why it is futile to resist Soviet supremacy!", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd11.xml", "RD Kharkov Rebellion", "Comrade General, I have grave news. Despite our recent successes in driving the Allies out of Europe, the Ukrainian people have risen against us out of sheer war weariness. There is only one response to such treachery.  <br><br>You must take your troops and kill the traitors, the majority of whom have taken up positions near Kharkov.  I must warn you Comrade General: Though the mutinous Ukrainian troops are nowhere near as experienced as your men, they are using the same combat equipment you have been using against the Allies for several years.  You must be prepared for anything.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 64}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["rd12.xml", "RD Storming Dover '53", "Comrade General, the time has finally come.  Over three years have passed since the Allies fled Europe from the city of Dunkirk, and now our carefully made plans are going into action.  <br><br>Your decorated forces have been specially chosen by comrade Stalin himself to land on the British mainland and secure the beaches at Dover. While the British troops outnumber us almost two-to-one, the majority of them are inexperienced recruits.  The Free French and German troops we expect you to encounter are more experienced but far fewer in number.  <br><br>Submarines have been sent to neutralize the British ships in the area, an assigment of which I am sure they shall have no trouble with. <br><br>Task Force Bear is landing to the west of your position, in order to secure one of the airfields located along the shore. <br><br>There is a rumor that an experienced British force is being sent to reinforce the area within several days.  It would be in your best interest to secure the coast of Dover as quickly as possible.  Good luck, comrade General.", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["rd13.xml", "RD The Sack Of London '54", "Are you not excited? This is the last battle, comrade General! The British capital of London lies before our glorious Red Army of workers and peasants.  <br><br>However, as I am sure you know, this is not going to be an easy task, da? The pitiful Allied dogs have rallied what remains of their armies inside of London.  Though the British troops would be some threat to us alone, our intelligence reports that veteran Free German and French troops are supplementing the Allied defense force.  No matter.  With you in command, comrade General, the Allies do not stand a chance.  Go, forward! Destroy the Allies! For comrade Stalin, and mother Russia!", [{"id": 0, "country": 19}], [{"id": 1, "country": 22, "support": [33, 86]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["North Korea (1950-1953)"],
["ncampseo.xml", "Seoul", "SEOUL (25 June 1950)<br><br>Welcome, Comrade General, to this historic briefing.  Korea has been in the hands of foreign powers for far too long.  The Imperialist Japanese have been driven off our peninsula only to make room for capitalistic Americans - but only in the south.  The people of North Korea have the full support from our comrades in the Soviet Union.  They have supplied us with weapons, trucks, artillery, mortars, and their famous T-34 tanks!  Now the time has to come to unite Korea under the communist banner and free the people of South Korea from their capitalistic oppressors!!<br><br>From the border at the 38th Parellel, we will attack on a broad front.  You will be in charge of the operation directed at taking the capital of the South: Seoul.  Intelligence has made it clear that most South Korean divisions are deployed at or near the border.  A perfect opportunity to destroy them, don't you think?  The Southern army has little equipment, and they are lacking tanks, artillery and aircraft.<br><br>Comrade General, be careful with your equipment.  We have only limited stocks of tanks and artillery which means it will be very hard for us to replace any that are lost.  We will meet again in Seoul!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["ncamposa.xml", "Suwon", "SUWON (30 June 1950)<br><br>I see that you are eager to pursue the capitalist forces and destroy them, now we have the chance.  And we will!  They have concentrated just outside Seoul on the southern bank of the Han River and have blown the bridges.  We are certain that you will find a way to cross the river and liberate more of our beautiful peninsula!<br><br>The United Nations has passed a resolution in which we would have to stop our activities and retreat back behind the 38th Parallel.  Naturally, the capitalistic nations of the world are behind this.  There is a possibility that America and other nations will provide forces in support of the South.  Make speed so that we can liberate all of Korea before any decisive action can take place.  Once liberated the people in the South will show their gratitude and be happy to be reunited!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18, "support": [3, 9]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamptae.xml", "Taejon", "TAEJON (16 July 1950)<br><br>It looks like the United Nations has made good on their threats.  They have blockaded our ports and we have suffered the first bombardments from American aircraft.  Also we have recently encountered American ground units at Osan.  Reconnaissance has shown that the capitalists have deployed units in the direct line of your advance on Taejon, which might be of divisional strength.  However our People's Army has not been defeated and will not be defeated!<br><br>Comrade, you will take Taejon and advance next on Pusan.  Our 3rd division will frontally assault the American positions at the Kum River while you flank the Americans. This should force the retreat of the capitalists or it will result in their complete destruction!  We will meet in Taejon this time, Comrade General!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["ncamppu1.xml", "Pusan Perimeter 1", "PUSAN PERIMETER 1 (5 August 1950)<br><br>Comrade General, the end of our campaign for liberation is in sight.  We have driven away the capitalist forces of the South and United Nations down into a corner on our Korean peninsula.  The enemy is getting reinforced and the Southern army has regained strength.  Our army has been advancing for over a month and is getting exhausted but our hatred against the capitalist oppressors is driving us forward!<br><br>You have been put in command of the entire operation and will command our best comrades.  We will not give the enemy a chance to concentrate its forces by attacking almost across the entire front.  We will destroy them or drive them into the sea!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamppu2.xml", "Pusan Perimeter 2", "PUSAN PERIMETER 2 (30 August 1950)<br><br>Are you ready, Comrade General?  Good.  We expected nothing less.  We have increased your People's Army's strength as best we could.  Almost 100,000 eager troops are under your command.  Even some new T-34 tanks have been brought forward.  You will lead them in our liberation of the Pusan Perimeter!<br><br>The plan has not changed.  We will attack along the entire front and break the enemy line.  I will de-brief you in Pusan!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampwon.xml", "Wonsan", "WONSAN (10 October 1950)<br><br>Ah there you are, Comrade General.  That was a close encounter at that village near Kansong.  Fortunately we both made it out in time!  Quickly, we have no time to lose!  The enemy has crossed the border at the 38th Parallel and is now advancing into North Korea!  While the fury of our people can be seen in every village, our People's Army is in bad shape after retreating for hundreds of miles.  There are many troops fighting as partisans behind capitalist lines and in fact these few men and their equipment are the largest intact force we know of.  Naturally we are rebuilding our army deep in the mountains of North Korea and even across the border in Chinese owned Manchuria!<br><br>For now, you have other problems to deal with.  You have just reached the large port of Wonsan, but we cannot hold it for long.  Divisions of the capitalistic Southerners are close to Wonsan and might even try to cut off our route of retreat.  To buy us more time you must prevent this from happening and hold Wonsan as long as possible.  An untrained, fresh regiment of Communist Marines will be put under your command and even some mechanized guns are in the city.  We will meet in Hungnam next time!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18, "support": [9]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampcho.xml", "Chongju", "CHONGJU (27 October 1950)<br><br>Great news, Comrade General.  The warnings given by the Chinese premier Zhou Enlai did not turn the stupid capitalist armies.  Now the people of China will support its Korean comrades in the struggle against capitalism.  Our armies have been allowed to reorganize in Manchuria and for days the Chinese have massed forces just across the Yalu waiting for the right moment to launch a counteroffensive!<br><br>Meanwhile we must resist the capitalist advance as long as possible.  This task will be easier with each passing sunrise as the Americans and their South Korean slaves have serious supply problems.   Your force has retreated to Chongju near the Yalu River which is the border with Chinese Manchuria.  You will defend this city and the vicinity against any attacks and if possible advance to pave the way for our Chinese comrades to assemble for a counteroffensive!   We must not let the enemy reach the Yalu River!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [3, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamphon.xml", "Hongch'on", "HONGCH'ON (26 December 1950)<br><br>The communist cause is stronger than ever!  The combined might of the expeditionary Chinese Liberation Army and the rebuilt North Korean People's Army will destroy the imperialistic ambitions on the Korean peninsula!  Our Chinese comrades have pushed the enemy back to just below the 38th Parallel.  Unfortunately our advance is losing steam; even spirited citizens cannot endure this much longer!  The United Nations is regaining its strength but we still own the momentum and we will not give it away until we see the last capitalists leave our Korea!<br><br>Take a look at this map, Comrade General.   It clearly shows that the Chinese have manned a line from the western coast to the central mountains.  Our People's Army will operate in the mountains and along the eastern coast!  Your Corps is deployed near Kansong but now you have orders to attack the southern positions between the coast to the east and the Hwach'on Reservoir to the west.   We still do not have the firepower needed to continue frontal assaults on the enemy.  You are familiar with our doctrine: \"Penetrate as deep as possible and then turn on the enemy flanks\".   We will meet again at your ultimate goal: Honch'on!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [6, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampwdr.xml", "Wonju Deep Raid", "WONJU DEEP RAID (7 January 1951)<br><br>Sorry for the interruption, Comrade General.  Orders have been given to continue the offensive.  We have reached the important communication center of Wonju.  The town is expected to be heavily guarded by capitalist forces, most likely to prevent an uprising of the Korean people against the imperialists!  Your Corps will attack due south and slip around Wonju from the east.  Making good use of the hills will allow you to penetrate deep into the enemy line.  Our V Corps will keep the forces west and north of Wonju occupied.  The enemy is gaining strength but we have still have them reeling.  Race forward, Comrade General!  Free Korea!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [6, 17, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncamphoe.xml", "Hoengsong", "HOENGSONG (11 February 1951)<br><br>Indeed, Comrade General.  It is clear that the imperialists have never heard of Sun Tzu.  Since we are very vulnerable; we should avoid getting involved in their offensive and retreat some miles to a strong defensive position.   Now we are better prepared to go on the offensive again and continue our push south!<br><br>This night, in cooperation with our Chinese Allies, we have resumed our offensive south.  It is restricted to the central sector near Hoengsong.  Our Chinese comrades have broken through the South Korean positions with their usual infiltrating tactics into enemy lines. Hoengsong itself is likely to be reinforced by the imperialists with their guns made by enslaved comrades in America.  While the Chinese attack from the west and north, you will attack from the east.  Show the communist strength by liberating Hoengsong and destroy any enemy you may find!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [17, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampmun.xml", "Munsan-ni", "MUNSAN-NI (22 March 1951)<br><br>Comrade General, follow me into this room.  Here.  This map is top secret.  You can see the advance that the imperialists have made.  In the central and eastern sectors heavy opposition was encountered from the enemy armies and we slowly gave ground, but always organized!   We do not run off like scared the capitalist dogs!  All has been quiet in the western sector and we have almost totally evacuated the region between the Imjin and Han Rivers.  We don't want the enemy to trap us there.  There is only a Chinese rearguard and some of your units still there.  Just half an hour ago I was ambushed by those capitalist swine when driving to Corps HQ.  It seems the enemy has sent in reinforcements from the air to block our retreat.  Yes, Comrade General, indeed.  We just evacuated the bulk of your forces but now go and quickly get your remaining troops out.  Seoul has just been recaptured and we will be under attack from multiple sides!  Once the road is opened we will drive to HQ in Kaesong!  Now hurry up, Comrade General, there is no time to waste!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [19, 21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampspr.xml", "Spring Offensive First Phase", "SPRING OFFENSIVE FIRST PHASE (22 April 1951)<br><br>This is the moment we have been waiting for, Comrade General.  The Chinese have prepared a huge force for an offensive aimed at destroying the capitalists!  Two North Korean Corps will attack near the eastern coast, while your Corps will attack along the western coast in the direction of Seoul.  The Chinese will attack in the middle.  The imperialists do have more guns, firepower and aircraft than we have but we have more men.  Most importantly are men are highly motivated.  This will overcome any obstacle!  Now go forward and liberate Korea!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [11, 16, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampsp2.xml", "Spring Offensive Second Phase", "SPRING OFFENSIVE SECOND PHASE (14 May 1951)<br><br>You must have heard it already at the Chinese headquarters Comrade General but let us go through the situation once more.  The offensive directed at Seoul has been halted in favor of a new offensive in the central and eastern sectors where the terrain is more to our advantage.  In the mountains the Americans cannot use their artillery and aircraft to full advantage.  Your Corps, along with major Chinese units, have been transferred to these sectors.  This offensive must succeed, Comrade General.  Do not let us down!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25, "support": [21]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [6, 17, 18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["ncampgue.xml", "Majon-ni", "MAJON-NI (11 November 1950)<br><br>Comrade General, our Chinese comrades are pushing south.  Since September we have left many troops behind during our retreat north.  Partisan groups have been formed to harass enemy communications and other targets in its rear.  However strong leadership can only help.  You will be flown by a small aircraft to a partisan group near the village Majon-ni halfway between Wonsan and our capital P'yongyang.  You will lead operations against the enemy there.  We know little but it appears that a South Korean battalion has been cut off.  American troops are on the way to rescue them.  You know what to do.<br><br>In two weeks the Chinese should have passed your area and you will be put back in command of your refitted troops.  Until then, harass the enemy as much as possible, destroy as much equipement as possible and show them that the communist cause will be victorious even after many bad turns!<br><br>Technical note: you will not be able to deploy any core units in this scenario. However from the next scenario onwards you can again.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], "eqp-lxf"],
["A Long Journey to Freedom (1848-1865)"],
["aljf_0.xml", "Prologue: Knechtschaft oder Revolution!", "20. 4. 1848, Prologue: Knechtschaft oder Revolution! (Slavery or Revolution!)<br><br>Lieber Freund,<br>not much time to write, hastily a short note for you:<br>I joined Friedrich Hecker who is negotiating at the moment with prussian general Friedrich von Gagen.<br>Von Gagen wants unconditional surrender which we never will accept.<br>But still we are not enough men, so we have to flee from here. At Rhine and Neckar we will surely find a lot of supporters...<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Save Friedrich Hecker or the Revolution will be lost!<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>It is important for us to gain experience but we should withdraw to the east....!", [{"id": 1, "country": 176}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_1.xml", "Der Heckerzug", "20. 4. 1848, Der Heckerzug (Hecker's Uprising)<br><br>Lieber Freund,<br><br>...I feel, now the time has come !<br>I've joined the \"Heckerzug\" and fight for a free, democratic Republic for all Germans.....<br><br>To hell with all those Dukes and Earls !<br>To hell with all Prussians !<br>Vivat the german Republic !<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Herr General, free all the Main Cities around the Neckar and take you radvance to the important City of Freiburg. <br>Reinforces from every liberated City will join our Revolution Army and the german democratic Legion aproaching in the South.<br>Hurry up! Our Spies report enemy forces, arriving in the east in a few days.<br>The Capital of Baden, Karlsruhe, we must take later.<br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Herr General, we must hurry up: speed is the key; but dont forget our back.....<br>And before you attack Freiburg, you must gather your troops !<br><br>NOTE:<br>It is only possible to deploy Friedrich Hecker at hex (29,29).", [{"id": 1, "country": 176, "support": [175]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["aljf_2.xml", "The Palataine Uprising", "13. 6. 1849, The Palataine Uprising<br><br>Lieber Freund,<br><br>...this is the opportunity, we have been waiting for: the Palatains continue the Fight for the Republic, and we have joined them.<br>The Prussians have send some of their best troops, but in our hearts is still burning a hot flame of freedom....<br>Vivat the german Republic !<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Herr General, this becomes a hard battle, we have to defend the revolution against the famous Prussian army....<br>Reinforces from every liberated city will join our Revolution army.<br>Liberate and defend the Land !<br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Herr General, we have no chance in the open field, stay in the hills and let them come....<br>...Try to flank the enemy artillery, and destroy them at first!<br>...keep in mind, that men from every liberated city will join our army...<br>And it seems, there are no enemies in the West...", [{"id": 1, "country": 157, "support": [176]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["aljf_3.xml", "The decisive Battle at Wagh\u00e4usel", "21. 6. 1849, The decisive Battle at Waghäusel<br><br>Lieber Freund,<br>...the superior prussian Army has pushed us back over the Rhine River, but the People in Baden, and their whole army have joined the Revolution again !<br>...now, we are encircled by the enemy and we must fight for our lives and the Republic....<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Herr General, many enemies in every direction.....<br>But we are in a good strategical position, and the Baden Army has joined our side...<br>We must hold our lines...<br>If we win this, I'm sure there will be uprisings in all german States...<br><br>HOLD 6, 4, 2 VH's for BV, V, TV<br><br>IMPORTANT NOTE:<br>Because of the historical correctness it's very hard to reach a BV", [{"id": 1, "country": 157, "support": [175]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 196, "support": [176]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["aljf_4.xml", "The St. Luis Arsenal", "May, 10., 1861 The St. Luis Arsenal<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>since I have been here I spent many years as Teacher and Editor of a \"german\" Journal....  <br>Me and my former Comrades have foundeed many gymnastics Clubs, Pubs, Factories... and Families...<br><br>For a long Time I have not thought about War and Battles.... but now our new freedom is threatened again. <br>I will never admit that a Man will be another Man´s Slave!<br><br>...So again I move into Battle...<br><br>----{secret telegraph depeche to general}-----<br>THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON,<br><br>General,<br>with Excitement we hear that our german Friends have formed four volunteer Regiments.<br>We regret that we must inform you that we will not be able to send you Support because at the moment all Connections are in the Hand of our Enemy.<br><br>Recommend requisition of Weapons out of St.Luis Arsenal...!<br><br>Further orders to follow......<br><br>THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES<br>-----{end of secret telegraph depeche}----<br><br>ORDERS:<br>what shall we do? Forward !!<br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>nor purchase, nor upgrade possible....we need at first the St. Luis Arsenal and supply Connections to the North....", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_5.xml", "The Boonville Races", "June, 17., 1861 The Boonville Races<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>wir haben uns mit modernem material ausgerüstet, und ziehen laut befehl nach westen- wenn wir die rebellen aus boonville vertreiben sind unsere versorgungswege bis auf weiteres sicher....<br><br>ORDERS:<br>General, we send you a ship to support your troops. hurry up ! we need boonville fast !<br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Dont forget to equip your men with modern weapons....<br><br>dear friend,<br><br>we have got modern matrerial and now move westward as ordered- if we drive the rebels out of Boonville our supply connections will be secure for some time", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_6.xml", "Flank them at Wilson's Creek", "August, 10., 1861 Wilson's Creek<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>the northern border of Missouri should be safe .... but now we have to annihilate the last rebel units to secure our supplylines...<br><br>General Sigel proposed to use one of our most successful strategies of the 48 revolution: General Lyon should occupy the enemy troops frontally and General Sigel and we will sneak into its back...<br><br>ORDERS:<br>General Sigel's Men, Forward ! Attack them in their Back !<br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Attention ! If you loose your last captured VH, you've lost the Battle !", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_7.xml", "Battle of the Hemp Bales", "September, 20., 1861 Battle of the Hemp Bales<br>Lexington, Missouri<br><br>Dear Friend, <br><br>the Missouri State Guard is attacking us for 8 days now. Thanks to god, we were able to build entrenchments before the fighting began. Now, our hospital at Anderson's House is  full  of many wounded soldiers and we are short of ammo and water. The only spring is under constant confederate fire and our canteens are almost empty.<br><br>They are rolling hemp bales up the hills and use them as a cover. We are loading our rifles and guns with red hot iron bullets but they soaked the hemp bales in missouri waters and our salvos won't light them up at all! We can only continue fighting for a short time, maybe only till the end of this day. We are going to die of thirst or will loose the battle and become prisoners of the Confederation!<br><br>ORDERS:<br><br>Hold the defense positions at Masonic College and Andersons's House north of Lexington and stop the confederate advance. Later you may want to take Lexington if possible.<br><br>Hold 4 VH for a brilliant victory<br>Hold 2 VH for a victory<br>Hold 1 VH for a tactical victory<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Sir, I don't think we can hold all positions at the same time. It seems to be a better tactic to defend one stronghold and recapture the other objectives later.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_8.xml", "Spearhead at Pea Ridge", "March, 3., 1862 Pea Ridge<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>our order is to secure Arkansas for the Union !<br><br>As we have won Missouri for us I think our meanwhile well established cavallery will free Arkansas quickly too...<br><br>Seemingly at the moment only weak enemy forces stand there against us, but reconnaissance reports that the Confederates have sent General van Dom with a relieving army....<br><br>ORDERS:<br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Don´t let the two Confederate army groups get into contact with each other !", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_9.xml", "Assault at Kernstown", "March, 23., 1862 Kernstown<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>now the time has come to draw our attack into enemy country...<br><br>I got command for our attack on Virginia...!<br><br>ORDERS:<br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>you should purchase some additional artillery and/or cavalry.<br>(watch out: a cheaper artillery, but with support-Fire [no \"s\"] is a better desicion as a heavy artillery with NO support-fire)<br>maybe a modern MG would be a wise decision, too....<br>and dont forget to upgrade your units from time to time....<br>---   * - *   ---<br>at first, you should just hold the Kernstown-line, and take glasshouse in the west; then move with your glasshouse-group forward to Kernstown...then you can attack Kernstown from two sides...<br>DONT attack Kernstown just with one group trough the river... tha´ts suicide !", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_10.xml", "Retreat at Bull Run", "August, 28., 1862 Retreat at Bull Run<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>General Lee fought his way trough all our armies and stands now close to Washington....but more bad news: the enemy uses our famous strategy and flanks us.... we must draw back to better positions.... <br>An orderly retreat...: one of the most difficult manuveurs...<br><br>ORDERS:<br>General, an enemy army, coming from the South !.... If we hold the actual positions, our Army, Washington and maybe the whole war is lost !....we must draw back and build a defense line on better positions...<br><br>HOLD ALL THE VH !<br><br>NOTE: In this Scenario \"Skip first Player Turn\" is activated : The Confederates starts...<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Dont forget: we must hold ALL VH's !", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_11.xml", "Must hold Harper's Ferry", "September, 15., 1862 Harpers Ferry<br><br>Dear Friend, we have been ordered to Harpers Ferry. It's such a beautiful place! A little town and important railroad crossing, were the Shenandoah and Potamac Rivers meet, surrounded by mountains...<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Stay calm and defend this very important town! Surrender is not an option!<br>If possible take the Maryland Heights and try to size Jackson's HQ at Keller.<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>No matter from which direction the wind is blowing -I can smell the confederats!", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}, {"id": 2, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_12.xml", "Take Fredericksburg", "December, 13., 1862 Fredericksburg<br><br>Dear Friend, this night we reached the city of Fredericksburg. The confederates had destroyed all bridges across Rappahannock River. Our sappers were busy building ponton bridges instead. We have been ordered to cross the river and attack the confederate positions on the heights west of Fredericksburg and the railway. <br>This mission seems to be insane!<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Congratulations Sir, we received a message from President Lincoln and the Army Headquaters and you will be promoted to Major General! Due to the reorganisation of the Army of the Potamac, you will command our new formed corps. Four regiments of colored soldiers will be attached to your core units.<br>....Cross the river and take the heights...!<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>A direct attack seems to be suicide but maybe we should remember Franz Sigel's favorite tactic and send the Cavalry far away to one of the flanks!<br><br>HISTORICAL NOTE:<br>The colored infantry regiments which join your core did not take part at the historic Battle of Fredericksburg or were established later but have been implemented at this point of the campaign for a better core development.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_13.xml", "Battle of Chancellorsville", "May, 2., 1863 Chancellorsville<br><br>Dear Friend, we are sitting in the middle of nowhere, waiting for the enemy. They are somewhere in the woods. This region is called \"The Wilderness\", and that's how it looks here: Deep forests and small creeks.... <br><br>ORDERS:<br>We have lost contact to the enemy armies! It is unclear what will happen and your orders are to keep position.<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Hold the line !!!", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_14.xml", "The Siege of Vicksburg", "May, 19., 1863  Vicksburg<br><br>Dear Friend, <br>the president has attached the USS Moose to our army corps... <br>I think she will be quite useful for us in the future...<br>So here I am again back to the Mississipi valley where everything started for me...<br>After all the drawbacks here a unique chance is offered to us.<br><br>ORDERS:<br>General, if Vicksburg is taken, only Port Hudson is left as last resort on the Mississipi for the rebels...   <br>If we can control both cities we have split the Confederates in two pieces....<br><br>TAKE AL VHs<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>do not sell the USS Moose ! <br>She will be of benefit for us till the end of war...<br><br>you should deploy most of your men in the west, to take the desoto peninsula.... and your cavalry should help in the east....", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_15.xml", "Gettysburg", "July, 1., 1863  Gettysburg<br><br>Dear Friend, <br>once again the best rebel general, General Lee, has penetrated far into the north of our territory...<br>He is threatening Washington D.C. as well as Baltimore and Philadelphia, and in addition he is tying useful troops of us up here...<br>Our cavallery scouts have spotted a  confederate reconnaissance unit near Gettysburg...expecting the mass of Lee´s army to be close our troops errected provisional defense positions around Gettysburg in the last moment..<br>My army Corps originally was intended to support the South East but being near by chance we have to support our comrades in Gettysburg...<br>My men think it has been only a small enemy rec unit, but I am sure General Lee will be here with the mass of his troops any moment...<br><br>ORDERS:<br>General, it is good fortune that you have been near. Strengthen immediately the front of Gettysburg with your men !<br>This might well be one of the decisive battles of the war... if we loose here the Hinterland is wide open for Lee... if we win, we will break the neck of general Lee´s army and do away with a permanent threat !<br>Hold the Codori- Heights at any cost !!!<br>Enemy reinforcement, the II. confederate Corps, will arrive from the west....<br>Our reinforcements are exected from the east and later on from the south.....<br><br>HOLD 4/3/2 VHs FOR BV/V/TV<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>If not already done, you should definitely deliver transport for your core-infantery: they have to disburden our comrades in Gettysburg as fast as possible...<br>It might be that we have to give up Gettysburg for the moment and to reconquer it later....<br>Eventually we should shorten our frontline and draw back; but on the other side our positions in the mountains are very valuable... so you have to act with care..<br>We should keep some pp in reserve, if we might be necessary to refresh our troops.... draw battered troops and those without ammunition from the first line and replace them immediately...<br><br>BE AWARE of Longstreet´s confederate reinforcement in the WEST. You should send our Corps against them FIRST !", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_16.xml", "Meeting at Bristoe Station", "October, 14., 1863  Bristoe Station<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>I have only time for a short letter.... The recent days saw only minor skirmishes. We don't know what is going on, and it seems our maneuvers were unsuccessful... <br>Now we are on our way to Manasas Junction and were marching all day long....<br>I have only few minutes because we can hear some battle noise from far ahead of us. Will it be a minor skirmish again?<br><br>ORDERS:<br>The Confederates are attacking the II corps but it seems they are not aware your corps is close behind. Repell the attack and continue your way to Manassas Junction. Reports from our scouts suggest that the enemy will attack from the north only.<br><br>Retreat 30 core and/or auxilliary units. (There is a total of 22 auxilliary units + some reinforements)<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Sir, may I suggest to stay near the railroad and keep the troops together?", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_17.xml", "Seamonsters at Charleston", "February, 17., 1864  Charleston<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>We have been on board of the ship for a week now. Most of us are sea-sick. We were sailing along the coast from New York City to the south. <br>There are rumors about our destination.... Is it Savannah or Wilmington? Charleston or Mobile? The officers dont't tell us no matter how often we ask. I hope next time when I write a letter I will stand on solid ground....<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Charleston is a important confederate port and one of the largest cities in the CSA. Taking Charleston will be vital for us and would weaken the confederates. You and your corps have been selected to carry out an amphibious landing operation. Some of our troops have already taken position in the southern swamps.<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Sir, it seems it is not necessary to take all of the forts and batteries. Most of them are protected by immobile units. Sir, we also hear rumors about sea monsters!<br><br>NOTE:<br>This is a (\"half-\") fictive scenario!<br><br>There were many battles in the Charleston area, but the Union was not able to take possession of the city before 18th February 1865.<br><br>04/1861 - Fort Sumter bombarded by CSA troops<br>12/1861 - The Union Navy sank 24 block ships <br>06/1862 - Battle of Secessionville <br>04/1863 - First Battle of Charleston Harbor<br>07/1863 - First Battle of Fort Wagner<br>07/1863 - Second Battle of Fort Wagner<br>08/1863 - \"Swamp Angel\" bombarding Charleston<br>09/1863 - Second Battle of Fort Sumter<br>02/1864 - H.L. Hunley sank USS Housatonic.<br>07/1864 - amphibious assault on Fort Johnson<br>02/1865 - Charleston surrendered", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_18.xml", "The Cadets in New Market", "May, 5., 1864  New Market<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>Once again our old friend Franz Sigel has taken command in our corps.... we have not met for a long time and the first night we talked an drank beer together...it has really been a long journey from the battlefields at the Rhine river up to here into Shenandoah valley....<br>Our original orders were to defend our own railway connections and to destroy the enemy ones...<br>But now Lee has sent General Breckinridge against us with all men he could collect...<br>The rebels seem to be really desperate now: they refreshed Breckinridge´s troops even with cadets from the Virginia Military Institute...<br>At this moment our vanguard has met Breckinridge´s men so I must hurry into our forward line...<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Take all VH's<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Caution ! We are deep in enemy country without lateral connection to our lines...we should reconnoiter in all directions and move forward very carefully !!!", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_19.xml", "Sigel's Last Command", "July, 4., 1864  Harper's Ferry<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>Once again we are in the Harper's Ferry vicinity. <br>When the confederate army under Jubel A. Early was approaching us, General Sigel gave orders to evacuate the city. We took positions north of the Potomac river on the Maryland Heights. <br>We hear rumors that the High Command of the Army once again fell in disfavor with Sigel and that he will be replaced soon. <br>We also received orders to attack in the next hours and retake the strategic important Harper's Ferry bridges, as well as the city.<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Retake the city!<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Sir, we should cross the rivers up- or downstream. The riverside at Harper's Ferry seems to be well defended....", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_20.xml", "Our Marines at Mobile Bay", "August, 5., 1864  Mobile Bay<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>We spend weeks travelling down the Mississippi and once we arrived at New Orleans, we had to board ocean going transport ships. <br>I was able to write and send this letter just before we left New Orleans for the Gulf of Mexico. They say we will sail westwards. So Florida is not our destination! It must be Alabama or Texas. <br>There are some siege engineers on our ship - does that mean we have to attack fortifications? I hope to receive a letter from you soon, no matter were I will be!<br><br>ORDERS:<br>Bombard the forts with your ships and weaken the defense. Then land your forces on the islands and capture the forts.<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Sir, we should deploy the USS Moose near the front of our line of battle. You know, the good old Moose is not the fastest ship in the Navy...", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_21.xml", "The Siege of Petersburg", "October, 25., 1864  Petersburg<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>our army corps has reached Petersburg...from here important roads and rails lead in all directions....but especially Petersburg controls the last working railway to Richmond...<br>by now we only control the area east of Petersburg.... <br>Trying to undermine the confederate fortifications south-east of Petersburg, sappers already created a huge crater in the rebel position. But it has been of little use as the walls of the crater are too steep to climp up, our attack commando has been brutally killed in attempting to make it up...<br>We will see what the HQ plans for my corps....<br><br>ORDERS:<br>General, looking at our forces, I still feel that it is impossible to take Petersburg frontally; but with the support of your army corps we are able to lay siege to Petersburg and cut it off from all connections...<br>Doing this, we also have encircled the rebel capital Richmond.<br><br>Transports delivering reinforcements will arrive from the east and our cavalry will be here soon coming from the south-east<br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>In the beginning, move forward with care and stay connected.<br>We should concentrate on our goals in the west; our cavalry corps will be very useful later there..", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_22.xml", "The U.S.C.T. attacks Fort Fisher", "January, 13., 1865  Fort Fisher<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>contrary to some other generals, I really appreciate my black units. Some of my best units are formed from black men...Finally we conduct this war for them and for the freedom of all men... as we did in 1848.. <br><br>ORDERS:<br>General, we have to take these important navy bases under all circumstances ... best land your troops on the peninsula north of Fort Fisher but keep some landing units for landing in th outmost west, after the sea has been cleared from enemies.<br>Be aware of the confederate fleet !<br>For our own fleet support will arrive in a few hours.<br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>NOTE: From this Scenario on, new purchased Units will start with 99 exp. pnts.<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>-buy or better upgrade some of your experienced units to sappers. they will be ble to better attack enemy fortresses and to build ports on Cape fear river..<br>-the slaves on confederate farms are waiting for being liberated and getting some preyed weapons from us so they can  join us in the battle..<br>-Scout the Cape fear river completely! According to our latest intelligence reports the confederate Cape fear river flotilla is still there!<br><br>Remark that different types of ships may use different areas...:<br>[ cape fear river is \"shallow sea\" in contrast to open sea \"ocean\". Activate unit view and move your mouse carefully on the move-icon in the upper right. Now you will see the moving points: 255 means not reachable, 1= normal move,2= double cost for move. If for a ship you see : \"shallow sea=255/ocean=1\" then this ship may only move in the open sea but not the Cape fear river. \"shallow sea=1/ocean=2\" means that ship may move on Cape fear river and the open sea but with double cost on open sea. <br>If you use\" additional options\" in the menu and activate submenu \"area\"there you will see the actual areas on the map ]", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_23.xml", "Close the Trap", "April, 1., 1865  Close the Trap (Ft. Stedman + Five Forks)<br><br>----{secret telegraph depeche to general}-----<br>THE WHITE HOUSE; WASHINGTON,<br><br>Dear Sir,<br>herewith, we comply with your request: General Franz Sigel will be detached as commander or your cavalry to your army corps. Furthermore we comply with the request of some of your best cavalrists to built a cavalry regiment of their own:<br>congratulations to the \"Revengers of Waghaeusel\" ! <br>Furthermore half of the liberated slaves from Fort Fisher wished to fight on with you: we have formed three regiments and have put them under your direct command....<br><br>THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES<br>-----{end of secret telegraph depeche}----<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>the rebels are quite desperate by now: General Lee exactly knows that by taking Petersburg, we would surround his whole army near Richmond.<br>If we close the siege and take Petersburg we have depraved General Lee from any action possibility.<br>Of course the rebels are aware of this, and I bet they will try everything to break the siege. I feel this might become one of the heaviest fights of the war. <br>Even more it has been raining for weeks and all rivers are impassable... my men are already joking that they will have to carry out their next land battle from canon boats. <br>But nevertheless, HQ has granted my request to put General Sigel in command of my cavalry... if its is about flanking, there is no one better than Franz....<br>It is dawning and I have to move to our positions....<br><br>ORDERS:<br>aah general, welcome to Fort Stedman  ...bourbon and beer?<br>well, meanwhile we gathered enough troops aruond Petersburg: time to take the next step...move forward with caution and take Petersburg and all the area south of Appomattox !<br>...then we have closed the trap for the rebels...<br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>NOTE: In this Scenario \"Skip first Player Turn\" is activated : The Confederates starts...<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Attention, General: the rebels are completely desperate and have nothing to loose....I bet my horse, my sabre and my pay of the next two years that they will attack us frontally disregarding losses.....", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_24.xml", "The Key to Richmond", "May, 9., 1865  The Key to Richmond<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>General Lee and President Davis flew to Richmond, capital of the CSA and their last stronghold. <br>Our men are joyous and some are already celebrating victory. But I fear there is still some hard fighting in front of us. I don't have time for a long letter, they put us in railroad cars and some of us had to board ships in order to steam upriver. I hope, that the war will be over when you receive my next letter!<br><br>ORDERS: Sir, now that we took Petersburg, the confederates are retreating to Richmond, their last stronghold and capital of the Confederate States of America. You and your Army have been ordered to proceed northwards and approach Richmond from the south. Only the Fortifications near the James River lie between us and Richmond. <br><br>Your orders are: Proceed northwards and take the Fortifications at Drewry's and Chaffin's Bluff and secure the Richmond & Petersburg Railroad. We captured a lot of locomotives and river steamboats at Petersburg, so transport of your heavy units should not be a problem. <br><br>Our Marines already established a bridgehead at the western ferry station.<br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>NOTE: <br>This is a fictive scenario.<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>Maybe we should send some additional men to the east while our main force advance on the western shore.", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["aljf_25.xml", "Final Assault at Richmond", "June, 23., 1865  Final Assault at Richmond<br><br>Dear Friend,<br>it is now that we are in front of the lion´s hole... the lion is hurted and has drawn back to the outmost corner of his cave... but he still is really dangerous..... may be even more dangerous then ever... before as he knows there is nothing to lose for him....<br><br>I do not know how this will end, but I feel this is the end of the war.. one way or the other..this is the final decision...<br>Wish me the best of luck. <br>I close this letter and will go to my men... it is dawning and the last attack is coming....<br><br>ORDERS: <br><br>TAKE ALL VH's<br><br>NOTE: <br>This is a fictive scenario.<br><br>ADVICE FROM YOUR OLDEST SERGEANT:<br>-You absolutely should keep some pp to refresh your troops during battle <br>-furthermore it would be a good idea to built ports at different places.<br>-Our cavalry should flank our attack at the right and the left side<br>-We can count on marines and later on infantry and cavalry support<br>-Furthermore the slaves from the confederate farms are only waiting to be freed to join our troops..", [{"id": 1, "country": 150}], [{"id": 0, "country": 162}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["Hungarian Soviet Republic (1919)"],
["rhu190416.xml", "1919/04/16 Escaping from Zilah (Zalau)", "Escaping from Zilah (Zalau)<br><br>April 16, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, the situation is dangerous. After our new, revolutionary government refused to retreat behind the new demarcation lines, the imperialist hyenas insited their capitalist lapdogs, the Romanian and the so called \"Czechoslovakian\" reactionists. They mobilized their armies and attacked our weak, inexperienced troops. Your job is securing the railway station at NagykÃ¡roly as long as possible to cover our retreat.<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least one VH, keep your MSU alive and move it onto the Escape Hex at NagykÃ¡roly.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- AI moves first.<br>- The longer you hold on, the better result you get.<br>- You have 3 free RTP slots.<br><br>12 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190424.xml", "1919/04/24 Breaking through Nyíregyháza", "Breaking through Nyíregyháza<br><br>April 24, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, our troops weren't able to stop the overwhelmind Romanian attacks. We executed a few ex-KuK officers but it didn't help too much. We should retreat behind the Tisza River. You'd better hurry, two Romanian pincers are closing around Nyíregyháza.<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least one VH, keep your MSU alive and move it onto the Escape Hex at Tokaj.<br><br>NOTE: You have 3 free RTP slots.<br><br>16 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190501.xml", "1919/05/01 Szolnok: Securing The Bridgehead", "Szolnok: Securing The Bridgehead<br><br>May 1, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, the Romanians have reached the Tisza, and a smaller vanguard has crossed the river at Szolnok. The retreat must end here and now, if the main troops of the reactionists can cross the Tisza, our proletarian state will collapse. Your job is to secure the western bank of the river and form a bridgehead on the eastern bank, if possible. But be cautious, more and more Romanian divisions are on their way.<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least 4 VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You are awarded by an Ammunition Wagon (depot RTP) detachment.<br>- You can purchase two new units.<br>- You have 4 free RTP slots.<br><br>14 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190509.xml", "1919/05/09 Defending Salgótarján", "Defending Salgótarján<br><br>May 9, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, while your troops defended Szolnok, the Czech henchmen of the capitalist warlords took Miskolc, the biggest industrial center in North-East Hungary. Now they are surrounding Salgótarján, the last city with steal factory and strong organized working class outside of Budapest. You should relieve Salgótarján immediately!<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least 2 VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can purchase three new units.<br>- You have 4 free RTP slots.<br><br>15 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190523.xml", "1919/05/23 Liberating Miskolc", "Liberating Miskolc<br><br>May 23, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, tens of thousands proletars joined the Hungarian Red Army. These factory workers are eager to fight against the capitalist marauders and their mercenaries. Though our new red soldiers aren't trained well enough to defeat the Romanians, we are ready to push back the Czechs, who are famous for their low commitment to fight. Comrade, let's liberate Miskolc!<br><br>ORDER: Take all VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can purchase two new units.<br>- You have 5 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190530.xml", "1919/05/30  Liberating Kassa (Koice)", "Liberating Kassa (Koice)<br><br>May 30, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, our offensive is going well, and our soldiers are eager to take a revenge for previous losses, another shiny victory would boost their morale. More importantly, there is a good opportunity to deliver a severe blow\tto the Czech marauders. Comrade, your job is to liberate Kassa with its important steel industry and railways junctions.<br><br>ORDER: Take all VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can purchase two new units.<br>- You have 5 free RTP slots.<br><br>18 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190609.xml", "1919/06/09 Bártfa (Bardejov): Reaching The Polish Border", "Bártfa (Bardejov): Reaching The Polish Border<br><br>June 9, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, the Czech capitalists are in disarray, they didn't expect how strong the Red Army of workers and peasants could be when they get a proper training about the dialectical materialism. Now we have a unique chance to cut off the Czech defense lines and separate the Romanian and Czech invaders once and for all. Let the Iron Fist of the factory workers smash these imperialist bandits! Your order is to liberate Bártfa near the Polish border.<br><br>ORDER: Take all VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can purchase two new units.<br>- You have 5 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190613.xml", "1919/06/13 Defending Érsekújvár (Nové Zámky)", "Defending Érsekújvár (Nové Zámky)<br><br>June 13, 1919<br><br>Ah, dear Comrade Commisar, have you got the dedicated copy of Lenin's The State and Revolution? Comrade Szamuely has just arrived from Moscow with the warmest greetings and this special present for you. Our international revolution is going well, our Slovakian comrades will declare their Soviet Republic within days. Unfortunately these pesky Czech marauders simply can't accept their defeat, and they launched a strong counterattack in the area of Nyitra (Nitra) - Vág (Váh) - Garam (Hron) rivers. Give these imperialist lapdogs a bloody nose again!<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least 3 VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can repurchase only the lost units.<br>- Both sides get valuable reinforcements.<br>- You have 5 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 47}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190719.xml", "1919/07/19 Szolnok-Mezöhegyes Offensive", "Szolnok-Mezöhegyes Offensive<br><br>July 19, 1919<br><br>The imperialists fooled us. They promised the Romanian troops would withdraw behind the demarcation line declared on March 20 in exchange for our withdrawal from the Fölvidék (Upper Hungary). But the enemies of our communist revolution broke their words, and their Romanian mercenaries are still staying behind the Tisza. It's time to teach these truce-breakers a hard lesson and liberate our proletarian sisters and brothers by force! Lead our troops to victory, Comrade Commisar!<br><br>ORDER: Take all VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- You can repurchase only the lost units.<br>- AI gets valuable reinforcements.<br>- You have 6 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["rhu190724.xml", "1919/07/21 Szolnok: The Collapse", "Szolnok: The Collapse<br><br>July 24, 1919<br><br>Comrade Commisar, the situation is critical. Though we have managed to cross Tisza at three locations, and we have gained a large bridgehead east of Szolnok, our offensive has stalled. Our soldiers are exhausted, we have serious difficulties to resupply them, while more and more fresh Romanian troops are arriving at the battlefields. We suspects some of the former KuK officiers in our rank have betrayed our Soviet Republic and delivered important intels to the imperialists. Comrade, a strong and overwhelming capitalist counterattack is imminent! Save our revolution and do not let them cross the Tisza!<br><br>ORDER: Hold at least three VHs and keep your MSU alive.<br><br>NOTES:<br>- AI moves first.<br>- You can repurchase only the lost units.<br>- AI gets valuable reinforcements.<br>- You have 4 free RTP slots.<br><br>20 Turns<br><br>Scenario designed by Csaba (lvjtn)", [{"id": 0, "country": 187}], [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["Bolshevik Cavalry (1918-1920)"],
["ccampore.xml", "Voronezh", "VORONEZH (22 OCTOBER 1919)<br><br>Comrade Commander! Come quickly, we must act swiftly.  Let me introduce you. I am the political commissar attached to your command.  The capitalist swine's are close to crushing our glorious revolution!  The Great War is over but the war for communism is still in its early phase.  We have overthrown the Tsar but that has not stopped the capitalists, monarchists and other enemies of the people to unite, raise forces and march on our people's republic!  Petrograd lies under attack and Siberia is under enemy control.   Now from the Ukraine a certain traitor named Denikin is directing his army towards our capital of Moscow!<br><br>But we are not defeated yet!  While the White armies of Denikin march north, their front becomes wider and wider.  Our Eight Army has just now lost the city of Voronezh at the Don River.  However the army is still intact and resumes fighting.  Reinforcements from Moscow are on their way as we speak!  Your newly formed command of the First Cavalry Army has been ordered to move out and attack Voronezh from the west.  Indeed comrade, you will be cutting through their flank like a knife through butter! <br><br>Do not stop for nothing.  Go for your objectives.  Make terror your weapon!  Liberate the peasants of Voronezh!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampros.xml", "Rostov", "ROSTOV (6 January 1920)<br><br>I bring good news from Moscow, comrade!  The leaders are very happy with your progress.  The fear of a successful army full of horse warriors is excellent propaganda material.  Yet it is not only propaganda!  Your army has not been defeated and is close to dealing another crucial blow to the capitalist's cause in southern Russia!<br><br>The momentum still lies with our cause!  The capitalist armies are ever retreating further  south.  Your Army has the opportunity to capture the important communication center of Rostov.  If we control Rostov the Caucasus will also fall into our hands!<br><br>Again, comrade, do not watch your back. Only go for Rostov and do not let your troops be stopped by road blocks or anything else important. It is vital that we capture Rostov before the capitalist swines have the time to reinforce the city!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampvol.xml", "Battle of Volodarka", "BATTLE OF VOLODARKA (29 May 1920)<br><br>Comrade, finally all of your command has arrived at the new front in the west.  The front against the Poles!  The newly emerged Polish state has invaded our sacred territory both in the Belarus as here in the Ukraine.  Kiev has fallen into Polish hands already but again the enemy is widespread and this offers chances to turn the tide!<br><br>Your force will assemble south of Kiev and attack the Polish positions well south of Kiev.  Your goal will be to force a way through the Polish line and open up a gap so we can pour in infantry and cut off the enemy at Kiev.  Your operation will be supported by the 3rd Don Cossack Brigade which is few days march behind you.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampkie.xml", "Kiev Counteroffensive", "KIEV COUNTEROFFENSIVE (9 June 1920)<br><br>The Revolution is on its way to the West!  Comrade, a major offensive by our armies north and south of Kiev has pushed back the Polish bandits.  Even blind people can see that Kiev is about to fall.  Or better said, given back to the people of Kiev!<br><br>Your Cavalry Army has taken part of the push south of Kiev and is now in excellent position to cut off the capitalist's troops still in Kiev.  The Twelfth Army is approaching Kiev from the east.  The Polish criminals have no respect for the property of the Kiev people and are likely to demolish the bridges and perhaps even more!  You are ordered to liberate Kiev, and join up with Twelfth Army and advance as far as you can to the west!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccamprov.xml", "Delay at Rovno", "DELAY AT ROVNO (1 July 1920)<br><br>No, comrade, you do have to worry about your food supply.  Take anything from the country as you go.  The people will help you and if they do not it is because they are still terrified of repressions by the capitalist pigs.  Now let us go back to our plan of operations, comrade. <br><br>After our success at Kiev, the entire front in the Ukraine is moving west.  And still is! The Polish armies are far from defeated but they lack the power to stop our people's army for once and for all.  While our strategic goal will be Lwow, or Lemberg as the old imperialists from Germany would name it.  However the Poles seem to everything to stop them from liberating the people they are oppressing!<br><br>You are near Rovno.  As always you know what to do.  Capture all vital communication centers and push as far west as possible.  Most of all let nothing stop you!  Like a tornado you must use your mobility.  After all it is the symbol for cavalry!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccampbro.xml", "Battle of Brody", "BATTLE OF BRODY (29 July 1920)<br><br>The war is going excellently!  The Revolution will soon liberate the rest of Europe and join with other communists all over the continent!  But first we must concentrate on capturing Warsaw in the north and Lwow here in the south!<br><br>Yesterday your forces captured the town of Brody.  Your pursuit of the Polish Army has left them shattered and desperately awaiting reserves.  Let them tremble under the hooves of your horses!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [191]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccampzad.xml", "Battle of Zadworze", "BATTLE OF ZADWORZE (17 August 1920)<br><br>Comrade, let me quote something for the French socialist newspaper \"L'Humanite\" from early August.  \"Not a man, not a soul, not a shell for reactionary and capitalist Poland. Long live the Russian Revolution!  Long live the Workmen's International!\"  As you can see our struggle against the capitalists is not going unnoticed.  The eyes of the socialists all over the world are upon us!<br><br>Now back to the battle situation, comrade!  There will be time for rejoicing after our victory is certain!  I know I have been saying this for days but Lwow is now really within our grasp.  We stand some 50 kilometers from Lwow and it appears that there is little between us and the city.  However we cannot take a city, always a very hostile terrain for cavalry, without infantry support and better supply.  Hence, it is vital that we capture the railroad junction of Zadworze.  What the capitalists can gather to resist, I cannot tell. What I can tell is that within days we will be marching into Lwow!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccamplwo.xml", "Lwow", "LWOW (20 August 1920)<br><br>Comrade there lays the old city of Lwow.  It was the goal of the Tsar in 1914, Brusilov in 1916 and our goal in 1920.  The goal of the Revolution!<br><br>Our Red Army is closing in on the city from the north and east.  Do I have to tell you about the instructions from Moscow?  They are expecting the Red Flag of the Revolution in Lwow as soon as possible!  Divisions of our Fourteenth Army are closely following your cavalry.  Polish resistance is unknown although interrogations have reported that the Poles bought time at Zadworze for defensive and offensive operations.  I believe these are capitalistic and criminal lies imprinted on the Polish soldiers.<br><br>Go, comrade, liberate Lwow!!!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20, "support": [64]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["ccampkom.xml", "Battle of Komarow", "BATTLE OF KOMAROW (29 August 1920)<br><br>I have some bad news, comrade.  A few days ago while you were busy trying to capture Lwow; the Polish imperialists started a counteroffensive pushing through the center of the line between Lwow and Warsaw.  After their breakthrough they turned north and now the entire northern command is retreating in order not to be encircled!  Our dreams of capturing Warsaw have to be shelved!<br><br>Your cavalry is needed north!  If you sweep northwards and cut into the right flank of the Polish offensive we might again turn the tide and Poland will be liberated from their reactionary capitalists!<br><br>The Poles have been able to form some kind of defensive line while you were pulling back from the Lwow operation.  However, this is no reason to be worried.  I am talking about the Cavalry Army!  It has not been defeated for months and just saying the name strikes terror into the enemy!  Strike north, and join up with our people's army in the north!!!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampro2.xml", "Retreat from Rovno", "RETREAT FROM ROVNO (18 September 1920)<br><br>Comrade have I ever told you why I joined the Bolshevik party?  No, but you are right. There is no time for such tales.  I have noticed it, comrade.  Morale is low among the ranks.  The sudden change in the course of the war has left its traces.  This is a serious set back.  But it is merely a set back!<br><br>The Northern armies will have to retreat on their own to defensive positions while we prepare to strike again and then finally make the wishes of millions of proletarians come true!  In the south it has been quieter but it seems the imperialists in Warsaw have gathered enough men to continue the counteroffensive in the south as well.<br><br>There is no hope of stopping the monarchists now but we will not fall into enemy hands. We will retreat, reorganize and make the Polish capitalists pay for this!  The Revolution will not be tamed!  Make your way east, comrade, the town of Rovno has fallen into the dirty hands of the enemy!  Retreat!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampwr1.xml", "Kakhovka", "KAKHOVKA (20 October 1920)<br><br>That traitor Wrangel still operates like a wolf from the Crimea.  He stabbed the people's army in the back while we were occupied with the war against Poland.  Now that those reactionaries have seen that the Revolution in Russia cannot be stopped, we can muster all resources to bring peace to Russia!  Russia ruled by its people!<br><br>Wrangel has broken out of the Crimea some time ago and captured land north of the Perekop isthmus.  We can only be grateful for a foolish act like that.  His forces are now strung out and have few reserves.  The idiots aligning themselves with Wrangel's fate must now even face the Cavalry Army!<br><br>Comrade, cross the Dnjepr River near Kakhovka and quickly penetrate through the enemy lines.  Their force must not reach the Perekop isthmus before we do if we are to gain an easy victory!  The proletariat has suffered enough during the last years!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampwr2.xml", "Perekop", "PEREKOP (28 October 1920)<br><br>Quickly, comrade.  We have almost made it to the Perekop isthmus.  If those Tsarists are willing to make a stand against the glorious people of Russia then they will do it there!<br><br>While other armies are mopping up enemy criminals that have been encircled, all of the remaining people's army not occupied with that task is being directed to the Perekop isthmus. They will be placed under your command as soon as they arrive in the region, comrade! In Moscow they regard you as a military genius!  The Revolution is driving the proletariat to great acts!<br><br>Your horses are the most mobile force that we have, comrade.  Dash to the isthmus and force your way into the Crimea!!!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["ccampwr3.xml", "Sevastopol", "SEVASTOPOL (11 November 1920)<br><br>It all does not matter anymore, comrade.  Strategy?  We want victory!  The Tsarist monarchists know their fate.  Their dream of a Russia full of slaves they can control is gone!  The people have stood up against this injustice and united itself to drive out the capitalist oppressors!<br><br>There are clear signs that the capitalists from London will send the Royal Navy to Russia and attempt to evacuate Wrangel and his forces.  Comrade, this shows the lies told by the British and Wrangel.  How are they to evacuate a massive army?  Most likely they will only bring him and a few others to safety while the rest await the mercy of the glorious people's army!<br><br>Now, go forward and hunt down the criminals of the people of Russia before they can get away!", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100, "support": [151]}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["The November Revolution (1918)"],
["n_kiel.xml", "1918 Kieler Matrosenaufstand", "1918 - Sailors revolt<br><br>No one still wants war, but the government does not get it. It sends the German fleet into the final battle against the Royal Navy. Your comrades defend themselves. This means mutiny. The ships turned back. The mutineers, however, were captured ...<br>Your comrades need help. Karl Artelt and Lothar Popp, leader of the revolt and USPD members, stand by your side. Go in and win!! <br><br>Note: The Steinhäuser Patrol is on the way to knock down the revolt ...<br><br>Historical:<br>The fleet had been moved from Kiel to Wilhelmshaven to set from there sail to the last battle. Despite utmost secrecy the plans came through to the crews.<br>Thereupon the sailors on three ships of the Third Naval Battle Squadron refused to weigh anchor for the last naval battle of WW1.<br>Part of the crew of SMS Thüringen and SMS Helgoland, two battle ships of the First Naval Battle Squadron, committed outright mutiny and sabotage. However, when a day later some torpedo boats directed their cannons onto these ships, the mutineers gave up and were led away without any resistance.<br>The fleet again entered Kiel. 47 sailors were arrested and detained at the naval base 'Wilhelm Souchon'.<br>Some 250 sailors met in the evening of 1 November in the Union House in Kiel and prevented the fleet from setting sail again. <br>The Revolution started from here with the sailor Karl Artelt and shipyard worker Lothar Popp (both USPD) as ringleaders.<br>The next day, police closed the Union House. Several thousand sailors and workers moved to the \"Großer Exerzierplatz\" (large drill ground). Under the slogan: \"peace and bread\" they demanded the release of the mutineers.<br>On 4 November the governor of the naval base, Wilhelm Souchon, gave way and let the detained sailors free. However, foreign troops marched on to defeat the movement.<br>These were intercepted by the rebels, captured, or joined the uprising.<br>On the evening of 4 November's Kiel was firmly in the hands of about 40,000 rebellious sailors, soldiers and workers.", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["n_willhelmsh.xml", "1918 Willhelmshafen", "1918 Willhelmshafen<br><br>After Kiel, the naval base of Wilhelmshaven is now rebelling. Under the leadership of Bernhard Kuhnt, you are now the one representative for the Council of the 21, whom the revolution now badly needs<br>Conquer the north, Aurich, Emden and especially the reservists garrison Oldenburg!!!<br><br>Historically: <br><br>In Wilhelmshaven-Rüstringen was founded on 6th November 1918, after a mass demonstration of over 20,000 naval and shipyard workers and other civilians a workers and Soldiers Council, with its executive organ, the so-called Council or the 21.<br>To Chairman of the Council was appointed Bernhard Kuhnt. The \"21er\" Council <br>took over the power of the fortified towns,the North Sea Station,the encircling land of Oldenburg in Ostfriesland and all the surrounding islands, without resistance of the military station commands and declared on 10 November 1918 in front of 100,000 enthusiastic demonstrators in Wilhelmshaven,<br>the Socialist Republic of Oldenburg and the deposition of the Grand Duke of Oldenburg.<br>Under the impression of demonstrations and pressure from the large majority of Members of Parliament,Grand Duke Friedrich August of Oldenburg declared his abdication on 11 November 1918.<br>The Free State of Oldenburg was therefore declared in the territory of the Grand Duchy of Oldenburg.<br>As a provisional government was formed a Land-governing-body, to what, among others, the Rüstringer Member of Parliament Paul Hug and Kuhnt belonged.<br>Kuhnt became president of the new Free State of Oldenburg.<br>-------------------------------------<br><br>Autor = Matze (M. Kessler)", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["n_frankfurt.xml", "1918 Der Aufstand erfasst Frankfurt am Main", "1918 The revolt comes upon Frankfurt<br><br>7 November<br><br>The revolution is fomented. The coastal towns are in our hands. Now freed Frankfurt on Main and  conquer by this the city of Finance, or can Großherzog Ernst Ludwig of Hessen put down the rebellion?<br><br>Historical:<br>According to the Sailors' revolt in Kiel, the revolution spreads to Frankfurt<br><br>There they formed Workers' and Soldiers' Councils and called for the abdication of Grand Duke Ernst Ludwig of Hesse. But he refuses ...<br><br>Autor = Matze (M. Kessler)", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["n_berlin.xml", "1918 Ende der Monarchie", "1918 End of the Monarchy<br><br>When the Emperor heard of the revolts in Kiel, he orderd the 4th Jäger Regiment to Berlin. The city burns. The insurgents have the working-class neighborhoods under control.<br><br>Can Police and Jäger put down the rebellion? Or has the Kaiser to quit and leave Berlin?<br><br>there is little support announced for both sides ..<br><br>Historical :<br>In reality, everything went bloodless. After the revolt in Kiel, Wilhelmshaven and other towns the USPD planned in Berlin mass demonstrations and a general strike for the 9th November 1918 . This was heard by the competing SPD under leadership of its chairman, Friedrich Ebert.<br><br>In order to remain master of the situation, <br><br>To anticipate the USPD, Ebert forced Chancellor Max von Baden to announce the abdication of Wilhelm II. <br>The Kaiser was this time at Spa, where the allied armistice terms had been previously negotiated. He then fled to his Dutch exile where he signed the abdication on 28.11.1919.<br><br>Autor = Matze (M. Kessler)", [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["The Defeat of Denikin (1918-1920)"],
["volarm_00.xml", "The Ice March", "The Ice March<br><br>February 23rd, 1918<br><br>Rostov is ours as of this morning: empty barracks, a burning quartermaster's store, and a city that had hung out red cloth before our patrols were through the outskirts. The Volunteer Army walked out of it in the dark and took every pair of felt boots in the town with it.<br><br>Four years ago I was an officer of the Imperial Army, and a good many of the men I once messed with are in the column now crawling south across the frozen steppe. Alekseyev and Kornilov have taken everything that will march - their staffs, their cadets, their wounded, their families - and they have gone off the railway on purpose, into open country where our armoured trains cannot follow.<br><br>The Military Revolutionary Committee has not ordered me to chase them into the snow. Whatever that column becomes, it becomes it somewhere else. My orders are to close the Don behind it - the crossings and the stanitsas it is using - so that nothing of theirs can turn back on Rostov or reach Novocherkassk from the south.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Rostov (19,17), Aksaiskaya (26,16) and Ol'ginskaya (29,20).<br>- The Volunteer column wins instead if four of its formations reach Kraskynova (38,32).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_01.xml", "Tragedy at Ekaterinodar", "Tragedy at Ekaterinodar<br><br>April 9th, 1918<br><br>Kornilov has perhaps six thousand men. There are three times that in and around Ekaterinodar, and he is going to attack anyway, because our detachments hold every railway in the Kuban and the Rada's own ministers are sitting in our jails. He can attack or he can starve on the steppe.<br><br>He will not try the front of the city. Our scouts have found a crossing being prepared to the west, at Elizabetinskaya - a flanking march in the old style, with Cossack guides who know the fords. Which means the city has to be held on two faces at once, and the village of Takhtamukay across the river, where his column forms up, has to be taken away from him.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Ekaterinodar (17,7) and Elizabetinskaya (5,10).<br>- Take Takhtamukay (20,19).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_02.xml", "Belaya Glina", "Belaya Glina<br><br>June 28th, 1918<br><br>Denikin has come back into the Kuban, and this time his people are not refugees: nine thousand men, German rifles bought through Krasnov's Don government, and the whole of the Don behind him.<br><br>We are the Red Army of the North Caucasus and we are on our own. Moscow has the Germans on the Ukrainian line and the Czechoslovak revolt on the Volga; nothing is coming from the north. Five days ago they took Torgovaya and cut the railway to Tsaritsyn, and an army larger than theirs on paper is now an army with no telegraph, no supply and no orders except the ones we write ourselves.<br><br>My sector is the line itself. Belaya Glina, Novopokrovskaya and Peschanokopskoye are junctions: while we sit on them this army still has a spine. Their forward depot has halted north of us, and I intend to take it off them.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Belaya Glina (14,6), Novopokrovskaya (4,7) and Peschanokopskoye (21,7).<br>- Take their supply line at (24,1).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_03.xml", "The liberation of Ekaterinodar", "The battle for Ekaterinodar<br><br>August 13th, 1918<br><br>My dear Katya,<br><br>You will read in the papers that the Kuban is holding. It is holding here, in front of me, on a line I could walk before breakfast.<br><br>Tikhoretskaya has gone, Armavir is threatened, and Denikin has brought up everything he has for the capital of the Kuban. His army has grown - half the stanitsas have gone over to him - and I can tell you exactly how far ahead of him the news travels, because I have been reading the reports out of the districts he has already taken. The land goes back to the man who owned it in 1916. The ataman comes back with him. Then the punitive detachment comes to explain the arrangement to the village. Every one of those villages is recruiting for us now, and he has not worked out why.<br><br>My orders are the city and the western crossing, and to clear Plastunovskaya on the north road where his staff has installed itself. Anatoly is with the machine-gun company. He is twenty-two and he thinks that is very old.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Ekaterinodar (19,9), Ekaterinodar (20,13) and Elizabetinskaya (5,10).<br>- Take Plastunovskaya (25,1).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_04.xml", "Novorossiysk", "The Taman Army<br><br>August 23rd, 1918<br><br>The Taman Group is cut off from the rest of the army by two hundred versts of White cavalry, with the sea on one side and the mountains on the other. There are thirty thousand people on the Novorossiysk road with it and perhaps a third of them carry a rifle; the rest are the families of the ones who do, and they know precisely what the punitive detachments do in the coastal stanitsas, because that is why they are on the road.<br><br>Kovtyukh has exactly one route - the coast road east through Gelendzhik - and there are German warships off the port to make sure he does not use the harbour instead.<br><br>His order to me is four words long: get the columns out. Not the ground. Not the town. Not the guns, if it comes to that.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Bring eight of the ten marked Taman columns out through Gelendzhik (39,37).<br>- Or take the village at (41,3).<br>- You lose if not one marked column survives.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_05.xml", "Stavropol", "Stavropol<br><br>November 10th, 1918<br><br>Denikin has drawn a ring round this army from the east, the west and the north, and is pressing it back against the mountains. Stavropol has already changed hands twice, and both times the change was paid for in whole regiments.<br><br>We are the 11th Army now, on paper, which has improved nothing. Sorokin, who commanded it, shot four members of the regional Party committee in October and was shot himself a fortnight later. The typhus is taking more of us than the shelling.<br><br>We hold the town and the villages that cover the road out of it. Wrangel is coming from the west, Drozdovsky from the north, and two batteries are ranging on us from ground I can see from the church tower. Hold the town, hold the road, and take those two villages away.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Stavropol (12,10), Novomaryevskaya (4,6), Tatarka (12,12) and Nadezhda (18,13).<br>- Take Dubovka (21,0) and Temnolesskaya (18,24).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_06.xml", "Grozny", "Grozny<br><br>February 1st, 1919<br><br>The Terek is the last thing we hold south of the Don and it is being taken away from us a stanitsa at a time. Grozny itself held for a hundred days last year - oilfield workers, Chechen and Ingush volunteers, a scratch garrison and no reserves at all - and the wells have been burning ever since. You can see them from thirty versts out; by now everyone here navigates by them.<br><br>What has changed is not on this map. The Great War ended in November, the Germans are gone from Ukraine, and the Entente has begun unloading at Novorossiysk for Denikin: British rifles, British shells, British instructors. Wrangel is already at Vladikavkaz.<br><br>The 12th Army holds Grozny, Shali and Samashki, and behind them there is nothing but the mountain passes. Hold the three towns. Take Novoshchendrinskaya, which is where their cavalry waters.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Grozny (21,23), Shali (33,27) and Samashki (7,31).<br>- Take Novoshchendrinskaya (31,5).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_07.xml", "Operation Manych", "The Manych<br><br>May 1st, 1919<br><br>The 10th Army came down off the Tsaritsyn line in the winter, took Torgovaya and put itself across the Manych, and for a few weeks it looked as though the southern front might be split in two. It has not happened. Wrangel has brought his Caucasus corps up by rail with British armour on the flat cars, and this steppe is flat, dry and belongs to whoever has the most horses - which is not us.<br><br>So it comes down to the crossings, and for once we are standing on ground we chose ourselves. Velikoknyazheskaya, Uyutnyy and Ekaterinovka cover the fords. Torgovaya, which we took in the winter, has been taken back, and I want it again.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Velikoknyazheskaya (40,13), Uyutnyy (34,14) and Ekaterinovka (23,23).<br>- Take Torgovaya (21,37).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_08.xml", "Tsaritsyn", "Tsaritsyn<br><br>June 14th, 1919<br><br>The Cossacks have come at this town three times since last summer and gone back three times with nothing, which is why the newspapers have started calling it the Red Verdun. What held it was not a miracle: the workers' regiments out of the French Factory, the armoured trains, the gunboats on the Volga, and a position that was dug and wired properly before anybody needed it. All of that is still here.<br><br>What is different is Wrangel, and the tanks the British landed for him at Novorossiysk, and the fact that our own front north of here has been coming apart since the Veshenskaya rising.<br><br>Hold the city, its approaches and the river crossing. Their heavy batteries have come into position at Gorodistsje; clear them off it.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold the three Tsaritsyn sectors (22,13), (26,17), (14,21) and Wolzskij (37,10).<br>- Take Gorodistsje (4,12).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_09.xml", "Oboyan", "Oboyan<br><br>August 12th, 1919<br><br>Denikin signed his Moscow Directive last month in Tsaritsyn: three armies, three axes, one capital. May-Mayevsky's corps is coming up the Kharkov railway to deliver the middle of it, and Mamontov's cavalry is already somewhere behind us doing as it pleases in our rear areas - which is the part of the Directive that actually works.<br><br>The 13th Army has been ordered to hold the Oboyan-Pristen line long enough for the reserves forming at Orel and Tula to be worth something. That is a screen, and everyone from the army commander down has been careful to call it something else. There is no more to my task than that, and no less.<br><br>Break their forward group at Yakovlevo and buy the Republic three weeks.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Oboyan (22,7), Pristen (39,7), Trubezh (11,9) and the crossing at (9,1).<br>- Take Yakovlevo (26,27).<br><br>Intelligence: enemy cavalry has been reported in our rear areas. Expect to be raided.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_10.xml", "Peregonovka", "Peregonovka<br><br>September 26th, 1919<br><br>Makhno's people have been retreating west across half of Ukraine for a month with Slashchev's regiments driving them. This morning they stopped retreating: the whole Insurgent Army turned round in the dark near Peregonovka and went at the pursuit column head-on, and the tachanka squadrons are swinging wide to come in behind it.<br><br>I am attached to them as a liaison officer, which is a polite word for several things at once, and every one of them is somebody's problem for later. There is a great deal between us politically and there will be a reckoning over it.<br><br>Tonight none of that is the point. The group in front of us is Denikin's, it is sitting astride the railway to his rear at the exact moment his front line is reaching for Orel, and it can be destroyed. My formations remain the Red Army's, and so do I.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Peregonovka (20,13).<br>- Or destroy 22 enemy formations.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_11.xml", "Orel: White avalanche", "Orel: the avalanche<br><br>October 11th, 1919<br><br>Kutepov is coming up the Moscow highway with the Kornilov, Markov, Drozdovsky and Alekseyev regiments in his first line - four regiments of officers with nothing left to go home to, the best infantry the Whites have, and nobody has stopped them this summer. In front of them is the 13th Army, which has been retreating since August, and me.<br><br>We are not asked to stop them here. We are asked to hold Orel and the road towns long enough for the shock group forming behind Kromy - the Latvian Rifle Division, the Estonians, Primakov's Chervonny Cossacks - to come into line with its strength unspent. Eleven thousand bayonets that have not yet been in this battle, and every day this sector holds is a day they are still eleven thousand.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold four of the objectives for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take their forward depot at (41,27).<br>- The objectives are Orel (31,20), Mtsensk (33,9), Kromy (24,23) and Dmitrovsk (19,28).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_12.xml", "Orel: Red storm", "Orel: the storm<br><br>October 16th, 1919<br><br>Comrades of the shock group.<br><br>Five days ago their newspapers in Kharkov printed the distance from Orel to Moscow. They were right about the distance and wrong about everything else.<br><br>That corps has been marching and fighting for eleven weeks without a reserve, on a front that gets wider with every verst it advances. Makhno is across its supply line. Its regiments are officers, and officers cannot be replaced out of the villages it has just requisitioned - those villages are recruiting for us. It is a spear thrown a very long way by an arm that is now behind it.<br><br>You are the Latvian Rifle Division, the Estonian division and the Chervonny Cossacks, and you are going in on the flank at Kromy, where the corps is thinnest and where its line of retreat runs. Take Orel back. Take Kromy and Dmitrovsk. Do not let them straighten the front.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Orel (31,20), Kromy (24,23) and Dmitrovsk (19,28).<br>- Hold Mtsensk (33,9) and Karachev (19,13).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_13.xml", "Tula", "Tula<br><br>November 3rd, 1919<br><br>Tula makes the rifles. That sentence is the whole of the situation, and it is why I am here and not anywhere else.<br><br>Their advanced parties are at Plavsk, thirty versts down the road. Against them: the workers' regiments of the arms works, a fortified belt that the townspeople dug themselves through October, and six divisions brought in from the Voronezh and Tsaritsyn sectors - which the enemy has kindly made possible by concentrating everything against this one town and leaving his own left flank standing in the air.<br><br>Hold the belt. And if the chance offers, take Plavsk off them and their staging point with it.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold four of the objectives for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Plavsk (4,36).<br>- The objectives are Tula (13,13), Bronnokovo (28,12), Novomoskovsk (31,22) and Bogoroditsk (30,34).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_14.xml", "Moscow", "Moscow<br><br>December 12th, 1919<br><br>I did not expect to write this heading.<br><br>Their cavalry is in the outer suburbs. The Council of Defence has not left. The Kremlin garrison is in the line like everybody else, and the barricades on the southern approaches were thrown up by people who came out of the factories carrying their own tools.<br><br>We hold the three southern sectors and the centre. Volkhonka, on the Kaluga road, is where their staff and their heavy batteries have come up; take it and the whole attack loses its hinge. There is no line behind this one, which simplifies the orders considerably.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold four of the objectives for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Volkhonka (24,35).<br>- The objectives are the three Moscow sectors (18,14), (36,17), (12,19) and Red Square (24,20).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_15.xml", "Petrograd", "Petrograd<br><br>January 26th, 1920<br><br>I am detached from the Southern Front and placed under the 7th Army. My opponent is no longer Denikin but Yudenich - the North-Western Army, fed and armed out of Reval, with British tanks and British naval guns off Kronstadt, making one more winter push at the city while there is still enough of it left to push at.<br><br>Petrograd has been stripped for every other front for two years. What is here is the workers' regiments, the sailors, the courses cadets and whatever the districts can still put in the line. We hold the four city sectors and the airfield. Their road in - and their road out - runs through the Moscow highway junction.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold five of the objectives for a brilliant victory, four for a victory, three for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take the Moscow Road junction (34,33).<br>- The objectives are the four Petrograd sectors (16,12), (22,12), (14,15), (18,15) and the airfield (24,20).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_16.xml", "Kharkov", "Kharkov<br><br>December 4th, 1919<br><br>Since Orel this front has not stopped. Kursk went in the middle of November. Budyonny's cavalry is cutting the Donets railway in three places at once. The Volunteer Army that was going to be in Moscow by Christmas is trying to hold a line it does not have the men for, and it is finding out what its own rear is worth: the districts it requisitioned all summer are not sending it a single recruit. We are the ones advancing now, and it has taken some getting used to.<br><br>Kharkov is the hinge. Take the three city sectors and the whole Donbass position goes with them; leave it and their army has somewhere to reform. There is not much time - their rearguard is fighting for days, not for ground.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take the three Kharkov sectors (21,16), (14,18) and (15,21) - fast. Six turns for a brilliant victory, nine for a victory, twelve at the outside.<br>- Hold Lyubotyn (3,14) and the crossing at (24,8).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_17.xml", "Last days in Novorossiysk", "Novorossiysk<br><br>March 12th, 1920<br><br>The Kuban has gone. Rostov has gone. Ekaterinodar went last week. Everything left of them in the south is trying to get into the last port they hold on this coast, and the roads down to the harbour are one continuous column of transport.<br><br>In the roadstead there are British and French warships and nothing like enough transports. Their command has drawn up a list of who is taken off and who is not, and the men who are not have begun to work that out for themselves. Two years of Entente supply comes down to the tonnage in that bay this week.<br><br>Our task is the harbour and the loading. Take the port and the evacuation stops; break up the columns at the moles and it stops anyway. Six marked columns are what the whole affair now turns on.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take the Novorossiysk port (16,14).<br>- Or destroy 18 enemy formations.<br>- The enemy also loses if four of his six marked evacuation columns are destroyed.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["volarm_18.xml", "Perekop", "Perekop<br><br>November 7th, 1920<br><br>Wrangel has spent a summer turning the isthmus into a fortress: the Turkish Wall across the neck at Perekop, the Yushun positions behind it, eight belts of wire, concrete emplacements and every gun the French landed at Sevastopol. He has said publicly that it cannot be taken. Several of our own specialists have said the same thing rather more quietly.<br><br>So we are not going to take it the way he has built it to be taken. The front attacks frontally at Perekop and, on the same night, crosses the Sivash - which is shallow, freezing, and with this wind fordable. The 15th and 52nd divisions and the Latvian riflemen go across the mud in the dark; Blyukher's 51st goes at the Wall.<br><br>Take Armyansk and the wall positions, then Krasnoperekopsk and Zalivnaye behind them. Three years to the day since the Revolution, and the last of them is behind this wall.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Krasnoperekopsk (40,34) and Zalivnaye (27,36).<br>- Hold Armyansk (21,12) and the two flanking positions (28,7) and (4,18).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["Czech Legion - Siberian Anabasis (1917-1920)"],
["acampzbo.xml", "Zborov", "Zborov<br><br>July 2nd, 1917<br><br>I am a staff captain of the old army, seconded to the Czechoslovak brigade because I speak enough Czech to be useful and because nobody senior wanted the posting. Four months ago there was a Tsar. There is now a Provisional Government, a Petrograd Soviet, a committee in every regiment, and an offensive ordered by a minister who has never commanded anything.<br><br>Half the divisions on this front will not attack. They have voted on it. The men are not cowards - they have been in the line for three years and they have worked out that the government asking them for one more push is the same government that will not give them the land. The brigade beside me is different: seven thousand men who were Austrian subjects until they crossed over, fighting for a country that does not exist yet, and for whom capture means a rope.<br><br>Opposite us is the 19th Division of the same empire, and it is itself half Czech. There will be men in those trenches this morning who grew up in the same streets as the men going into them.<br><br>The brigade's task is Pluhiv, behind the Austrian third line.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Pluhiv (14,8).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 143}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampkie.xml", "Kiev", "Kiev<br><br>February 28th, 1918<br><br>The old army has dissolved. I mean that literally: there is no army, there are trains full of men going home. In October the Soviets took power, in December there was an armistice, and at Brest-Litovsk the German delegation has been raising its price every week because it can see there is nothing left to stop it with.<br><br>So the Germans are marching. Eleven divisions into the Ukraine, invited by a Rada that signed its own peace, and they are covering forty versts a day because nobody is in front of them. Kiev falls this week.<br><br>What is in Kiev is everything the Soviet power in the Ukraine still owns - the arsenal workers' detachments, the Red Guard, the archives, the treasury of the Kharkov government and eleven thousand people who will be shot or hanged if they are here when the Germans arrive. What is holding the Dnieper bridges to let them out is my detachment and the Legion's 2nd Regiment, who are trying to get east themselves and have agreed that for the moment we are going the same way.<br><br>I took the Soviet oath in December. The legionnaires took nothing - they are neutral in Russian affairs, on the orders of a National Council in Paris - but a neutral holding a bridge under German artillery is doing the same work as I am, and we shall argue about it afterwards.<br><br>Five days. Hold the bridges to the last turn.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold the Dnieper bridges at (21,11), (23,15) and (24,16) at the last turn - three for a brilliant victory or a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Shpitka (1,16).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampbac.xml", "Bachmach", "Bachmach<br><br>March 13th, 1918<br><br>The treaty was signed on the third and it is the worst peace any Russian government has ever put its name to: Poland, the Baltic, Finland, the Ukraine, a third of the population, half the industry. Lenin's argument for signing it was that a government with no army cannot bargain and that a breathing space is worth more than a gesture. Standing at Bachmach I find the argument hard to refute and harder to swallow.<br><br>The Germans are still advancing to the new border and the new border is east of here. Between Kiev and Kursk there is one railway junction that matters, and it is this one. Through it must pass sixty thousand legionnaires in echelon after echelon, our own withdrawing detachments, and every train of grain and rolling stock that can be got out of the Ukraine before the line is cut.<br><br>The Legion's command and ours have made a local agreement, in writing, with a Soviet signature and a Czechoslovak one: they cover the junction, we cover the crossing, and neither side interferes with the other's trains. It is the last agreement of its kind we shall make.<br><br>Hold Konotop and Bachmach until the echelons are through.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Konotop (30,26) and Bachmach (19,28) at the last turn - both for a brilliant victory or a victory, one for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take the Ezuch River crossing (42,27) and the Bachmach railroad (18,28).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 117}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acamptsj.xml", "Chelyabinsk", "Chelyabinsk<br><br>May 14th, 1918<br><br>It began with a stove leg thrown from a train.<br><br>There are two sets of echelons on this station. Ours going east are legionnaires; ours going west are Hungarian and Austrian prisoners of war being repatriated under the treaty - ordinary conscripts going home, not the volunteers who joined our formations and call themselves internationalists, and it matters that the two are not confused. Between the two sets of trains there is four years of a war they were all in, on opposite sides, and this morning something was thrown from a Hungarian carriage and a Czech soldier is dead of it.<br><br>The Soviet arrested the men who lynched the thrower, which was correct. The Legion surrounded the town, took the arsenal and freed them by force, which was not. And in Moscow, hearing that armed foreign troops have seized a Russian town, Trotsky has wired an order to disarm the Legion completely and shoot anyone found with a rifle - which any corps strung out over six thousand versts in a country in civil war will read as a sentence of death, and refuse.<br><br>Both sides have now done the thing that makes the other's fear reasonable. From today the Legion is in arms against the Soviets, the Committee at Samara will have an army by June, and half of Siberia will be gone by August.<br><br>I am on the Soviet side of it. I have friends in those echelons. The task is the town: the prison where their people and now some of ours are held, and the station hexes east of it that the district's grain trains and the workers' detachments have to come out through.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold the prison (19,3) and the stations at (31,9), (25,11) and (30,14) at the last turn - four for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take the town station (14,5).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampsam.xml", "Samara", "Samara<br><br>May 26th, 1918<br><br>The Committee of Members of the Constituent Assembly has declared itself the government of Russia in a building whose garrison it has not yet taken. It has five deputies, a printing press and no soldiers of its own; what it has is the Legion's echelons on the Samara-Zlatoust line and an understanding with them.<br><br>This is the shape of the whole summer. The men who will actually take these towns are foreign troops who say they only want to go home, and the government they install behind them is a committee of Socialist-Revolutionary deputies who will be swept away by Kolchak's officers in November - because an assembly with no army is a tenant of whoever does have one.<br><br>The city has a Soviet, a workers' militia, a bridge over the Volga and one line of approach from the east. My detachment is what there is. The task is to hold the city and the station long enough to get the Party organisation, the treasury and the arms out over the bridge - and if their echelons can be cut behind Kansk, they walk instead of ride.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold the Samara stations at (9,9) and (6,10), Samara itself (7,10) and Kansk (19,9) at the last turn - four for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take the eastern railway at (36,7) and (30,8).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampkaz.xml", "Kazan", "Kazan<br><br>August 7th, 1918<br><br>Six hundred million roubles of the Imperial gold reserve are in the vaults under this city. They were sent here for safety in 1915 and they are still here because the order to move them was given too late and executed by men who had never moved six hundred tons of anything.<br><br>That is why the attack is here and not somewhere that makes military sense. Kappel has perhaps three thousand men, a Serbian battalion and two gunboats; we have the Fifth Army, which is nine days old, has a staff that has never worked together, and includes one Latvian regiment whose commander will go over to them tomorrow and take his men with him.<br><br>I am not going to promise anyone that the gold stays. Most of it will not: what can be loaded in the time will be loaded and the rest will go east on their trains and pay for their war. What can be saved is the army and the crossings, and an army that still exists in August can come back for the city in September.<br><br>Hold the Kremlin, the city and the Volga crossing to the last turn.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Kazan (25,2) and (27,2) and the Volga crossing (24,4) at the last turn - three for a brilliant victory, two for a victory, one for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take the railway at (6,27).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampoms.xml", "Omsk", "Omsk<br><br>December 22nd, 1918<br><br>There is no Committee any more. On the eighteenth of November the officers arrested the Directory in its beds, and Admiral Kolchak - a naval officer who has never commanded on land and does not much like the men who made him - is Supreme Ruler of Russia, in Omsk, with British advisers, Japanese money and a war ministry made of the same people who ran the old one.<br><br>Tonight the city rises against him. Railway workshops at Kulomzino across the Irtysh, the garrison's Second Regiment, the Bolshevik underground and about two hundred political prisoners in the town gaol who will be let out by the risers or shot in the yard, depending on the hour.<br><br>I am here because the Fifth Army sent me here, and I have no illusions about the odds. The rising is a few thousand men with three hundred rifles against a garrison, an officers' detachment and Cossack cavalry, and the Legion's echelons sit on the railway in between deciding whose side neutrality is on this week. It will be put down. Almost five hundred people will be shot for it, many of them after surrendering under an amnesty that Kolchak's officers will simply ignore, and the men who do the shooting will spend the next year teaching every village in Siberia to hate the government they serve.<br><br>What can be done is to hold the two workers' quarters long enough for the people who can still get out to get out - to the taiga, to the partisan detachments, to us.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold the workers' quarters at (15,14) and (17,19) at the last turn - both for a brilliant victory or a victory, one for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take the city at (9,13), (16,17), (20,18) and (16,23).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampsem.xml", "Semenov", "Semenov<br><br>February 10th, 1920<br><br>Kolchak was shot at Irkutsk three days ago, by sentence of a revolutionary committee, after the Legion handed him over along with the gold in exchange for a clear line east. That is the end of the Supreme Ruler and very nearly the end of the whole business.<br><br>What is left is Transbaikalia, which was never really his. Ataman Semenov has ruled the line from Chita eastward for two years with Japanese money, Japanese rifles and armoured trains, and has run it the way he ran everything: station by station, with a firing party. There are villages along this railway where the male population is a number in his own reports.<br><br>Which is why the partisan detachments here are not a Party creation. They are the villages themselves, with their own commanders, their own quarrels and about four rifles per ten men, and they have been fighting him without us since 1918. We are coming up the line to join them, not to command them.<br><br>Chita is the knot. Take it and the Transbaikal is open to the Pacific.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Chita (36,9).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 191}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampwla.xml", "Vladivostok", "Vladivostok<br><br>March 10th, 1920<br><br>The end of the line. Nine thousand versts of railway from Bachmach, three years, and a city at the end of it that belongs to nobody in particular.<br><br>In January the partisans and the Zemstvo took Vladivostok from Kolchak's people without much of a fight. What they did not take, and cannot, is the garrison: Japanese divisions in the port and along the railway, American troops embarking, and the last of the Legion waiting on the quay for the ships that will finally take them home. Tokyo has not decided yet whether to go or to stay, and in three weeks it will decide to stay and will shoot up the town to make the point.<br><br>I am not here to take a city. Nobody is taking this city in March 1920 and anyone who tells you otherwise is writing fiction. I am here to bring the couriers and the underground's people through the occupation zones to the contact point on the city road, where the Far Eastern organisation is waiting for them.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Reach the contact point on the road into the city (12,25).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 152}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampka2.xml", "Kazan: the Red offensive", "Kazan: the Red offensive<br><br>September 10th, 1918<br><br>One month. In one month the Fifth Army has been rebuilt from the outside in - commissars, tribunals, a supply service, forty-eight guns, the Volga flotilla brought up from Nizhny, and reinforcements that arrived as detachments and are leaving as regiments.<br><br>Opposite us the People's Army is coming apart at the seams. The Committee's conscripts are deserting in companies; the Legion has decided it is going home after all and would rather not die on the Volga first; and Kappel's three thousand cannot hold a city of two hundred thousand that does not want them.<br><br>This is the first attack this army has made. Everything before it was holding on. Today we go back over the river for the bridge, the city and the eastern railway, and after Kazan there is Simbirsk on the twelfth and Samara in October and the whole Volga.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take the Romanov Bridge (13,2), Kazan (27,2) and the eastern railway (36,2).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["acampufa.xml", "Ufa", "Ufa<br><br>June 9th, 1919<br><br>Ufa was taken this morning. The Fifth Army crossed the Belaya on rafts in the dark, under shrapnel, with Chapayev's division leading, and the Siberian Army that was outside Kazan in April is now going back over the Urals with our cavalry in its transport.<br><br>Kolchak's spring offensive lasted ten weeks and collapsed for reasons that had nothing to do with the fighting. He mobilised the Siberian villages and they deserted; he restored the landlords behind his own front and the villages rose; he let his atamans hang people along the railway and the railway stopped working. An army supplied through one port by two foreign governments is exactly as reliable as their politics, and the politics changed in April.<br><br>My task is the railway east of the city. Their rearguards and what is left of the Legion's echelons are holding the junctions to get the trains out; take the junctions and the trains stay.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take the junctions at (7,18), Alatorka (22,18) and Iglino (38,21).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 144}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["The Polish-Soviet War: The Red Advance (1919-1920)"],
["polsov_01.xml", "Approach to Wilno", "Approach to Wilno<br><br>April 15th, 1919<br><br>There is no front here in the sense the staff manuals mean. There is a railway, there are four towns on it, and between them there is nobody at all - the divisions that should be holding this ground are in the Ukraine and on the Don, because that is where the war is being decided. What Lithuania and Byelorussia have is a screen: my detachment, a half-strength brigade of the Western Division, and a great deal of empty country.<br><br>Pilsudski is coming for Wilno with cavalry moving off the roads and infantry following on the rails. He is not trying to break us; he is trying to get behind us, and against a screen that works. Moscow's instruction is plain and I will not pretend it is generous: the Wilno group is not to be encircled, and the road south is to stay open until the Soviet institutions and the rolling stock are out of the city.<br><br>So this is a delaying action, and it is scored as one. Hold the towns on the withdrawal road until the clock runs out. If their forward assembly area is thinner than it looks, take it and the whole advance loses a week.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Olita (9,18), Orany (16,20) and Lida (23,27) at the last turn - three for a brilliant victory, two for a victory, one for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take their assembly area at (15,27).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_02.xml", "Assault on Wilno", "Assault on Wilno<br><br>April 18th, 1919<br><br>They came into the city at first light along the railway - an armoured train and a cavalry group that rode through the gap between us and Lida in the dark, dismounted at the station and were in the streets before the garrison knew the line was cut.<br><br>The city is going. That was decided at Olita three days ago and nothing I do here changes it. What is not decided is what happens to the twelve thousand men and the four hospital trains north and east of it, and to the Soviet of the city, whose people are being hunted through the Jewish quarter as I write this. The order from the Western Front is to hold the northern and eastern roads open until they are through.<br><br>Malaty and Swieciany are the northern gate; the city hexes are the eastern one. Hold them to the last turn. Lida behind them is their forward supply head, and if it can be taken the pursuit stops for a fortnight.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Malaty (24,3), Swieciany (41,6) and Wilno (24,11) at the last turn - three for a brilliant victory, two for a victory, one for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Lida (23,27).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_03.xml", "Minsk and the Berezina", "Minsk and the Berezina<br><br>August 4th, 1919<br><br>The summer has been a lesson in arithmetic. Denikin is at Kharkov and Kolchak has only just been pushed off the Urals, and everything the Republic owns that can march is committed to one or the other. The Western Front has sixteen thousand bayonets on a line four hundred versts long, and orders that begin with the word nevertheless.<br><br>Pilsudski is about to take Minsk. Two of his divisions are already past Molodeczno and the Lithuanian-Byelorussian division is coming up the Nieman. He is doing it now, and not in September, because Denikin has told Paris that a Polish state is a temporary administrative inconvenience and will not be recognised by a restored Russia - so Warsaw has a short season in which our defeat is not yet their defeat, and they know it.<br><br>The city cannot be held with what I have. The Berezina line behind it can. My task is the railway junctions and the crossings that let the 16th Army get onto that line as an army and not as a crowd, and to keep Minsk itself until the last echelon has cleared it.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Minsk (41,5), Stolpce (30,12) and the crossings at (39,2) and (40,20) at the last turn - four for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Lida (20,3), Grodno (2,4) and Baranowicze (22,19).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_04.xml", "Dyneburg: the Latgale winter", "Dyneburg: the Latgale winter<br><br>January 3rd, 1920<br><br>Minus twenty-five degrees, snow to the waist off the roads, and not a machine on either side that will start without a fire under it. The 15th Army holds Dyneburg with fortified positions, minefields and men who have been in them since November.<br><br>The attack is a Polish one with the Latvian army coming up from the north-west, and its purpose is political before it is military: to put Latgale into Riga's hands and cut the wire between us and Kaunas. Smigly-Rydz has the 1st and 3rd Legion divisions and the weather with him, because we are the ones who must sit still in it.<br><br>The town will be given up if it must be. What may not be given up is the corps, and what must be kept to the hour is the crossing and the two positions covering it, so that the guns and the field hospitals go out on the ice road instead of being left in the snow. Their own aerodrome and railhead lie behind the attack, and a raid on them would end the operation before it starts.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Laci (31,9), Cietoksnis (15,13), Gajoks Castle (24,20) and Dyneburg (20,26) at the last turn - four for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Tilti Aerodrome (5,1), Rubeniski (20,1) and the Dyneburg-Wilno railway (19,35).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_05.xml", "Zhitomir: the Polish blow", "Zhitomir: the Polish blow<br><br>April 25th, 1920<br><br>It has begun, and it has begun where the front was thinnest. Three Polish armies and Petliura's two divisions came through the 12th and 14th Armies this morning on a hundred-verst frontage, and the 12th Army is not so much retreating as coming apart into detachments.<br><br>The purpose is not Kiev. The purpose is a Ukrainian state under Petliura that will hold the Dnieper for Warsaw, and the price agreed for it in Warsaw last week was eastern Galicia and western Volhynia - which is to say Petliura sold four million Ukrainians to buy an army, and the villages here know it. That is the whole weakness of the enterprise, and in six weeks it will be the whole reason it fails.<br><br>For now they have the initiative, the railways and the better cavalry. I am to slow them on the Korosten-Zhitomir-Kazatin triangle so that the 12th and 14th can be got behind the Dnieper and the reserves coming from the Caucasus can be unloaded east of it. Six towns. Hold as many as I can to the last turn.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Korosten (23,2), Malin (34,8), Radomysl (34,13), Zhitomir (20,19), Fastov (42,26) and Kazatin (24,33) at the last turn - five for a brilliant victory, four for a victory, three for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take their forward positions at (3,6) and Polonne (2,21).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_06.xml", "The Dnieper crossings", "The Dnieper crossings<br><br>May 5th, 1920<br><br>The order is to give up Kiev without fighting for it, and I have read it three times.<br><br>It is the right order. The city is a salient with one river at its back and their cavalry already north of it at Chernobyl; a garrison left in it would be a garrison lost, and the 12th Army is worth more to the Republic than the honour of the streets. So the army goes over to the eastern bank and the bridgeheads are held open behind it until the last battery is across.<br><br>My detachment is the rearguard. We have the demolition parties, the mined roads, the wire and the blockhouses, and almost nothing that moves - the cavalry went east three days ago. Their advance guard is racing us for the crossings and the Ukrainian division is coming up on the southern road to be first into the city for the politics of it.<br><br>Hold the crossings until the clock runs out. If their leading squadrons over-run themselves, the crossing they are riding for can be taken from them instead.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold the crossings at (22,12) and (29,13) at the last turn - both for a brilliant victory, one for a victory or a tactical victory.<br>- Or take their crossing at (24,16).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_07.xml", "The Red tide", "The Red tide<br><br>June 4th, 1920<br><br>The Konarmia is up. Fourteen thousand sabres that walked from the Kuban to the Dnieper in fifty-three days, and tomorrow morning they go into the seam between their 3rd and 6th Armies at Samhorodok.<br><br>The whole Polish position rests on a front too long for the troops holding it, supplied through a rail net we tore up in May, in a country where the requisition parties have already turned the villages against them. Break the crust anywhere and there is nothing behind it but staffs and depots. That is the theory. It is also, this once, the fact.<br><br>My task is the railway line behind the breach. Not their field army - it will not stand to be fought - but the junctions and stations it must have to withdraw in order: Zhitomir and Berdichev first, then Korosten, Fastov and Kazatin. Take them all and their two armies have to come out across country on their feet.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Korosten (23,2), Malin (34,8), Zwiahel (4,10), Zhitomir (20,18), Fastov (41,25), Kazatin (24,33) and the junction at (40,7).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_08.xml", "Before Warsaw: the Wkra", "Before Warsaw: the Wkra<br><br>August 13th, 1920<br><br>Read the orders in the order they were written and you can see the disaster coming.<br><br>The 4th Army and Gai's cavalry corps are to swing north-west around Warsaw. The 1st Cavalry Army is to go for Lvov, four hundred versts away, and has been told twice to come north and has not come. Between the two halves of our own front there is a gap of a hundred and fifty versts held by nothing, our men have marched six hundred versts from their railheads on what they could take from the villages, and the Polish workers who were supposed to rise have instead volunteered by the hundred thousand, because an army coming over the Vistula does not look like a revolution from underneath - it looks like Russia.<br><br>I am on the Wkra with the 15th Army's left. Sikorski's 5th Army is attacking into our flank from Modlin and there is a counterstroke forming south of the city that will be behind us by the sixteenth. My task is not the capital. My task is that this army group does not end up in the bag: hold the northern towns while the trains and the wounded go east, and get the divisional cores out through the crossings behind us.<br><br>Four of the designated formations out through the eastern exits and three of them still alive - only the designated formations may use an exit. Take Modlin and Legionowo instead if their line north of the city can be broken.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Bring 4 of the designated formations off the map at (43,18), (43,24), (43,26) or (43,28), keeping at least 3 of them alive.<br>- Or hold Ciechanow (15,2), Szczytno (3,4), Plonsk (5,10), Siennica (21,10), Rozan (39,10), Pultusk (27,13), Nasielsk (16,18) and Radzymin (31,23) at the last turn - six for a brilliant victory, five for a victory, four for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Szczypiorno (6,22), Stary Modlin (11,25) and Legionowo (19,27).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_09.xml", "Komarow: the Konarmia breaks out", "Komarow: the Konarmia breaks out<br><br>August 31st, 1920<br><br>The Konarmia was ordered north on the eleventh, argued for four days, and turned north on the twentieth with Warsaw already lost. It has spent the last week riding into a pocket that closed behind it, and this morning the Polish 1st Cavalry Division is astride the eastern road at Komarow with the 13th Infantry coming up behind it.<br><br>So the last great cavalry battle of this war is being fought over a road junction, because everything else has already been decided. Twelve regiments of ours against six of theirs, in fog, on ploughed fields, at the sabre - and the arithmetic does not help us, because they are between us and the east and we have to go through them and they only have to stand.<br><br>Budyonny's order is to break out to the east and keep the army. Mine is the same, written smaller: hold the northern road while the transport and the wounded clear it, and take the designated divisions out through the eastern edge. Only those formations may use an exit. If Komarow itself can be taken the road opens for everybody.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Bring 4 of the designated formations off the map at (27,12), (27,17) or (27,22), keeping at least 3 of them alive.<br>- Or hold Miaczyn (12,6), Niewirkow (24,6) and Wolica Brzozowa (5,10) at the last turn - three for a brilliant victory, two for a victory, one for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Wolica Sniatycka (13,12) and Komarow (11,19).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_10.xml", "The Niemen", "The Niemen<br><br>September 20th, 1920<br><br>Six weeks ago this army was at the gates of Warsaw. It is now digging on the Niemen with eight thousand rifles where it had thirty, and the peace conference has already opened at Riga.<br><br>That last fact is the whole shape of this battle. Both governments know the line where the war stops will be roughly the line the armies stand on when it stops, so every verst held into October is a verst at the table, and Warsaw is attacking now precisely because the Entente is about to impose an armistice on them.<br><br>They are coming at Grodno frontally and sending a group north through Lithuanian territory - a neutral country whose border they have decided not to notice - to come out at Lida behind us. My task is the line itself: the crossings, the two railway towns and the junctions south of them, held to the last turn. If their northern group can be cut off against the Augustow canal, better still.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Orany (27,6), Werenow (40,8), Druskieniki (17,12), Lida (40,15), Wasiliszki (32,18), Grodno (15,20), Mosty (27,26) and Wolkowysk (26,35) at the last turn - six for a brilliant victory, five for a victory, four for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Augustow (1,17), Brzostowica Wielka (19,33), Bialystok (4,35) and the crossing at (8,24).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["polsov_11.xml", "Back to Minsk", "Back to Minsk<br><br>October 9th, 1920<br><br>The preliminary peace was signed at Riga three days ago and the guns stop on the eighteenth. Nine days.<br><br>This morning General Zeligowski's division mutinied, on orders nobody in Warsaw will ever put in writing, and took Wilno from the Lithuanians as a private enterprise. That is the kind of week this is. On our sector both sides are doing the same arithmetic: whatever is held on the eighteenth is what the commission will draw a line around next spring.<br><br>So we go forward one last time, not for Minsk - the city is already behind our line - but for the road and rail junctions west of it that the frontier commission will otherwise hand across. Hold what we have and take what we can reach in nine days. Then it is over, and this front becomes a border.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Molodeczno (13,2), Radoszkowicze (26,10), Zaslaw (27,18) and Kojdanow (23,35) at the last turn - four for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- Or take Wolozyn (2,14) and the junction at (0,27).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["Ejercito Popular (1936-1939)"],
["gce1.xml", "Batalla por Madrid", "Batalla por Madrid<br><br>13 de Noviembre de 1936<br><br>Bien comandante, le pondre al corriente de la situacion presente; 4 meses despues del golpe de Julio la situacion es caotica, algunos sectores de la Peninsula y la totalidad del protectorado de Marruecos se han unido a la sublevacion. Columnas rebeldes provenientes del Norte y el Sur han alcanzado Madrid. Mientras que las columnas del general Mola se han visto detenidas en las sierras del Norte de la capital, el ejercito de Africa al mando del general Franco ha alcanzado los barrios del Sur y del Oeste de la ciudad y constituye una gravisima amenaza, no deben cruzar el rio Manzanares!. Ademas se teme que elementos quintacolumnistas aparezcan dentro de la ciudad segun se vayan acercando las columnas rebeldes.<br><br>El gobierno de la Republica ha dado la orden de la formacion de un ejercito popular del que comienzan a formarse las primeras brigadas mixtas. Ademas, contamos con la valerosa aportacion de los voluntarios extranjeros, que hemos agrupado en algunas ''Brigadas Internacionales''. Su mision consistira en dirigir esas unidades de nueva creacion y algunas milicias para defender Madrid. Si Madrid cae, de por sentado que habremos perdido la guerra.<br>Recuerde el lema de Madrid; No pasaran!.<br><br>Batalla por Madrid<br><br>November 13th, 1936<br><br>Well commander, please listen to me, I will explain you the present situation. 4 months after the coup de'etat of July the situation is chaotic, some peninsular areas and the whole of Spanish Morocco are supporting the uprising. Rebel columns coming from the North, and from the South have reached Madrid. While the columns from the North under the command of the General Mola have been stopped in the mountains north of Madrid, the African Army under the command of the General Franco is now approaching the South and West neighborhoods of Madrid. They are a dangerous menace, and they must not cross the Manzanares river! Also, probably ''5th column'' elements will appear with the rebel approach to Madrid.<br><br>The Republican government has finally given the order to form a People's Army, some Mixed Brigades (Brigadas Mixtas, ''BM'') are now ready, and also other International Brigades (consisting mainly of foreign anti-fascist volunteers) should be ready for the battle!<br><br>Your mission is to defend Madrid at any cost, if Madrid falls, the whole Spain will fall! Remember the Madrid people's slogan; No pasaran! (\"They shall not pass!\").", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [203, 205, 206, 210]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce2.xml", "Valle del Jarama", "Jarama Valley<br><br>16 de Febrero de 1937<br><br>La marcha rebelde sobre Madrid esta completamente detenida por el momento. En las ultimas semanas los movimientos fascistas delatan que los planes del enemigo han cambiado y ahora en lugar del asalto directo a la capital se han decantado por rodearla, primero atacando nuestro sector Sur-Este en el rio Jarama para despues enlazar con las columnas que estan mas al norte.<br>Por tanto, evite que el enemigo cruce el rio Jarama a cualquier precio!!!. Tampoco se olvide que el importante punto estrategico del Cerro de los Angeles no debe caer en manos rebeldes<br><br>Se han tomado un par decisiones para tratar de poner orden en el caos reinante organizando unas cuantas divisiones provisionales para el Ejercito Popular, ademas esperamos que las recientes llegadas de armamento sovietico nos sean de ayuda para acometer esta tarea.<br><br>Buena suerte.<br><br>Valle del Jarama<br><br>February 16th, 1937<br><br>The rebel march on Madrid is completely stopped for the moment. In the past weeks, the movements of the fascist have shown us that the enemy's plans have changed. Now they will try to encircle the capital, cutting our communications with Valencia (new seat of the Republican goverment). The High Command thinks that stopping the rebel plans is possible, and the best sector to do it is the Jarama river area (SE of Madrid). Provisional divisions have been formed for this duty.<br><br>Your mission is to stop the rebels here, by counterattacking, and keeping open communications with Madrid.<br><br>Buena suerte.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce3.xml", "Batalla de Guadalajara", "Guadalajara<br><br>8 de Marzo de 1937<br><br>A primeras horas nuestros asesores sovieticos (Rodimtsev y Goriev) nos han informado de una gran concentracion de tropas en la linea Brihuega-Torija, y que se oyen a lo lejos raras canciones italianas, lo que hace indicar que el nucleo de esas tropas es el CTV italiano que capturo Malaga en fechas pasadas.<br><br>Tras el exito en el valle del Jarama nuestro objetivo ahora es asestar un duro golpe al enemigo, que tiene una confianza excesiva en sus propios medios, y hacer dudar a los rebeldes de la valia de la cooperacion que reciben de los italianos. <br><br>Una gran victoria aqui podra poner punto y final a las aspiraciones rebeldes sobre Madrid, al menos por el momento.<br><br>Guadalajara<br><br>March 8th, 1937<br><br>Early this morning, our Soviet advisors (Rodimtsev and Goriev) informed us of a large concentration of troops spotted along the Brihuega-Torija line. Our advanced recon units have heard strange Italian songs. There is no doubt the Italian CTV which captured Malaga the past days is on the way to strike again, here in Guadalajara.<br><br>After your success in the Jarama Valley, our aim now, is to accomplish a grand victory over the overconfident Italian troops.<br><br>A decisive victory here will be the end of the rebel's menacing threat to Madrid, at least for the moment.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce4.xml", "Ofensiva de Brunete", "Ofensiva de Brunete<br><br>6 de Julio de 1937<br><br>Tras las primeras pruebas de fuego mas o menos victoriosas para el Ejercito Popular, sumado eso a los ultimos envios de armas que han llegado desde la URSS, se puede decir que estamos en posicion de lanzar nuestra primera gran ofensiva de la guerra.<br>El plan consiste en un ataque desde el Norte y el Este en el sector de Brunete para embolsar a las fuerzas rebeldes aqui presentes. La mayor parte del V y el XVIII cuerpos atacaran desde el Norte en direccion a Brunete y Villafranca del Castillo, mientras que desde Madrid llegara el II cuerpo por el Este en direccion a Villaviciosa de Odon. Tambien llegara la 14 Division posteriormente como refuerzo, ademas de una buena cantidad de aparatos de las FARE.<br><br>Los motivos de esta ofensiva son varios, por un lado el objetivo principal es embolsar al enemigo, pero tambien alejar a los fascistas definitivamente de Madrid y conseguir que estos retiren parte de sus tropas del frente Norte, para asi aliviar la presion ejercida sobre el mismo. Desde algunas instancias tambien se espera que esta ofensiva de lugar al final de la guerra, pero entre nosotros, creo que eso es algo complicado.<br><br>Espero que a pesar del aplastante calor reinante, sus acciones alcancen los resultados previstos. <br><br>Ofensiva de Brunete<br><br>July 6th, 1937<br><br>After your first successful actions with the People's Army, and with our new Soviet equipment, received in the past few days, we are in a good position to launch our first big offensive of the war.<br><br>The plan consists of an attack from the North and the East on the Brunete sector, to surround the rebel forces there. The main part of the V and the XVIII Army Corps will attack from the North southwards to Brunete and Villafranca del Castillo, while the II Army Corp arrives from Madrid, taking the Villaviciosa de Odon. Also, the 14th Division will arrive as reinforcements, as well as a good number of FARE aircraft.<br><br>The High Command wants to encircle the rebel troops, create a pocket, and then destroy it. This will allow us to push the rebel lines far away from Madrid. A success here would make the rebels withdraw troops from the Austrian Front in the North, which is under horrible pressure.<br><br>Some people also believe that a major success for us here would finish the war... but personally I don't think so.<br><br>I hope that in spite of the African heat we are suffering this Summer, the People's Army will be able to achieve all the scheduled goals.<br><br>Buena Suerte.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce5.xml", "Ofensiva de Aragon", "Ofensiva de Aragon<br><br>24 de Agosto de 1937<br><br>Bienvenido al frente de Aragon, general. Los objetivos alcanzados en el sector de Brunete no correspondieron finalmente con nuestras aspiraciones, pero la ofensiva franquista sobre el Frente Norte se ha visto afectada.<br>Para tratar de nuevo de frenar completamente la tremenda presion que los rebeldes ejercen sobre Asturias y Cantabria, el alto mando ha creado esta nueva operacion sobre Aragon, consistente en un ataque concentrico que caera finalmente sobre Zaragoza. En su camino hacia la capital aragonesa encontrara multitud de guarniciones falangistas bien atrincheradas que trataran de resistir hasta la llegada de refuerzos, asi que actue con rapidez. Contara tambien con la ayuda de un grupo de guerrilleros cuya mision es capturar los puentes de Zaragoza...<br>Tenemos mas equipo que en Brunete, asi que se esperan amplios resultados de esta operacion.<br><br>---Historicamente la operacion fue un fracaso, ya que las divisiones republicanas se vieron detenidas por las guarniciones fuertemente atrincheradas, y posteriormente la ofensiva acabaria conociendose como batalla de Belchite.<br><br>Ofensiva de Aragon<br><br>August 24th, 1937<br><br>Welcome to the Aragon front, general. The operation of Brunete did not achieve everything that we wanted. However, the enemy has withdrawn some troops from the Northern Front. In order to try again to stop the rebel offensive in Asturias and Cantabria, the High Command has planned a new operation, here in Aragon. Its purposes are twofold. First, capture the objectives. Second, draw more troops away from our weakened northern front.<br><br>This is again a coordinated attack. The goal is Aragon's capital, Zaragoza. On your way to Zaragoza, you will encounter a lot of strongly-entreched falangist garrisons. These garrisons will try to resist, and delay you, until the arrival of rebel reinforcements, so a fast advance is needed. A guerrilla group has been deployed also to capture the Zaragoza bridges, but will not be able to hold them indefinitely.<br><br>--- Historically, this operation was a minor victory for the Republicans, achieved in the battle for the small village Belchite, where the rebel reinforcements attacked the Republican left flank. This battle is known as ''Battle for Belchite'' or Batalla de Belchite in Spanish.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce6.xml", "Batalla de Teruel", "Batalla de Teruel<br><br>15 de Diciembre de 1937<br><br>A pesar de los esfuerzos realizados, las operaciones de los meses pasados no alcanzaron sus objetivos primarios, el frente Norte ha caido, y la ofensiva rebelde sobre el Levante se acerca cada vez mas a Valencia (capital de la Republica provisionalmente). Para ayudarse en su avance hacia el Mediterraneo, el enemigo cuenta con la estrategica posicion de Teruel, que capturo tiempo atras. Esta posicion constituye un enorme peligro para Levante, por lo que no podemos permitir que continue en manos rebeldes.<br>La ofensiva que lanzaremos consiste en otro ataque envolvente que acabara rapidamente con la guarnicion enemiga, pero de por sentado que recibiremos un duro contraataque seguidamente. Las condiciones climatologicas este invierno estan siendo especialmente duras... los -28 grados que hace ahi fuera seran un problema mas.<br><br>Buena suerte.<br><br>Batalla de Teruel<br><br>December 15th, 1937<br><br>Althought we have made valiant efforts to change the tactical and strategic situation, recent operations have not achieved the High Command's goals. The Northern front has fallen, and the rebel offensive over the Levante is approaching the Republic's provisional capital in Valencia. Now, the enemy has an important base to aid his advance on the Mediterranean Sea, Teruel. The enemy base at Teruel is a great danger for the whole Levante area. We cannot allow the enemy to continue holding Teruel, if we are to save the Republic!<br><br>The planned offensive consist of a concentrated attack on Teruel, in order to quickly finish the rebel garrison defending Teruel. The rebels are commanded by Colonel Rey D'Harcourt, a clever opponent. The High Command thinks the fascists will send a huge number of reinforcements as soon as our troops appear at Teruel, so drive your troops quickly to the objectives and be careful to secure your flanks... Reinforcements of the V Army Corps will arrive to help you.<br><br>Ah, one more thing... as you surely already know it's minus 28 degrees (-18 Fahrenheit) and the snow will be another enemy to face for El Ejercito Popular...<br><br>Buena suerte.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226, "support": [206]}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce7.xml", "Ofensiva del Ebro", "Ofensiva del Ebro<br><br>25 de Julio de 1938<br><br>El enemigo ha alcanzado el mar Mediterraneo y las cosas no pueden ir peor, tal vez esta sea nuestra ultima oportunidad de encauzar la situacion, general. Se ha concebido un nuevo plan de batalla, esta ocasion es el mas ambicioso de todo cuanto hemos hecho hasta ahora. Nuestro Ejercito Popular ha tomado sigilosamente posiciones en torno al rio Ebro, cerca de Amposta, en Tarragona, con la mision de cruzarlo y romper asi el frente por una zona por la que el enemigo no se lo espera.<br>El objetivo primario es cruzar el rio y establecer una fuerte cabeza de puente alcanzando la capital de la comarca; Gandesa. Una posible victoria en esta operacion nos permitiria futuros avances que tal vez pudiesen re-equilibrar la situacion.<br><br>Buena suerte.<br><br>Ofensiva del Ebro<br><br>July 25th, 1938<br><br>[Handwritten message received by courier]<br><br>The enemy has finally reached the Mediterranean sea, and things can't be worse. Maybe this will be our last chance to reverse the fortunes of war, commandante. A new plan has been designed. This offensive is our biggest gamble in the war up to now. People's Army units have silently taken positions along the river Ebro, nearly to the town of Amposta, in the province of Tarragona. The main mission is to cross the great Ebro river and break through the enemy lines here, in a place where an attack is not expected. Your mission is to cross the river, make a bridgehead to allow more troops to cross, and finally reach and conquer the town of Gandesa.<br><br>A victory here would allow us further advances. If we are defeated here ... No, failure is too terrible to contemplate.<br><br>Buena suerte.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce8.xml", "Contraofensiva del Ebro", "Contraofensiva del Ebro<br><br>3 de Septiembre de 1938<br><br>Los fascistas han detenido en seco nuestra ofensiva, nos hemos quedado a las puertas de Gandesa y la aviacion Italoalemana nos hostiga continuamente. La ofensiva ha fracasado rotundamente, nuestra unica opcion ahora es retirar nuestras tropas para evitar mayores bajas.<br>Su mision es hacer una retirada ordenada hacia la otra orilla del rio Ebro, tratando de tener el menor numero posible de bajas.<br><br>Instrucciones: Para ganar el escenario debe retirar sus tropas hacia la orilla derecha del Ebro y despues tomar las dos banderas nacionalistas nombradas en el mapa como ''EXIT''. Atencion, obteniendo una BV PIERDE EL ESCENARIO, obtener una V se considera como una TV y una TV se considera como BV y da prestigio.<br><br>Contraofensiva del Ebro<br><br>September 3rd, 1938<br><br>\"The fascists have stopped our offensive, we are at the gates of Gandesa, and the enemy Italian - German airforce is smashing us. Our offensive is a complete dissaster, and our last chance now is to retreat our troops to the right bank of the Ebro river to avoid even greater losses.<br><br>Your mission is to make an organized retreat to the east bank of the Ebro river, trying to take as few losses as possible. Plus ultra, Senor General\"<br><br>---Instructions: To win this scenario, your should retreat your troops to the East bank of the river, and then take the two Nationalist flags named as ''EXIT''. GETTING A BV YOU WILL LOSE THE SCENARIO! In order to win you should get at least a V, which is considered as a classical TV, and a TV is considered a BV and brings you extra-prestige.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["gce9.xml", "Batalla del rio Segre", "Batalla del rio Segre<br><br>6 de Noviembre de 1938<br><br>El rotundo fracaso en el Ebro ha propiciado a los rebeldes lanzar una gran ofensiva sobre Catalunya. El alto mando tiene intencion de al menos detener esa ofensiva y se ha planeado una operacion en el sector de Lerida, destinada a corregir el frente y recuperar dos importantes centrales electricas al otro lado del rio.<br><br>Su mision se localizara al Norte del dispositivo, justo al Sur de Lerida, cruce el rio y alcance la localidad de Fraga, donde segun informes de agentes infiltrados se encuentra la comandancia de las tropas enemigas en este sector.<br><br>Mucho nos tememos que a pesar de todo la guerra estara perdida pase lo que pase...<br><br>Batalla del rio Segre<br><br>November 6th 1938<br><br>The disaster in the Ebro operation has allow the rebels to launch a big offensive over Catalunya. The high command wants to (at least) stop that offensive, or delay it basically. The current operation consist of an attack in the Segre river sector, Southwards to Lerida, aimed to stabilize our front and to recapture two important electric plants in the other side of the river.<br><br>Your mission is to cross the river, and take the town of Fraga, where intelligence reports the enemy command center is deployed.<br><br>However, personally I think the fate of the Republica is sealed, my friend.  If you fail, there is no one to help you.<br><br>Buena suerte.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["vgce0.xml", "Batalla del rio Segre", "Batalla del rio Segre<br><br>6 de Noviembre de 1938<br><br>Todas las cancillerias europeas estan absolutamente sorprendidas por el fulgurante cambio de rumbo que la guerra parece estar dando. Para completar la victoria se ha creado una operacion en el sector catalan al sur de Lerida, donde los rebeldes han tratado de avanzar para tratar de equilibrar la situacion. Su mision es salir al encuentro del avance fascista en el sector del rio Segre, encontrar la formacion de tropas atacantes y neutralizarla.<br><br>Agentes infiltrados informan de que el puesto de mando enemigo se encuentra en la localidad de Fraga, que constituye uno de los objetivos de la mision.<br><br>Buena suerte!, si logramos la victoria total en esta operacion la puerta hacia la capital de Aragon quedara abierta.<br><br>Batalla del rio Segre<br><br>November 6th, 1938<br><br>All the foreign goverments are absolutely amazed by the striking change of the war! To complete the victory over the rebel troops we have planned an attack along the Segre river, southwards from Lerida, where the rebels are trying to advance to halt our attacks. Your mission is to face the rebel attack on the Segre river.<br><br>Intelligence reports that the enemy command point is located in the village of Fraga, and obviously that is one of the main goals of your mission.<br><br>Buena suerte!  If we can achieve a complete victory, this operation will open the way to Zaragoza again!", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["vgce1.xml", "Ataque a Zaragoza", "Ataque a Zaragoza<br><br>12 de Febrero de 1939<br><br>Felicidades por su ascenso general!, tras el rotundo exito en la ofensiva del Ebro el enemigo se ha visto obligado a retirarse de las zonas contiguas al Mediterraneo que habia ocupado, sumado a nuestra victoria, los franceses han levantado el cierre de la frontera y las armas sovieticas que esperabamos han logrado pasar la frontera. Gracias a todo esto, es la hora de explotar nuestro exito!, ademas los aliados de los rebeldes estan perdiendo la paciencia con ellos.<br>Nuevamente el plan es atacar Zaragoza, aprendiendo de los errores del pasado. Zaragoza es la puerta hacia Burgos, la capital fascista. Una gran victoria aqui podria cambiar el curso de la guerra y desestabilizar toda la retaguardia enemiga, incluso incitando al levantamiento en las zonas del Norte contra los ocupantes rebeldes.<br><br>Hemos infiltrado algunos grupos de guerrilleros tras las lineas enemigas, que seguro le seran de utilidad. De paso, estos guerrilleros nos informan que los rebeldes han desplegado aqui el CTV al completo, y es probable que la 13 Division vuelva a presentar batalla... <br><br>Esta es la batalla decisiva!!!.<br><br>Ataque a Zaragoza<br><br>February 12th, 1939<br><br>Congratulations on your promotion general! After the big success in the Ebro Offensive the enemy has retreated many troops from the Mediterranean areas. The French government has opened the border and we have received more Soviet weapons. This is the hour to start the exploiting of the present situation! Again, the plan is to attack Zaragoza, taking into account the past experiences in the Aragon front. Capturing Zaragoza will clear the path to Burgos; the Fascist capital!. A major victory here surely will change all our fortunes, and the Northern areas would rise up against the Fascists also.<br><br>Some guerrilla groups are beyond the enemy lines, and you can probably use them to our advantage. This guerrilla units have informed us that the enemy troops here are mainly composed of the complete Italian CTV and the famous rebel 13th Division.  Do not underestimate the enemy, General.<br><br>Buena suerte.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [207, 208, 209, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["vgce4.xml", "Ceuta", "Ceuta<br><br>5 de Agosto de 1939<br><br>La rebelion ha terminado en toda la Peninsula, la debilidad de retaguardia del enemigo ha sido clave para que el Norte se levantara contra los rebeldes, e incluso muchas unidades rebeldes se hayan cambiado de bando. Burgos, la capital enemiga ha caido, y las fuerzas insurgentes en el Sur han embarcado hacia el protectorado de Marruecos.<br><br>Para terminar la guerra debemos asaltar el protectorado. El plan consiste en atacar el puerto de Ceuta, y despues avanzar hacia Tetuan, donde se ha establecido el centro de mando de los rebeldes. Unidades navales han salido de la base de Cartagena, ademas el V cuerpo ha llegado a costas proximas a Ceuta desde Cadiz.<br><br>Algunos de nuestros valerosos guerrilleros operan ya sobre el terreno, nos han remitido informes que muestran que el enemigo cuenta con fuerzas de las que se retiraron de la Peninsula, y que ha organizado en dos divisiones, compuestas por banderas de la Legion; la division ''Ceuta'' y la division ''Tetuan'', asi como otros elementos de la ya famosa 13 Division. Los rebeldes siguen recibiendo cierta ayuda italiana, lo que complicara las cosas.<br><br>Buena suerte.<br><br>Ceuta<br><br>August 5th, 1939<br><br>The uprising against the Republic is completely smashed by our People's Army, the weakness of the rear rebel territories has been a key for our final victory, Northern places like Asturias, Santander or Euzkadi started a revolt against the rebel opressors, also, some rebel units joined the People's Army, and Burgos, the enemy capital has fallen. Many rebel troops have embarked to the Spanish Morocco, where they will try to resist with some Italian help.<br><br>To finish the war, we must clear Morocco. The high command has designed a plan, disembarking our troops in the Ceuta area and establishing two beach heads to cut the communications between Ceuta and Tetuan.<br><br>Intelligence reports the rebel forces are mainly composed by the elements from the 13th Division, and some Legion Banderas, which have been included into two newly formed divisions; the division Tetuan and the division Ceuta, which will surely be extremely hard. Also, Italian units will make harder the things.<br><br>Naval forces from the Cartagena base are also here to destroy the rebel naval power, but be careful, Italian submarines have been spotted.<br><br>Buena suerte.  Victoria or muerte!", [{"id": 1, "country": 225, "support": [208, 214]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce"],
["Zhukov: Red God of War (1939-1945)"],
["ga4_0.xml", "Khalkin Gol", "Good morning comrade Lieutenant-General. STAVKA has decided it is time for you to break the stalemate at Khalkin Gol. The Japanese have been pouring reinforcements into the area, but, as you know, so have we, and we continue to do so. Therefore you will expel the invaders and push them back to where they came from!", [{"id": 1, "country": 5, "support": [24]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [304]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_1.xml", "Chisinau", "Comrade General, as you are now commander of the Kiev Special Military District, we have a special assignment for you to organize! As you know, the Romanians have consented to give us back the territory taken from us during the civil war, but, in disregard of the agreement, they are also attempting to take with them railroad rolling stock, factory equipment, and other supplies as they evacuate the area! To help halt this blatant violation of the agreement, you must secure the Chisinau vicinity by occupying as many cities as possible and by cutting off their routes of exit over the Prut river. We are still trying to determine exactly where they plan on crossing the Prut river, but as soon as we know, you will know...", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_2.xml", "Yelnya", "Comrade General, STAVKA applauds your decision in rejecting a  defensive posture in favor of a more active stance. As a result, the German offensive has been brought to a halt here in the Yelnya sector. Stalin now requests that You and General Rokossovsky turn the tables on the Germans by retaking Yelnya and securing the remainder of the area....", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_3.xml", "Istra", "Comrade General, the lead German forces now stand less than 30 kilometers away from the Kremlin! Stalin has finally approved the counter offensive proposed by You and General Vasilevsky. You will commence it immediately!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_4.xml", "Rzhev", "Comrade Zhukov, the desired effect of compelling the Germans to bring up four additional panzer divisions and one motorized division to deal with your attack, (thus effectively depriving their Stalingrad sector of the reinforcements they needed to deal with the Uranus operation), appears to have been accomplished. Therefore, Stalin has now authorized  your order for  the remnants of the 6th Tank Corps and three Cavalry divisions to break the encirclement...<br><br>VICTORY CONDITIONS:<br><br>Exit 6 Ground units...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_5.xml", "Operation Iskra", "Comrade Zhukov, I am sure that Stalin has already briefed you on the importance of this operation to our starving people trapped in Leningrad. They are depending for their lives on your leadership of the Leningrad and Volkov fronts!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_6.xml", "Operation Kutuzov", "Comrade Zhukov, your prediction made back in April has come to pass! The Germans have launched a massive attack towards Kursk. But as you have also foreseen, the German onslaught has more or less stalled in front of our defensive preparations. As per your orders, General Popov's Bryansk front, and General Sokolovsky's Western front,  have a few days ago initiated their attacks in the direction of Orel. As STAVKA  advisor to General Rokossovsky's Central front, Stalin has given the OK for you to now order the Central front to stage a counter-attack in the general direction of the Orel sector, thus unfolding a powerful three-front offensive on the Orel region...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_7.xml", "Kamenets-Podolsk", "Comrade Marshal, the joint attack by your 1st Ukrainian Front and Marshal Konev's 2nd Ukrainian Front has been approved by Stalin! The 2nd Ukrainian Front will move against Uman tommorrow, and then with any luck, we will end up encircling  the 1st Panzer Armee in the Kamenets-Podolsk region...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_8.xml", "Bagration (Choice)", "Good Morning Comrade Marshal. Since you are now Stavka coordinator for both the 1st and 2nd Belorussian fronts, and we know how you like to be close to the front lines with your troops, Stalin has given you the option to decide at which front you would like to be...<br><br>Note: To choose the 1st Belorussian path, go to Staging Area 1. To choose the 2nd Belorussian path, go to Staging Area 2...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_9.xml", "Bobruisk", "Comrade Marshal, latest intelligence and recon reports show that the Germans have made extensive defensive preparations around Bobruisk, and have declared it a fortified area, nonetheless, we will proceed as planned. As you already know, the goal of this operation is twofold: breakthrough the defensive positions and take Bobruisk, and exploit any gaps that are opened, with the objective of forcing open a southern route towards Minsk...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_10.xml", "Brest-Litovsk", "Comrade Marshal, due to the staggering success of the Belorussian operations thus far, Stalin has decided to implement the plan for the expansion of the offensive to the Northern and Southern flanks. You will now \"suggest\" to Rokossovsky that he deploy the left wing of the 1st Belorussian front to the south of the Pripet  Marshes. From there, see to it that  Brest-Litovsk is taken...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_11.xml", "Praga", "Comrade Marshal, as you know, two bridgeheads over the Vistula have already been secured in preparation for the drive into Warsaw, and now that You and  Rokossovsky are finished preparing, Stalin has given the go ahead for the last remaining key German bridgehead on the east bank to be taken, thus eliminating a dangerous bulge in the Vistula Front, which Stalin would like to have straightened out before starting any large scale operations. But, just between You and Me comrade, I think Stalin also sees this operation as an opportunity to appear to the world as finally addressing the situation in Warsaw...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_12.xml", "Mogilev", "STAVKA agrees with you Comrade Marshal; the drive to capture Mogilev will be critical to the overall success of the Bagration operation. The German forces holding the Mogilev sector have a high proportion of very good units which cannot be allowed to reinforce either of the sectors to the north or south. Your's and general Zakarov's primary objectives are: capture Mogilev, thus taking control of the network of roads running from Mogilev to Minsk, and also to pin down the bulk of the German 4th Armee while the parallel offensives are taking place around Vitebsk and Bobruisk...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_13.xml", "Novogrudok", "Comrade Marshal, now that the trapped German 4th Armee has, for the most part, been reduced in the pocket east of Minsk, STAVKA has issued  new objectives for You and general Zakharov; secure the Novogrudok area, capture the key points of enemy resistance, especially Grodno and Volkovysk, and advance in the direction of Bialystok. To aid you in this task, STAVKA has subordinated the 3rd army from the 1st Belorussian front to be under your command, and has ordered elements of the 3rd Belorussian front to provide support for the duration of this operation...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [4, 303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_14.xml", "Osowiec", "August 6 1944<br><br>Comrade Marshal, now that you have successfully taken Grodno and Bialystok, STAVKA has issued new objectives for the 2nd Belorussian front; capture the fortress of Osowiec whilst securing the area and moving in the direction of Lomza, enlarging the bridgeheads in preparation for a further advance into East Prussia...", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["ga4_15.xml", "Stargard", "Comrade Marshal, seeing as the German counter attack has been blunted here in the Arnswalde sector with the result that the Germans are slowly falling back to their staging areas, Stalin suggests that you take the initiative and drive as far west as you can! This will assist Rossokovsky and the 2nd Belorussian front in clearing the enemy from all of Eastern Pomerania between Danzig and Stettin...", [{"id": 1, "country": 303, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2"],
["ga4_16.xml", "Seelow Heights", "Comrade Marshal, in view of the existing military and political situation, STAVKA has decided that the Berlin operation should be launched no later than April 16th, so here we are! Reviewing the plan once more: The main thrust toward Berlin and the capture of the city are entrusted to You and the 1st Belorussian front. Marshal Konev's 1st Ukrainian front is to strike from the Neisse river against enemy forces south of Berlin and cut off the main force of Army Group Center, thus securing your operations from the south. Konev should then be in a position to strike at Berlin from the south if necessary. Since Rossokovsky's 2nd Belorussian front will not be able to cross the Oder river before April 20th, you will have to advance with an uncovered right flank for the first crucial days of the operation, but, we have faith in your abilities!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [303]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89, "support": [20]}], "eqp-comww2"],
["Spartacus: The Slave Revolt (73-71 BC)"],
["spa0.xml", "AC 073 - Escape from gladiator school", "AC 073 The escape from the gladiatorial school<br><br>\"Spartacus! How long do you want to train great men, to slaughter each other in the arena? <br>No, it can´t go on!<br>Arise - 200 gladiators are behind you !!! Flee to the east and try to reach the Vesuvius . \"<br><br>Historical: <br>Spartacus was born about 110 BC in the area around the middle course of the Strymon<br>(modern-day Struma river, Bulgaria) 82 BC he was sold to Lentulus Batiatus, owner of a gladiatorial school (ludus) near Capua. He appointet Spartacus to sword trainer for his school.<br>In 73 BC, Spartacus was among a group of gladiators plotting an escape.<br>The plot was betrayed but about 78 men seized kitchen implements, fought their way free from the school, and seized several wagons of gladiatorial weapons and armor.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa1.xml", "AC 073 - Liberation of surrounding land", "AC073 - Liberation of the surrounding area<br><br>Your escape from Capua was succesfull !!! Now go get food and weapons from the transport and freed the slaves of the surrounding area. Along with these new followers you perhaps have a chance to see your homeland !!!<br><br>Historical:<br><br>After escaping from Capua they settled at the foot of Vesuvius, and hold up transports to get to food. So they also came to weapons. In the course of time, more and more slaves and outlaws joined the group, as their leader Spartacus was chosen. His lieutenants were the Celts Crixus and Oinominos. <br>The response of the Romans was hampered by the absence of the Roman legions, which were already engaged in fighting a revolt in Hispania and the Third Mithridatic War. So the Senate sent propraetor C. Claudius Glaber with only 3000 recruits.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa2.xml", "AC 073 - Battle at Vesuvius ", "AC 073 - Battle at Vesuvius (Schlacht am Vesus)<br><br>Spartacus - Months have passed and your followers entreched at Vesuvius. Gaius Claudius Glaber by now received the order to put down the rebellion.<br>Spartacus ! Now it's your turn to avert this threat. The first real battle is to win !<br><br>Historical:<br>Propraetor C. Claudius Glaber drove with 3000 recruits Spartacus and his bunch before him, up to Mount Vesuvius, where he wanted to starve out the slaves. Spartacus was not discouraged, raided one night foolhardy the besiegers, who thought they were safe, and put them to flight.<br>The arrogant error of Glaudius Glaber, to dispense the usual fortification with wooden palisades, retaliated strongly. The frightened recruits fled and Glaber barely escaped. This sensational victory not only caused more slaves, but also impoverished farmers, farm workers and adventurers to join Spartacus.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa3.xml", "AC 073 - Conquest of Nola", "Conquest of Nola (Die Eroberung von Nola)<br><br>Our army is growing, and the city of Nola lies ahead. The local slaves will help us in conquering by opening the doors at night. A daring plan! <br>Can you manage to conquer Nola, free the slaves and saturate your army?<br><br>Historical:<br>The army of Spartacus conquered the city of Nola, after slaves opened the town gates from the inside. The former slaves rage in the city, killing their former masters through no vault of Spartacus. He can only stop them when he announced that praetor Publius Varinius is with his troops on the march - In fact, he was on the way, but Spartacus could Nola leave on time.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa4.xml", "AC 073 - Battle of Acerrae", "Battle of Acerrae - Spartacus vs. Furius<br><br>Nola you have left  in chaos behind you, but your pursuers are already within reach. Furius, sergeant of praetor Publius Varinius, stands with 3,000 men at Acerrea.<br>Show them who you are<br><br>Historical:<br>Praetor Publius Varinius was elected by Rome to put down the uprising. His sergeant, Furius, met first on the slave army. With 3,000 men, Furius saw towards an easy victory. But Spartacus had set his troops excellent, and Furius lost the battle.<br>Where the battle took place is not known to me, Acerrae is selected fictitious.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa5.xml", "AC 073 - Battle near Salinae Heraclae", "Battle near Salinae Heraclea<br><br>Spartacus, now you have to prove yourself in the fight against Varius's legacy Cossinius.<br>His troops have theur camp at Salinae Hercalea. Prepare your wild bunch for it !!!<br><br>Historical:<br>After Spartacus had defeated Varinius lieutenant Furius, he encountered the troops of Varinius' legat Cossinius. He carefree had a bath, while Spartacus blasted his troops at Heraclea Salinae.<br>He fled into his fortified camp but was killed when Spartacus's forces overrun it in the flush of victory.<br><br>Since the position of Salinae Heraclea is not known, I made the better-known map of Herculaneum.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa6.xml", "AC 073 - Escape from the camp of slaves", "AC 073 - Escape from the camp of slaves<br><br>Spartacus, after defeating two of Varinius subordinate leaders, you are now almost surrounded by Varinius´ main troops.<br>It seems a pitched battle would take no good end. Will you succeed the outbreak and retreat over the mountains ???<br><br>Historical:<br>After the defeat of his lieutenants, Varinius was finally having a larger troop contingent to the site and surrounded the slave army at the camp of Heraclea. Spartacus recognized the weakness of his position, where he and his men would soon be cut off from supply. Nevertheless, he let his troops continue to strengthen the fortifications, so that Varinius happy believed that the Thracian prepared to a long siege. At night, Spartacus let bodies set up as guardians and left quietly position. He successfully led his men under the protection of the night, passing the too careless Romans. Varinius only became suspicious when he no longer heard the usual background noise from the slave camp. He conquered the empty camp and would have torn his hair when realizing how he had been led around by the nose.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa7.xml", "AC 073 - Conquest of Nuceria", "AC073 - Conquest of Nuceria<br><br>Varinius you have tricked excellent. Now Nuceria lies ahead of you, but i don´t think he will let you flee without further ado. So be on your guard !<br><br>Historical:<br>Varinius started persecution immediately after he had \"conquered\" Spartacus´ vacated camp. On Spartacus way lay several cities, including Nuceria that he captured and reinforced his army with the freed slaves. Varinius pursued him, but could not prevent the loss of Nuceria.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa8.xml", "AC 073 - Destruction of Varinius at Picentia", "AC 073 - Destruction of Varinius at Picentia<br><br>Varinius is going to follow you to the back of the Moon. Bring this to an End. He stays together with his troops in Front of you at Picentia.<br><br>Historical:<br>Varinius was finally beaten by Spartacus and his Troops, his army was nearly exterminated. In this Scenario at Picentia, where exact I din`t know. Picentia was conquered by Spartacus without a doubt.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa9.xml", "Spartacus or Krixos", "AC 072 - Spartacus or Krixos<br><br>We are writing the Year 72 BC. The Celts are getting more and more aggressive and want to defeat Rome. For that Reason, Krixos seperates from Spartacus and takes his own way. <br><br>Now it is your choice to go either with Spartacus or Krixos.<br><br>Historical: <br>As described, a Group of Celts under the command of Sparatcus Friend and Subleader \"Krixos\" indeed seperated to keep going to attack the Romans in their own Country. Spartacus still followed his target to cross the Alps from Italy.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa10.xml", "AC 072 - Battle of Mons Garganos", "AC 072 - Battle of Mons Garganos<br><br>Crixus, prepare yourself for your first fight without Spartacus against the Romans. In front of you is the camp of Arrius. Raze it and him to the ground !<br><br>Historical:<br>Rome, now finally taking the uprising serious, brought in the big guns. The Roman Senate dispatched a pair of consular legions under the command of Lucius Gellius Publicola and Gnaeus Cornelius Lentulus Clodianus.<br>Gellius subleader, propraetor Q. Arrius, lost at Mons Gargano a skirmish against the Celts of Crixus.<br>These, however, did not use their victory, but got pointless drunk in the conquered Roman camp.<br>Arrius went back and annihilate the drunken Celts almost completely.<br><br>ATTENTION:<br>NOT USE SPARTACUS !!!!", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa11.xml", "AC 072 - Battle against L. Gellius Poplicola", "AC 072 Battle against L. Gellius Poplicola<br><br>You have defeated subleader Arrius. But his general \"Gellius' comes to avenge him.<br>Can you put him to him to flight ???<br><br>HIstorical:<br>This is a fictional scenario, because Crixos never came to this.<br><br>ATTENTION:<br>NOT USE SPARTACUS", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa12.xml", "AC 072 - Battle against Lentullus", "AC 072 - Battle against Lentullus<br><br>In front of you lies consul Cornelius Lentullus Clodianus with two legions. Behind you, Gellius and Arrius are moving up with two legions.<br>Spartacus, here you only have one option -> Defeat Lentullus and moves on to the north.<br><br>Historical:<br>Rome sent 4 legions against Spartacus. Two were led by consul Cornelius Lentullus Clodianus, who thwarted Spartacus on his way north. The other two legions, running from the south up to Spartacus, were led by Consul L. Gellius Poplicola and his praetor Arrius, who had defeated Crixus.<br>Lentullus did not wait until they had encircled Spartacus and attacked to soon. That was was Spartacus chance, and he used it.<br><br>ATTENTION:<br>NOT USE KRIXOS !!!", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa13.xml", "AC 072 - revenge for Krixos", "AC072 - revenge for Krixos (Rache für Krixos)<br><br>After you've beaten Lentullus, you hear of the defeat that Crixus had suffered against Gellius and Arrius. You couldn´t put up with this accusation.<br>Go into Battle with them, they persecute you anyway ...<br>Historical:<br><br>After beating Lentullus, Spartacus also defeated his pursuer Consul L. Gellius Poplicola.<br>Spartacus aligned obsequies for the fallen Crixus, where between 300 and 400 prisoned Romans had to fight against each other in a gladiatorial combat<br><br>ATTENTION:<br>NOT USE KRIXOS !!!", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa14.xml", "AC 072 - Battle at Gallia Cisalpina", "AC 072 - Battle at Gallia Cisalpina (Schlacht bei Gallia Cisalpina)<br><br>After you defeated Gellius and Arrius, the path to freedom over the Alps, where many of your followers have their home, lays clear. But is the way really free? <br>No! In the province of Gallia Cisalpina, strong Roman troops  under governor C. Cassius Longinus and praetor Cn. Manlius are awaiting you ...<br><br>Historical:<br>While Arrius newly arranged the battered legions of the two consuls, Spartacus moved further north, to the pre-Alpine province of Cisalpine Gaul.<br>Once again strong Roman troops under governor C. Cassius Longinus and praetor Cn. Manlius made a stand against him<br>Again the Thracian and his slave army won. Surprisingly, Spartacus chose to lead his army of slaves back into Italy.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa15.xml", "AC 072 - Battle at Firmum Picenum", "AC 072 - Battle at Firmum Picenum (Schlacht bei Firmum Picenum)<br><br>Look at one: We know them yet! In front of us are the contracted troops of Lentulus, Gellius and Arrius, or what's left of it them. It's time to destroy them finally<br><br>Historical:<br>After the turn to the south, Spartacus met the newly organized Roman legions, probably under the joint command of Lentulus, Gellius and Arrius. They again experienced a setback. <br>So Spartacus stood shortly thereafterbefore Rome. He did not lay siege to the city and moved even further south.<br>It took half a century that an enemy,  the Visigoth Alaric,  again stood an enemy army before Rome.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa16.xml", "AC 071 - break the siege", "AC 071 - break the siege<br><br>Spartacus, we`ve spend the Winter at the Söuth and consolidated. But Crassus used the Time. He has build up a mighty siege. Could we break through and invade the interior of the country? It has to be done soon, because we are running out of supplys...<br><br>Historical:<br>M. Licinius Crassus became Prätor and voluntarily took command of the Troops against Spartacus. The defeated Troops of Subleader Mummius had to endure the Decimation (Every 10th legionary was executed). Trough this harsh treatment he bucked up his Troops and brought the Slaves to the edge of a defeat.<br><br>Spartacus had spend the Winter at the bleak headland of South Italy. The escape overseas using the kilikian Pirates worked, despite a big advanced payment. That was how he had to break trough the siege of Crassus. At their first try about 12.000 Slaves died and it looked as if the fate of the Slave army was sealed. But the tide turned. At their second try the Slaves suddenly recovered their old strength, broke through the siege and invaded the interior of the Province Lukania.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["spa17.xml", "AC 071 - Attack on the camp of the Celts", "AC071 Attack on the camp of the Celts<br><br>Spartacus! The Celts that had seperated from you need your help! Crassus redeployed his troops undetected to the close Camp and is attacking our Friends Gannius and Castus. Come on there is no time to waste...<br><br>Historical:<br>After the break trough Crassus siege Spartacus again invaded the interior of Italy as far as the Province of Lukania. Here the Celts under the command of Gannius and Castus devided from Spartacus. Spartacus encamped nearby the Celts to support them in case of an emergency. That was what happened. Crassus redeployed his troops undetected from the main camp to a smaller camp and attacked the Celts at the morning with his entire force. He annihilated them. Spartacus arrived too late, to support them sustainably. As he notified the hopeless Situation of the Celts, he pulled back. The second Commander Quästor Tremellius attacked Spartacus. But Spartacus was able to defeat the Quästor and fled to Lukania.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310, "support": [308]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag"],
["spa18.xml", "AC 071 - Battle of Paestum", "AC 071- Battle of Paestum<br><br>Spartacus now it`s getting tough. You march in the direction of Paestum. Certainly here are four Legions of Crassus - ready to fight. According to rumors Pompeius is also on the way to Paestum. This means now: Fight for your Life !!!<br>  <br>Historical:<br>Spartacus encountered the strong forces of Crassus at Paestum. It is told, that he killed his own horse while saying, that if they would lose today, he wouldn`t need one anymore and, if they would win, he would have more Horses then he could ever need. He personally lead the attack on the roman Camp. The heroic, but because of the secession of the Celts weakened Slaves were defeated by the heavily superiority of Crassus. Only a few survived. Crassus gave order to crucify 6.000 captured Slaves along the Via Appia towards Rome. The fate of Spartacus is unknown, even the romans were not able to find his dead body or identify him underneath the captives. By this, the Trakian disappeared as shrouded in mystery as he had risen from it in the past, to shock the foundations of the triumphant Rome and to defeat several roman armys.", [{"id": 0, "country": 310}], [{"id": 1, "country": 307}], "eqp-ag" ],
["Viet Cong (1964-1975)"],
["nvc00.xml", "Raid at Binh Gia", "Raid at Binh Gia<br><br>December, 1964<br><br>[Your speech to your men] <br><br>Ah brave fighters of the Viet-Cong!  Today will be our first action against our brothers, but do not see them as equals for they are traitors. Yes! Traitors!  They have prostituted their souls to US imperialism!  Now, it's our time to strike and give them a true taste of  Vietnamese fighters. Comrades, under the cover of the night we will take the enemy by surprise.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["nvc01.xml", "Escape from Vung Tau", "Escape from Vung Tau<br><br>December, 1964<br><br>Well, comrade commander, you have done very well. Nevertheless, at the first light of day our agents in Saigon have reported that the puny so-called ''ARVN'' will sent a large number of troops to clear the Vung-Tau area of our men.<br><br>The central office of the Viet-Cong thinks you must undertake an organized withdrawal to safer positions at the jungle. Your men must not be killed or taken prisoner since they must fight another day against the dirty imperialists. It will be at a more adventageous location of our choice. However, I know the central office would also be happy if you are able to show some resistance to the enemy.  This can be accomplished by holding one objective until the end of this mission. One final thing comrade. Our agents have also reported a heli crash near your positions. At least one company of marines have died in the accident, but we are sure that reinforcements will fly over there to recover the corpses.<br><br>So, the choice is save all your fighters or hold a position until the end, the decision is yours.<br><br>Victory Conditions:<br><br>- Hold one victory hex until the end will be considered as a Brilliant Victory.<br>- Or retreat at least 5 units to fight another day (the red boardered hex is the retreat point).", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc02.xml", "Attack on the Plei Me Camp", "Attack on the Plei Me Camp<br><br>October, 1965<br><br>Chao buoi sang comrade. As you know, in the central highlands near to the town of Pleiku, a couple of years ago the Americans constructed a so-called advanced combat base. Your task is to attack and take the camp. To undertake this mission your command will be split into two groups. The northern group must cut the national road and take one of the villages close to the road.  The southern must attack the camp, which it's currently garrisoned by irregular and Montagnard pro-Saigon militia troops.  Obviously it should not be too hard to take. Of course, some kind of retaliation from the Americans dogs is expected, so be careful.<br><br>Victory Conditions:<br><br>- Hold 2 victory objectives until the end to achieve a Brilliant Victory.<br>- Hold 1 victory objective until the end to achieve a Tactical Victory.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc03.xml", "Ia Drang", "Ia Drang Valley<br><br>November, 1965<br><br>Following your recent successes, Headquarters in Hanoi wants to continue the struggle.  You will attack the advanced outposts of the Americans close to the limits of Cambodia. As you know comrade, the puppet capitalist government of Phnom Phem can't prevent us from using their soil to support our operations and that's what we are going to continue to do.<br><br>In the jungle our advanced agents have spotted a number of good landing zones made by heli-transported American troops as well as an artillery position to the SE. They probably are trying pay us back for the blow of the Plei Me attack or just cutting our routes to Cambodia. Nevertheless, your mission will be to give the Americans another decisive defeat. Maybe they will learn the price for staying in Vietnam. Reinforcements from our nearby Viet-Cong comrades will arrive though our jungle supplies routes with ammo and men to support your command.  <br><br>You must clear the enemy landing zones, at any cost.<br><br>Don't forget to watch your back.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc04.xml", "Military Region IV Crisis", "Military Region IV Crisis<br><br>January, 1966<br><br>The vacations are over, commander. Our spies in Saigon have sent us information about an imminent enemy offensive of considerable size. It will be against our positions near Cu-Chi. Deploy your units quickly and take defensive positions to allow a retreat towards safer positions to the west in War Zone C.  It won't be easy, since we need to save the local VC units. American air strikes have destroyed the connections between our tunnels and War Zone C.  Saving the VC units will allow our troops to return to this area in the future. So, don't lose any VC Local units or the operation will be a failure. We need these comrades to maintain the support of south and its knowledge of the area.<br><br>Victory Conditions:<br><br>- Retreat 8 units to ''War Zone C''.<br><br>- Retreat the local Viet Cong units and avoid them be destroyed.", [{"id": 0, "country": 276, "support": [246]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [0, 3]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc05.xml", "Asian Clash", "Asian Clash<br><br>July, 1967<br><br>As you know, commander, our positions near Tuy Hoa are right next to the South Korean troops who are supporting the western invaders. Some of our men, are shortage that exists an operation denominated by the Koreans like ''Hong Kil Dong'', that consists of eliminating our defences in the zone.  We must defend the entire area at all costs, thus avoiding the enemy driving us out of here. However, if you need to retreat some units from the battlefield, there are some underground tunnels ready for your men to avoid annihilation... if needed.<br><br>Your current situation near the Ho Chi Minh trail will allow you to request units from the PAVN when you have enough prestige to do it. <br><br>Victory Conditions:<br><br>- Hold 4 victory objectives until the end to achieve a Brilliant Victory.<br>- Hold 3 victory objective until the end to achieve a Victory.<br>- Hold 2 victory objective until the end to achieve a Tactical Victory.<br><br>\"Some of our spies have reported that exists an operation denominated by the Koreans ''Hong Kil Dong'', that consists of eliminating our defenses in the zone. \"", [{"id": 0, "country": 246, "support": [276]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 18, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc05b.xml", "Strike on Kontum", "Strike on Kontum<br><br>November, 1967<br><br>Comrade commander, we again need your men. As you know, our mid year operations in the province of Kontum have gone well, nevertheless there are still several enemy forward bases that we must destroy. Those bases are too close to our supply routes for Ho the Chi Minh trail and our area 609.  For this reason they must be destroyed. In addition in the province of Kontum an enemy offensive is anticipated and our enemies do not have to count on those outposts.<br><br>Victory Conditions:<br><br>- Hold 5 victory objectives until the end to achieve a Brilliant Victory.<br>- Hold 4 victory objective until the end to achieve a Victory.<br>- Hold 3 victory objective until the end to achieve a Tactical Victory.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc06.xml", "Attack on Khe Sanh", "Attack on Khe Sanh<br><br>January, 1968<br><br>Good morning comrade commander. As you know, our campaign of attacking enemy forward bases continues.  Khe Sanh is the provincial capital and the key towards controlling our national Route 9. Your mission is to coordinate the attack against the Yankee base at Khe Sanh. That base is a constant threat against our supply routes through Laos.<br><br>After crossing the Ho Chi Minh trail you must deploy your troops to the north of Khe Sanh.  Clear the hills of any enemy troops and then undertake the attack on the enemy base. Reinforcements from the west and the east will arrive to help in the struggle against the enemy positions.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc07.xml", "Tet Offensive", "Tet Offensive - Hue and Da Nang<br><br>February, 1968<br><br>Hanoi thinks we can take advantage of the two-day ceasefire announced for the Tet by striking now while the enemy is celebrating the holiday.  They should be in no position to quickly respond.<br><br>Your command will be split into two groups. One will take Hue, where the enemy 2nd ARVN Division's HQ and the MACV compound are located.  The other one must attack Da Nang wherea yankee marine infantry base is located. Some chinese-made rocket launcher batteries will be put under your command. Select your best troops for the offensive and take advantage of the surprise.<br><br>I suggest you to be quick, take up good positions before the enemy can react and then counterattack if you can.<br><br>- Capture and hold 5 victory objectives until the end to achieve a Brilliant Victory.<br>- Capture and hold 4 victory objectives until the end to achieve a Victory.<br>- Capture and hold 2 victory objectives until the end to achieve a Tactical Victory.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246, "support": [276]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [253]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc08.xml", "Laos Counteroffensive", "Laos Counteroffensive<br><br>February, 1971<br><br>Welcome back to the front commander. Once again we need you to re-start the offensive against the enemy. The southern capitalist forces have invaded Laos.  They are trying to cut our supply lines in that country's jungle. By the way Hanoi wants to expunge the south Vietnamese troops from there to preserve our supply lines in Laos.  They also want to show our Laotian allies we can defeat their invaders. Your task is to free the entire Ye Pon river valley from the enemy.<br><br>Remember, for the past year we have been receiving a large surplus of weapons from our comrade allies from China and the USSR. You may now re-equip your units with new equipment.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc09.xml", "Battle of Kontum", "Battle of Kontum<br><br>May, 1972<br><br>Continuing with our campaign of harassment on our southern capitalist enemies, the next step now is to strike the South Vietnam on their home soil! Since our ... successful ... Tet Offensive the foreign allies of the Saigon government have progressively disappeared from the battlefield. Just a couple of advisors are still present in Vietnam. The main danger from the foreign capitalist powers now comes from the air. Well, but let me explain to you what your next task is going to be. <br><br>You are perfect for this operation since you already know the area around Kontum province. This operation is to attack and capture the provincial capital city of Kontum. The problem involves the enemy ''fire bases''.  They are fortified positions between the Laotian frontier and the outskirts of Kontum city. Take all of these fire bases and then attack Kontum. You will receive support from Regional Viet Cong units. Also, the B3 Front has deployed some AA emplacements near the fire bases, as an ''AA umbrella'' to protect your attack on the enemy fortified positions and yes we expect heavy enemy air attacks.<br><br>Chuc may man comrade.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246, "support": [276]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["nvc10.xml", "Liberation of Saigon", "Liberation of Saigon<br><br>April, 1975<br><br>Commander welcome again to the front. The war with the western imperialists and their South Vietnam puppets is about to end. As you know, our latest offensives against the so-called ARVN have all ended with an overwhelming victory. The northern part of South Vietnam has been cleared of enemies by the People's Army of Vietnam. Hue and Da Nang along other key cities have been also liberated and now it's time for the heart of South Vietnam: Saigon! We need to end this war as soon as possibe since the enemies ''stratofortresses'' are smashing Hanoi killing many woman and children.<br><br>As a reward for your past victories Hanoi wants to give you the opportunity to become the liberator of Saigon. The goal of central command is to make a fast advance on Saigon and continue to surprise the world with our lightning victorys over the enemy.  Maybe we can even trap the Americans on the roof of their embassy.<br><br>For Hanoi a Tactical Victory will be unacceptable. To help you in your advance some additional divisions have infiltrated into the South.", [{"id": 0, "country": 246}], [{"id": 1, "country": 253, "support": [9]}], "eqp-olgcw"],
["Soviet Black Sea Fleet (1941-1944)"],
["rcampfa1.xml", "Falciu 1", "00. FALCIU 1 (22 June 1941)<br><br>Dear Comrade. Today fascist forces from Germany have attacked our borders, from the Baltic to the Ukraine. To make things worse, Rumania has declared war upon us. The situation looks grim but we are prepared. Our Red Army is the biggest army in the world and we have more tanks and aircraft than any other country. Victory will be ours.<br><br>Your unit is part of the 150th Rifle Division located in Bessarabia, former part of Rumania. It is likely that the Rumanians will start an offensive here soon. To prevent this and conquer suitable defensive positions to start our own offensive from, you must cross the Prut River at Falciu, capture the bridge and form a bridgehead. Reinforcements will be brought in whenever possible. Beware of the Rumanians who will fight feriously because it is their own soil they will be fighting on. You must succeed. Good luck, Comrade!<br><br>NOTE: You do not start with core units. You have to buy them.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampfa2.xml", "Falciu 2", "01. FALCIU 2 (7 July 1941)<br><br>The war is not going as we had hoped for. North of the Pripjat Marshes the front has collapsed. However south of it, we have our front intact but are slowly being pushed back. <br><br>For weeks the Rumanians have preparing their offensive. They will first elimenate our bridgehead over the Prut River at Falciu. Comrade, you have orders not to step back and hold your lines at all costs! If possible we will arrange reinforcements. However the burden of the Rumanian counterattack will fall upon your troops. Good luck, Comrade!", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampki1.xml", "Kishenev", "02. KISHENEV (14 July 1941)<br><br>Comrade! The Germans have broken through our lines and are advancing with high speed. However, to their south, the Rumanians have still not managed a breakthrough thanks to your men. However if you do not retreat immediately you will be cut off and this would be a disaster! <br><br>You have orders to pull back to Odessa at once. First make it to Kishenev which contains the only road leading out of Bessarabia still in our hands. Be quick because the Rumanian and German fascists are on our heals! Good luck, comrade!", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampode.xml", "Odessa 1941", "03. ODESSA 1941 (13 August 1941)<br><br>Comrade, the situation is getting worse and worse. The Fascists are near Leningrad  and Smolensk in the north and Kiev in the south. Here, near the Black Sea coast, the Rumanian fascists with help of their German allies have advanced to the port of  Odessa which is an important base for our Black Sea Fleet. However we are encircled and cut off from land supplylines because the Germans are driving further and leaving the Rumanians to behind to capture Odessa. We will hold it as long as possible. Any supplies and reinforcements will be brought be sea from the Crimea. <br><br>NOTE: You can only lose this scenario. Goal is to play the full 20 turns and keeping your core alive. Then the scenario will end and you will continue to the next scenario!<br><br>HINT: There is nothing to win, so do not hesitate to retreat to better defensive positions. Be sure to cover your forces with artillery and keep the artillery resupplied. They are vital for the survival of your units.", [{"id": 1, "country": 13, "support": [7]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampper.xml", "Perekop", "04. PEREKOP (25 September 19411)<br><br>Comrade, although Odessa is still in our hands, the enemy rushes further east. At Kiev we have suffered enormous defeats with the losses of hundreds of thousands of soldiers. But we will continue to resist the invaders nonetheless!<br><br>The German fascists now turned their eyes on the Crimean peninsula with the mighty fortress of Sevastopol on it. The Crimea is only connected to the mainland, the Ukraine, with the Perekop peninsula. 24 Hours ago the enemy has surprisingly attacked and almost gained full control of the Perekop peninsula. We must retake Perekop before the fascists are able to pour their reserves into battle and break through. Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampro1.xml", "Rostov 1941", "05. ROSTOV 1941 (25 November 1941)<br><br>Our situation has reached a new depth. In the north the fascists have reached Leningrad and they are advancing on Moskva on the central front. In the south the fascists have captured Odessa, broken through into the Crimea, and days ago Rostov. Rostov is the gate to the Caucasus and its oilfields. We cannot allow the enemy to hold this position. An immediate counterattack has been ordered!<br><br>The Germans have taken Rostov with a number of motorized and armoured formations with lightening speed. However in the urban area of Rostov they have a huge disadvantage. Even more, the fascists advance has created a salient into our lines and this offers the possibility of encircling the fascists at Rostov. The winter has arrived and the plains are covered with snow. This is the time to attack again and drive them back west! Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [37]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampker.xml", "Kerch", "06. KERCH (26 December 1941)<br><br>On the central front, near Moskva, we have pushed the fasicsts armies almost hundred kilometers back, away from our capitol. Rostov is once again in Soviet hands. Sevastopol on the Crimea remains under our control but the remaining part of the Crimean peninsula is occupied by the Rumanian and German fascists. The enemy is attacking Sevastopol for days and without support it will fall. We must make sure this will not happen. Therefore we will invade the eastern Crimea at both Kerch and at Feodosiya. <br><br>You will lead our forces at the Kerch operation. From the Taman peninsula you will land at various places around the town of Kerch, on the far east end of the Kerch peninsula, part of the Crimean peninsula. The German forces are stretched to defend the coasts but they should be ready to counterattack once you have landed. So be quick, land your forces and attack!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampfeo.xml", "Feodosiya", "07. FEODOSIYA (29 December 1941)<br><br>On the central front, near Moskva, we have pushed the fasicsts armies almost hundred kilometers back, away from our capitol. Rostov is once again in Soviet hands. Sevastopol on the Crimea remains under our control but the remaining part of the Crimean peninsula is occupied by the Rumanian and German fascists. The enemy is attacking Sevastopol for days and without support it will fall. We must make sure this will not happen. Therefore we will invade the eastern Crimea at both Kerch and at Feodosiya. <br><br>You will lead our forces at the Feodosiya operation. From the Taman peninsula you will land at various places around the town of Feodosiya, which lies on the connection of the Kerch peninsula with the larger Crimean peninsula. The German forces are stretched to defend the coasts but they should be ready to counterattack once you have landed. So be quick, land your forces and attack!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampcho.xml", "Crimea Choice", "08. CRIMEA CHOICE SCENARIO (15 December 1941)<br><br>This is not a regular scenario but a so called 'player choice scenario'. <br><br>For the next scenario, two scenarios can be played. You can choose which one it will be: Kerch of Feodosiya. Both are similar scenarios, both having an amphibious invasion and followed by ground fighting. No matter what your choice will be, after you played the chosen scenario, you will play all scenarios. Your choice won't affect the further continuation of the campaign, nor the scenarios you will play.<br><br>So make a choice. Take a regular \"Victory\" by taking the first hex to play Kerch. Take a \"Tactical Victory\" by taking the second hex to play Feodosiya.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampsev.xml", "Sevastopol 1942", "09. SEVASTOPOL 1942 (6 June 1942)<br><br>Comrade, despite our initial successes in our Winter offensive, it has failed to defeat the fascist invaders. With the start of spring they have regained their iniative and at the moment are preparing a final assault on the fortress city of Sevastopol which is being cut off from our lines since last year. The Black Sea Fleet will transport your forces to Sevastopol where you will reinforce the defenses. The fascist attack is expected to start as we speak!<br><br>The garrison of Sevastopol has months of artillery and air bombardments survived, and repulsed already two fascist attacks to capture the port. Our forces are exhausted and not many reinforcements can be send. Supplies are hard to deliver. You must hold out for at least 15 days. Then Stavka will decide what to do next. Good luck, comrade.<br><br>NOTE: You can only lose this scenario. Goal is to play the full 15 turns and keeping your core alive. Then the scenario will end and you will continue to the next scenario!<br><br>NOTE: There is nothing to win, so do not hesitate to retreat to better defensive positions. Be sure to cover your forces with artillery and keep the artillery resupplied. They are vital for the survival of your units.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampno1.xml", "Novorossiysk 1", "10. NOVOROSSIYSK 1 (20 September 1942)<br><br>The fascist has started his summer offensive. We expected the fascists to strike against Moskva, our capitol, but they have attacked in the south. Within weeks they had reached the Don River and Stalingrad on the Volga River. Even more south, Rostov has once again switched hands, the oilfields of Maikop have fallen, and German and Rumanian forces poured into the steppes south of Rostov, leading to the Causasus mountains with the valuable oil. A week ago the enemy has taken the Black Sea port of Novorossiyk and if we fail to stop the enemy at the coastal road, other ports will soon be under enemy control as well. <br><br>Your forces must stop the enemy advance down south on the coastal road. Although the recapture of Novorriysk is beyond our limits, you are ordered to contain the German attack and retake several positions in the hills. Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13, 61]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampsuc.xml", "Suchumi", "11. SUCHUMI (28 September 1942)<br><br>THe enemy's advance on the coastal road has been halted and that saves many Black Sea ports still in our hands free from an attack on one side. However the German advance has penetrated deep into the southern steppes and has reached the foot of the Caucasus mountain range. There units, mainly mountain trained troops, are trying to cross the Caucasus mountains and attack the Black Sea ports from behind. The fascists stand on less than 25 kilometers of Suchumi. You must make sure the fascist sees no chance in capturing Suchumi.<br><br>We have been unable to stop the enemy in the mountains, but we will when they go down and try to reach the coast. Your units must secure the port of Suchumi, the coastal road which is our single supplyline to the front near Novorissiysk, and secure essential positions. Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampor1.xml", "Ordzhonikidze 1", "12. ORDZHONIKIDZE 1 (1 November 1942)<br><br>Comrade, the situation at the fronts is critical. We only possess a number of single buildings in Stalingrad. And in the Caucasus Army the German First Panzer Army has  refueled its offensive over the Terek River towards Grozny, and Baku where the oilfields are. After 48 hours of continuous airbombardment, the fascists are storming at the key town of Ordzhonikidze which is a very important communications center. We must deny the enemy control of this town at all costs!<br><br>Your force will be divided into two. One group will rush to Ordzhonikidze and garrison the city against the Germans. A second group will take part in a smart counterstrike on the German flank in order to destroy the attacking Germans from behind, or at least make them retreat. Good luck, comrade.<br><br>NOTE: There are two deployment areas. One on the northern part of the map and in the eastern part of the map.<br><br>NOTE: There are various SNOW hexes on the map. These have the same properties as SAND hexes in the desert. Supplying and reinforcing units on those hexes will never be a 100%.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampor2.xml", "Ordzhonikidze 2", "13. ORDZHONIKIDZE 2 (8 November 1942)<br><br>Of all sectors of the front, from Leningrad to Moscow and to Stalingrad, just here at Ordzhonikidze, we have the iniative, comrade. You have saved Ordzhonikidze from an immediately enemy invasion and cut off the supply lines for the fascist forces at Ordzhonikidze. However, as usual the enemy is persistant, we are sure the Germans have send reinforcements to restore the lines with the trapped Germans. It is likely that the encircled forces will participate in the breakout. If these forces join, then we are likely to lose Ordzhonikidze after all. You must make sure this does not happen by destroying the encircled enemy force and to drive west, away from Ordzhonikidze!<br><br>NOTE: There are various SNOW hexes on the map. These have the same properties as SAND hexes in the desert. Supplying and reinforcing units on those hexes will never be a 100%.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampmai.xml", "Maikop", "14. MAIKOP (10 January 1943)<br><br>We have had victories these last months, comrade! We have trapped hundreds of thousands fascist near Stalingrad where our forces are still feriously resisting the enemy. And in the Caucasus the Germans are slowly retreating. We started our winter offensive to liberate the Caucasus region all the way up to Novorossiysk and Rostov, some weeks ago. Your forces have been held in reserve but will now be deployed in order to recapture Maikop and hopefully cut off enemy forces. The fascist can only retreat west, to Novorossiysk and the Taman/Kuban peninsula, or north-west to Rostov. With the capture of Maikop we can force the fascist forces to take the longer way, to Rostov, where they should be met by our own forces coming from the Don. <br><br>Your goal is to recapture Maikop and the oilfields, as well as an advance to the Kuban River. The Germans are retreating but do this skillful. And the more west you will arrive, the more tenacious the fascist defenses will become. So be careful. Good luck, comrade!<br><br>NOTE: The 'Provisional Soviet Airstrip' can only be used to resupply and and refit air units. No air units can be deployed on it.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampro2.xml", "Rostov 1943", "15. ROSTOV 1943 (2 February 1943)<br><br>We have advanced hundreds of kilometers and we once again stand at the gates of Rostov. It is vital that we capture this gate to the Caucasus as soon as possible, because still not all German units have retreated over the Don, back into the Ukraine. Although many Germans are forced back to the Taman/Kuban peninsula, enemy mobile forces are rushing towards Rostov. If you are quick enough than you can trap them before they have crossed the Don River. In any case, it is vital that we do not lose the momentum in this winter offensive. We must push the fascists invaders back, back and back. Good luck, comrade!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampno2.xml", "Novorossiysk 2", "16. NOVOROSSIYSK 2 (18 March 1943)<br><br>Comrade, althought the fascist invaders cannot do anything about the stunning successes of our winter campaign, they have regained their spirit, again, even after a second winter. In the Ukraine near Kharkov huge battles are being fought and we are not in a position to win easy. We are happy to hold down the Germans. More south, the enemy is still holding the Kuban region, of which the Taman peninsula is only a few miles away from the Kerch peninsula of the Crimea. It offers a safe route of withdrawal for the enemy. <br><br>We have been given orders to drive the enemy out of the Caucasus steppes and the captured Black Sea ports. Attacks on the entire front in the Kuban will be made, but the biggest will take place near Novorossiysk. The Black Sea Fleet has offered a flotilla of cruisers and destroyers as well as thousands of trusty Marines. These, and a part of your force, will land near a large peninula south of Novorossiysk, in order to join up with the force coming from the coast, at Novorissiysk and defeat the enemy. It is a promising plan but it can be done. After all we are pushing the enemy back, west, west, all the the way west where they came from! Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampkry.xml", "Krymskaya", "17. KRYMSKAYA (18 April 1943)<br><br>In the Kuban steppes the enemy is stronger than expected. After a month of ferious attacks we have not breached the fascist front. We have only advanced several miles, and the cities of Novorossiysk and Krasnodar are still in enemy hands.  However we must maintain pressure and eventually the German and Rumanian positions must crack. <br><br>The fascists have started a counterattack to destroy our bridgehead near Novorossiysk, that you helped to form a month ago, and although we are holding on, we are about to crack. To draw away reserves, and to break through the fascist front in the center, we will attack near Krymskaya. Be aware that the Germans have reserves and will use it. On the other hand, we will commit as much forces as we can in order to force a breakthrough. Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampno3.xml", "Novocross", "18. NOVOROSSIYSK 3 (9 September 1943)<br><br>The time has come to destory the enemy on the Kuban steppes. They have been there for far too long. And finally, after months of preparations, we are in position for a full-scale attack on the fascist perimeter. Near Kursk, our units are rolling west again. We must follow and make the enemy see that the Red Army has arisen from its ashes! <br><br>Your force will attack towards Novorossiysk and beyond. Attacks will come from the bridgehead south of Novorossiysk, as well as along the coastal front. The Black Sea Fleet has once again committed Marines who are waiting to get revenge for their fallen comrades, months earlier. So attack, and let nothing stop you! The enemy is still strong and willing to resist so prepare for a ferious battle. We accept not anything less than the complete destruction of the enemy in the Novorossiysk area! Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13, 61]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcamptam.xml", "Taman", "19. TAMAN (25 September 1943)<br><br>Those were quite some days, comrade. Krasnodar and Novorossiysk have been liberated and the fascists cowards are fleeing towards the Taman peninsula where they should be evacuated to the Crimea. Our troops are close to exhausted but so is the enemy, and at least we are winning. The enemy will resist feriously but you should drive all the way west, until you have liberated the Kuban steppes totally!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampod2.xml", "Odessa 1944", "20. ODESSA 1944 (9 April 1944)<br><br>Our winter offensive has brought us on the other side of the Dnjepr River and Kiev has been liberated. Enemy resistance is still present and the fascists are hurt but not dead. Every day resistance increases. We must make optimal use of the momentum, as long as lasts. We will attack near Perekop and force ourselves into the Crimea. Your force will march along the coast and liberate Odessa. <br><br>Although the fascists have had a hard time, they are still able to resist. It is unsure if the enemy decides to defend Odessa. Nonetheless, we demand you take this port as soon as possible, and drive west, if possible up to the Rumanian border. Watch out for experienced elements of elite divisions. The past weeks these have been the prime source of resistance to our advance in the Ukraine. Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampse2.xml", "Sevastopol 1944", "21. SEVASTOPOL 1944 (7 May 1944)<br><br>A month ago we broke through fascist lines at the Perekop peninsula, the sole connection of the Crimean peninsula with the Ukrainian mainland. The enemy has retreated from all over the Crimea to Sevastopol which has been turned into a fortress once again. And this time we will be attacker - and we will gain victory!<br><br>Our forces might run of fuel and ammo before they reach Sevastopol, because of the distances traveled. Also non-motorized units are still on their way to the front. So expect them to arrive anytime. Moskva accepts no delay in taking the city, so you have orders to attack immediately. We are unsure if the enemy is trying to hold the city or to evactuate their forces. Because of the last option, you must attack quick and kill as many fascists as possible so the Crimea is once again free and liberated! Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampjas.xml", "Jassy", "22. JASSY (15 June 1944)<br><br>Since our spring offensives we have a bridgehead into Rumania over the Prut River, near Jassy.  The fascists have taken blow after blow but somehow have regained their spirit. We are convinced the enemy has concentrated a huge force to eliminate our bridgehead. We must hold it. It is an ideal starting point for the invasion of Rumania which is plannend within some months. <br><br>Our forces in the Jassy bridgehead are problaby outnumbered and lack supplies and manpower at the moment. The Germans are depending on the worn out Rumanians to have sufficient manpower. They will try to eliminate our bridgehead as long as this situation continues. You are ordered to hold the bridgehead and repel any fascist counterattack. You are permitted to withdraw to a smaller perimeter but in the end we must have a position on the other side of the Prut River! Watch out for the enemy Panther and Tiger tanks. Good luck, comrade!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampfa3.xml", "Falciu 3", "23. FALCIU 3 (22 August 1944)<br><br>After months of preparations, we have invaded Rumania. The biggest ally of the German cowards that invaded our country. Like our offensives in the Baltic and Byelorussia, we have made promising advances. From our bridgehead over the Prut River at Jassy and at a number of other places, we have broken fascist lines and are driving deep into their rear. If we could join two of our pincers near Falciu, at the Prut River, then we can cut of a considarable number of fascist troops. <br><br>Your force is coming from Rumanian soil, on the west side of the Prut River, down south to Falciu. Other forces will try to cross the Prut River from the area south of Kishenev. Be quick and make sure those fascists get caught. I believe you are familiar with this region, comrade. Good luck.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcampbuc.xml", "Bucharest", "24. BUCHAREST (30 August 1944)<br><br>Great news from some days ago: the Rumanians have surrendered to the mighty Soviet Union and are now fighting against the Germans. The German fascists are in disarray and lack leadership. Many of their forces find themselves trapped in Rumania. However there are still Rumanian fascists in the Rumanian Army that refuse to surrender and remain loyal to their fascists leaders and the Germans. Your force is closest to the Rumanian capital of Bucharest. You must rush into the city and clear it of any enemy. Moskva does not care who gets shot. Just make sure we are in possession of Bucharest as soon as possible. Watch out for still retreating Germans in the countryside. Also the Germans might plan to send reinforcements to the city by air. You will be supported by Rumanian units that have switched sides. It is a confusing time, but you must succeed.<br><br>I should warn you that you are close to the Bulgarian border. We are not in war with Bulgaria though the country is allied to Germany. You have orders not to cross the Danube and leave the Bulgarians for what they are. On later date Moskva will decide what we will do with Bulgaria.  Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7, "support": [8, 13]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61, "support": [13]}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["rcamprus.xml", "Ruse", "25. RUSE (8 September 1944)<br><br>While the front against the fascists moves west, into Yugoslavia, Hungary, Czechoslovakia and Poland, your force will used in a special mission. Bulgaria and our Soviet Union have never been in war. However the Bulgarians sided with the German fascists. Three days ago we have declared war on Bulgaria. Bulgaria still had German troops on its soil. The Bulgarian Army has been given orders not to fire on our troops. However like in the Rumanian Army there are still fascists in their lines and they will fire back. It is also possible that some units have not received the order. It is a confusing situation again. <br><br>Your force, located near Bucharest, must cross the Danube River at two of its crossings. Near Ruse and near Turlukai. After the crossing you must drive deep into Bulgaria and take control of all important positions. Be aware of fascist, resisting troops, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 8}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61}], "eqp-basekorp" ],
["rcampsof.xml", "Sofia", "26. SOFIA (12 September 1944)<br><br>The last days, we have not encountered heavy resistance. Most of the Bulgarian Army is deployed in occupied territories in Greece and Yugoslavia. With the sign of our invasion, fascist leaders have ordered some loyal units to come back and defend the Bulgarian capital of Sofia against a Red invasion. The Red Army must help its comrades in Sofia who are supressed by fascists and take control of the city and its vicinity. Bulgarian proletarian partisans might help you during your advance. There are no signs of German fascists in the area, but watch our for some loyal crack Bulgarian fascists. Good luck, comrade.", [{"id": 1, "country": 8}], [{"id": 0, "country": 61, "support": [8]}], "eqp-basekorp"],
["Red Star Over China (1927-1949)"],
["mao1.xml", "Nanchang Uprising", "Nanchang Uprising<br><br>1-8-1927, Nanchang, Jiangxi, SE China.<br><br>[Your speech to your men before the action]<br><br>Brave soldiers under my command!  The so-called ''united front'' with the Kuomingtan is over.  Today we will join the revolution against the ancient oppressors of the Chinese people and against the likes of Chiang-Kai-Shek.  Some of our comrades in other army units will also join us in our glorious uprising against the enemies of the people.  They are just now coming here to help us in the assault on the old city of Nanchang!  The end of the oppression, the capitalism, and the humiliations begins here on the West bank of the Gan River!  We are surrounded by the local warlords KMT troops, but our comrades will attack them from different directions, and the victory will be ours!<br><br>Men long live the revolution!<br><br>[Applause from the crowd..]", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao2.xml", "Autumn Harvest Uprising", "Autumn Harvest Uprising<br><br>7-9-1927, Changsha, Hunan, South-Central China.<br><br>The uprising at Guangzhou against the local warlords was successful and access by sea for Soviet aid was secured.  Now, comrade Mao from Hunan is planning an assault on the city fortress of Changsha against the local warlords and KMT troops placed at that city. The central Chinese Communist Party director dislikes this operation, but we are going to dispatch your troops there to help our comrades in the offensive.  Personally, I don't want the prestige of Mao Zedong to overly influence the ChCP.  He seems to gain more power each day.<br><br>Yun qi!", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao3.xml", "Jiangxi Soviet", "KMT Anihilation Campaign<br><br>10-11-1930, Jinggangshan mountains, Jiangxi, SE China.<br><br>Comrade Mao has established a \"Soviet Commune'' here in the Jinggangshan Mountains.  It is well protected and hidden from our enemies by a heavy wilderness and bamboo trees.  All the access points to our base are under continuous servalance and our Soviet GRU spies report that the Kuomingtan enemies and the Warlords are planning to eradicate us at once.  They are supported by German advisors who think the best way to eliminate us from here is the so-called strategy ''ferocious walls''.  They are blocking our exits by constructing blockhouses.  We will resist their attacks as long as possible.  Mao thinks we will leave here soon and go North which is much closer to the Soviet border.<br><br>Our Soviet advisors suggest that we let the enemy troops pass through the mountains and then annihilate them on a familiar battlefield.<br><br>Yu qi.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao4.xml", "Long March - Luding Bridge", "Long March - Luding Bridge<br><br>29-5-1935, Luding, Sichuan, Central China.<br><br>Welcome again commander.  We have escaped from Jingghanshan in our long march to the North.  Today the Dadu River lies in front of us, and your task is to cross that river.  The problem is, we have in front the city of Luding, which is in the hands of the local pro-KMT Warlord Liu Wenhui.  I see the chains bridge over the Dadu River is on fire, but our long march can't be stopped!  Go ahead soldier!<br><br>[Historically the crossing of the Dadu River by the chains bridge on fire is just a legend.  During the 80's, some PRC sources admitted the ChCP troops crossed the bridge without too many problems because the local warlord willingness of fight was not very high... like most other warlords.]", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao5.xml", "Pingxingguan Pass", "Pingxingguan Pass<br><br>25-9-1937, Pingxingguan Pass, near Datong, Northern China.<br><br>As you know, we have signed an alliance with our former enemies, the nationalists.  Now, the enemy is the foreign imperialist invader, it's time to forget our quarrel with the KMT for a while.  We are united with them against a common enemy: the Japanese Empire.  While the KMT troops are dealing with the Japanese armies in other parts of China, our guerrillas have been surrounded by the enemy advance in Manchuria and other many places in Northern China, and you (yes, you), a veteran ChCP commander will show the dirty invaders a bit of the people's revolution power.  We must harass the Japanese rearguard as much as possible without taking too many losses.  I'm sure the current KMT-ChCP alliance will not long too much longer.<br><br>This is your duty commander; the 5th Japanese division is driving south towards the Pingxingguan Pass. You must block their path, and then, annihilate all the Japanese, using your famous guerrilla tactics.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao5_2.xml", "100 Regiments Offensive", "100 Regiments Offensive<br><br>1-11-1940, Shanzi, North-Central China<br><br>Again, the central committee of the ChCP has agreed to launch another guerrilla assault on the Japanese rearguard in co-operation with our Kuomingtan ''allies''.  Comrade Mao dislikes this attack, but China is calling for Chinese action against the invaders, and that's what we are going to carry out.  The main objectives must be the capture of enemy resources present in your area: the coal mines and factories.  Your battle plan includes some cities and don't forget to cut all enemy lines of communication.<br><br>Act as quick as possible, the Japanese are going to use all available means to defeat any try to stop their penetration into China.<br><br>Fu qi!", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao6.xml", "Central Plains Breakout", "Central Plains Breakout<br><br>22-6-1946, Wuhan, Hubei province.<br><br>Nice to see you again... I hope the lessons you have reciently taken in the USSR about the modern warfare will be useful for us now. Well, please sit down, I have some information to bring you about the current situation.<br><br>As you know, the Soviet victory agaisnt the Japanese in Manchuria the past year has opened the gate of the regular support of hardware and weapons to us. Now, the ChCP troops are better equipped and trained. The Soviets have given us some Japanese captured equipment from Manchuria, like tanks and artillery and the Japanese prisoners are training our brave men. They had no choice: work in Siberia or work with us!.<br><br>However, it's still soon to enjoy our new training and equipment... the bad news?, well the mission of the US general George Marshall to pacificate China and reach an agreement between us and the KMT is a clear failure. The Kuomingtan have taken advantage of the time just to rearm their units, and now they are clearly taking positions around our areas, probably to anihilate us like in the 30's. In case of the outbreak of the war... your mission is to drive your units in Wuhan to the West, to join the central ChCP units in Central China.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao7.xml", "Linjiang Campaign", "Linjiang Campaign<br><br>8-3-1947, Jilin Province, NE China.<br><br>Congratulations on your promotion to commander of our reciently created People's Liberation Army!. Your actions were enough to support your upgrade decided in the ChCP council... Mao Zedong it's also pleased with you as PLA's general.<br><br>Your first assignment as PLA's commander will be in the Jilin province, our base there is placed at Linjiang. The situation in Manchuria is complex. We need Manchuria for some reasons, first, it's border is close with the USSR and the support we are receiving from the Soviets, and second, Manchuria is the most industrialised area in the whole China, we need the resources from here, and we need to avoid the profits the Kuomingtang can get from here.<br><br>General, deploy your forces along the front lines we have reached in the past months. Be careful, the lines are not safe; althought we are near to Jilin, Changchun and Siping, the KMT forces still keep a strong attack axis near to our base at Linjiang. The mission will be a complete success if you can besiege Changchun and Jilin, and stop the KMT's assault on Linjiang, GRU spies reports our enemies will also try to recapture the section of the Beijing-Changchun railroad, which is also now our main supply line, protect it at any costs!<br><br>Fu qi!.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao8.xml", "Summer Offensive 1947", "Summer Offensive 1947<br><br>16-5-47, Jilin Province, NE China.<br><br>Orders from the central ChCP comitte: it's time to capture Changchun, Siping, and Jilin to complete the conquest of Manchuria. The success on this offensive is extremely important, because it would allow us to undertake further penetrations on to Beijing and Nanjing in the next months.<br><br>It won't be easy, the nationalists still have good units with good equipment, but we count on your elite units to deal with the Kuomingtan troops. The planned Summer Offensive must be victorious.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao9.xml", "Winter Offensive 1947", "Winter Offensive<br><br>1-12-1947 Liaoning Province, NE China.<br><br>The KMT troops are badly wounded.  Our victories at Changchun and Siping have decimated their men, commander, and you must put an end to the nationalist resistance in Manchuria.  Your mission is to secure the communications between our base at Siping and our groups in the South, near to Shenyang.  Then you must take Shenyang.  It is the historical Manchurian capital and is both an important industrial and political center.  The capture of Shenyang will open the way to Beijing and Nanjing.<br><br>I don't think the snow and the bad weather conditions of the Manchurian Winter will be a major problem for you.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15}], [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao11.xml", "Pyongyang Liberation [Korean War]", "Pyongyang Liberation [Korean War]<br><br>25-11-1950 Chongchon River, near the Chinese border.<br><br>Nice to see you again commander. Your next mission is highly secret and will take you to the Sino-Korean border.  The dirty North American invaders and their South Korean allies have smashed the North Koreans.  Kim-Il-Sung was close to a total victory during the past summer, but he didn't protect his rearguard and as you know, the capitalist operation at Inch'on and Seoul has completely defeated the North Korean advance on Pusan.<br><br>We can't allow this situation; the capitalist unification of Korea must not be completed.  A capitalist state in Korea would be like a gun aimed at the People's Republic of China, and we know that the puny North American general McArthur has maintained some conversations with Chaing-Kai-Shek about a possible continuation of the war against us.<br><br>Build your army, and cross the Yalu River to help the North Koreans and strike the UN forces.  Liberate Pyongyang to allow further advances to the 38 parallel and beyond.  We will have help from the air from our recently created People's Liberation Army Air Force. Remember all the principles of the People's War doctrine on your way.<br><br>Fu qi, commander.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao12.xml", "Chosin Reservoir [Korean War]", "Chosin Reservoir [Korean War]<br><br>27-11-1950 Chosin Reservoir, N of North Korea.<br><br>Your quick advance has created a salient in the enemy lines, like the one at the Chosin Reservoir.  This sector is protected by a North American division.  Your task is to make a surprise attack from two different directions and destroy the entire enemy division.  Be careful, our spies report that it's a crack division and they have air support from an improvised airstrip near the reservoir.  Air reinforcements are on the way.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao13.xml", "Hungnam Pocket [Korean War]", "Hungnam Pocket [Korean War]<br><br>11-12-1950, Hungnam, North Korea.<br><br>Again, your smashing attack has left the enemy forces on the ground isolated.  This is the situation at Hungnam.  The UN forces are surrounded from the North and South by us while the North Korean units will attack from the East.  However, the Hungnam port continues to be their main lifeline, supported by their overwhelming naval power.<br><br>Your mission is to reach the port of Hungnam while destroying all enemy forces along your way.  You must stop any UN evacuation as soon as possible.  A successful evacuation will be a victory for them.  The 2nd, 6th and 10th North Korean divisions (the 2nd Korean People's Army) will be under your direct command and the 20th PLA will arrive from the South as reinforcements.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao13_2.xml", "UN Counterattack [Korean War]", "Seoul: UN Counterattack<br><br>Seoul, beyond the 38th Paralell, near to the former DMZ.<br><br>25-1-1951<br><br>The lightning advances of December and early January provide us with the opportunity to easily retake Seoul for the North Koreans.  However, the situation is becoming dangerous.  Our supply lines to China are long and are constantly being bombed and strafed by the UN air force.  Because of this they are preparing a counterattack to again liberate Seoul.  Our Korean spies have told us that a great number of troops are concentrating South of Suwon, including modern tanks and heavy artillery.<br><br>Be careful, our troops are nearly exhausted due to the quick advances in the past months. Your mission is to protect Seoul at all costs and if possible defeat the capitalist advance.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao14.xml", "Spring Offensive [Korean War]", "Spring Offensive [Korean War]<br><br>22-4-1951 Seoul, near the 38th Paralell.<br><br>It's time to go back to Seoul.  We have deployed a large number of PLA and KPA units Northwards toward Seoul and with your armies nothing will stop us in our drive.  The South Korean capital must be in our hands again.<br><br>The UN forces have massed their units to protect their silly so-called ''No-Named line''.  Anyway, this situation fits perfectly with our People's War doctrine.  Launch your armies and over run the dirty capitalist's invaders on your way to recapture Seoul.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [18, 22, 73]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao14_2.xml", "Pusan Revisited [Korean War]", "Pusan Revisited<br><br>27-6-1951 Pusan, South Korea<br><br>Just like last year, the UN forces are again encircled on the ''Pusan Perimeter''.  Now, with the bulk of the North Korean forces are guarding the rear, we can assault the enemy positions without the fear of an assault on our back like last years landings at Inch'on.<br><br>You have one mission; destroy the remnants of the capitalist forces.  Otherwise, they will receive more reinforcements and support from their stronghold at Pusan.  Quick drive them into the sea and Korea will become the unified Korean People's Republic.", [{"id": 1, "country": 9, "support": [3, 18, 22]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [25]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao15.xml", "Taiwan Strait - Nuclear Crisis", "Taiwan Strait - Nuclear Crisis<br><br>1-9-1953, Sea of China.<br><br>I hope you had enough rest from your participation on the Korean War.  As one of the heroes of the PRC the High Command of the PLA has a new mission for you.  The new North American government has retired the fleet that was guarding the Taiwan Strait.  This is the opportunity we have been waiting for; the assault on the rebel province of Taiwan.  You must end the existence of the KMT and its leader, Chiang-Kai-Shek.<br><br>Embark your units in Tianjing and reach the Taiwanese coast as soon as possible.  Beijing is sure the UN will take part in operations like in Korea, this time supporting the KMT in Taiwan.  Your highest priority is the conquest of Taipei.  With this city we will complete the unification of all the Chinese territories.", [{"id": 1, "country": 15, "support": [9]}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["mao16.xml", "Sino - Soviet Incident", "Sino - Soviet Incident<br><br>1-10-1955, Amur river, Sino-Soviet border, near Khabarovsk, Far Eastern Siberia.<br><br>A chain of unfortunate incidents with the Soviets along the Chinese - Soviet border has opened the way for the outbreak of full scale military operations.  As you know, the relationship with our former Soviet allies has badly deteriorated.  Moscow doesn't like our own interpretation of Marxism and wants to take us back to the ''correct'' communist system.  To punish us, they have launched an invasion across the Amur River, the natural border between the PRC and the USSR.  They have captured a many square kilometers of Chinese territory, including some villages.<br><br>You are the commander of the best units in the whole PLA, and your mission is to counter-strike the Soviet invaders.  If we want to continue with our own interpretation of the Marxism, we must defeat the Soviets.  Also Mao would be most pleased, if your men capture the important city of Khabarovsk.  He says that these territories are historically Chinese and no soviets must remain on Chinese lands! <br><br>Fu qi!", [{"id": 1, "country": 89}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233}], "eqp-olgww2" ],
["mao17.xml", "Great Leap Forward", "Great Leap Forward<br><br>1-12-1955, Beijing.<br><br>Private Tovarich!  Nice to see you again.  It has been a while since our last meeting at Khabarovsk.  It was a shame to lose the battle against you, but now we can re-negotiate the conditions of the peace treaty.  This is Top Secret and I hope you have told no one of our plans.  As our men from the KGB have told you, we are ready to support you, if you finally decide to undertake a coup against Mao Zedong and his reformed communism.  It is literally destroying China.  We need to take China back to the right and true communist way.  We think you and your so-called ''Gang of Four'' are the perfect team to take down the Maoist system and that destructive plan named ''Great Leap Forward''.  That woman of your gang, ''Madame Mao'' can be very useful in the near future, when you will need to destroy the political image of Mao.<br><br>This is the plan we suggest; in the past month the units under your direct management have been deployed on the coast of the Sea of China in preparation for the Coup.   We are ready to support you by sea.  The Chinese navy will remain loyal to Mao, but it is not powerful enough to deal with a minor Soviet submarine unit.  After we secure the entire coast by taking Tanggu, you must launch the counterattack against the government loyalist units which surely will be sent to defeat our plans.  Take the Tanggu airfield as soon as possible as this will allow us to send you reinforcements by air.  Our planes will be painted with the PRC symbols.  You must avoid the Americans as we don't need any problems with them now.  The incident should be only between Chinese forces.<br><br>The last stand will be Beijing, this won't be easy, as you know, the best PLA units are deployed there.  The price maybe high, but it deserves a try.  You can become the new premier of the People's Republic of China!<br><br>Udachi tovarich!", [{"id": 1, "country": 233}], [{"id": 0, "country": 233, "support": [89]}], "eqp-olgww2"],
["The Great Patriotic War USSR Campaign (1942-1945)"],
["ruscam00.xml", "Operation Uranus", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. The time for retreating is over, now we must drive the fascist beasts from the soil of the Motherland! Now we began with Operation Uranus here on the Chir. The wider stakes are clear: The Soviet 21st Army and 5th Tank Army were able to capture some 27,000 Romanian prisoners—the bulk of three divisions— and then continue their advance southwards. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 13, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam01.xml", "Operation Saturn", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Now is the time to crush the Italians. General Fyodor Isidorovich Kuznetsov's 1st Guards Army and General Dmitri Danilovich Lelyushenko's 3rd Guards Army attacked from the north, encircling 130,000 soldiers of the Italian 8th Army on the Don and advancing to Millerovo. (Manstein sent the 6th Panzer Division to the Italians' aid of the 130,000 encircled troops, 45,000 survived to join the Panzers at Chertkovo on 17 January). Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{'country': 12, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam02.xml", "Magyar Massacre", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Clear the Highway of Hungarians and break their line of communications and reinforcement in support of our attack in the south on Rostov and Kharkov. On January 13, 1943, Soviet forces, overwhelming in numbers and equipment, began the Voronezh-Kharkov Strategic Offensive Operation on the Bryansk, Voronezh, and Southwestern Fronts simultaneously. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 4, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam03.xml", " During Operation Star", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. We have swung you around to the north now, a little more now and we liberate Izium, we must drive on, drive the point of the sword through and gut the Fascist beast. As the German Sixth Army was encircled in Stalingrad, the Red Army undertook a series of wider offensives against the rest of Army Group South. The wider stakes are clear: These culminated on 2 January 1943, when the Soviets launched Operation Star, which between January and early February broke German defenses and led to the Soviet recapture of Kharkov, Belgorod and Kursk. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam04.xml", "Kursk", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Here at Prokhorovka you have been attached to the 5th Guards Tank Army, this will not be easy Comrade General. Directly facing you is the elite of the SS: Adolf Hitler's named Liebstandarte Division and Das Reich in the south. The wider stakes are clear: Regardless of the tactical outcome, the Battle of Prokhorovka was turned into a critical propaganda and operational victory for the Red Army. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam05.xml", "Orel Counter Offensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Here is our counter stroke to the German operations aimed at Kursk, it is to break through at Karachev and destroy this fortified salient around Orel. Beware the Fortresses at both Orel and Bryansk are fortified with heavy artillery, invest these fortresses and we shall move west. The wider stakes are clear: Operation Kutuzov set the stage for the liberation of Smolensk in September 1943. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam06.xml", "Krivoi Rog", "There is nowhere left to yield: hold this ground and make the enemy pay for every hex. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. On 17 October Konev attacked out of his bridgehead at Kremenchug and swung to the south toward the iron ore center at Krivoi Rog and the main rail line into the Dnepr bend from the west. This threat forced the Germans to give up Dnepropetrovsk, but the First Panzer Army was able to hold in front of Krivoi Rog. The wider stakes are clear: While the attack seemed of little value, it did force the Germans back, even further from the Dnepr and any territory freed, meant a better hope for life to the civilians there. Use terrain, entrenchment, and supporting fire to survive the first blow—then punish every exposed formation.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam07.xml", "Crossing Kiev", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Kiev has languished for too long under Nazi rule, they impatiently await your liberation. Nobody has said this will be easy, undoubtedly the Germans will throw much strength into the defence of the city in their fortress ideology. The wider stakes are clear: On the morning of 3 November 1943, the 4th Panzer Army awoke to a massive Soviet bombardment. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam08.xml", "Zhitomir Halt", "The campaign has reached a point where speed matters as much as firepower. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Taking Zhitomir will cut communications between Army Groups North and South, the 25th Panzer Division under General Jauer is counter-attacking here reinforced by Fallschirmjagers. The first unit to arrive from 48th Panzer Corps was the newly formed 25th Panzer Division commanded by General der Panzertruppen Georg Jauer, on 7 November. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam09.xml", "Iasi Invasion", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. STAVKA feels that the whole Romanian army here can be brought down with a few hard blows, your mission is to apply those blows here at Iasi. The First Jassy-Kishinev Offensive, was fought between 8 April and 6 June 1944 by the Soviets and Axis powers of World War II. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 13, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam10.xml", "Operation Bagration", "A narrow window has opened in the enemy line; turn it into a strategic rupture. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Three years ago, the fascists invaded Mother Russia causing untold suffering to the Soviet people. Today on the 3rd anniversary of that hateful day, we begin the final Operation to drive them from our soil, Operation Bagration shall be their crescendo of doom. The wider stakes are clear: Bobruisk was liberated on June 29, the German 383rd Infantry Division commencing withdrawal towards dawn: no further elements of Ninth Army would escape from east of the Berezina. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam11.xml", "Minsk Offensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Here at Minsk the Germans have little chance of reinforcement before you surround them and destroy their Festung. With this action we will completely encircle their 4th Army from the north. The wider stakes are clear: In total, around 100,000 troops from Fourth and Ninth Armies were caught in the encirclement, of whom some 40,000 were killed, most of the remainder being captured. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam12.xml", "Vilnius Offensive", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Chernyakhovsky ordered that his main mobile 'exploitation' forces, the 5th Guards Tank Army and 3rd Guards Cavalry Corps continue their advance from Minsk on July 5 in the direction of Vilnius, with the aim of reaching the city by the following day: they were to encircle Vilnius from the south and north respectively. The rifle divisions of 5th Army were ordered to follow and close up to them. The wider stakes are clear: Without the traffic network based on Vilnius, the German position in the northern Baltics was untenable. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam13.xml", "The Gates of Warsaw", "The enemy has filled the approaches with strongpoints, but the city beyond them is the campaign's prize. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. After the Soviet reconnaissance units reached Warsaw in late July, on August 1, 1944 the Warsaw Uprising started. Starting from an area south of Minsk Mazowiecki, Lieutenant-General N. D. Vedeneev's 3rd Tank Corps (part of the Soviet Second Tank Army) thrust northwest through Okuniew and Wolomin to Radzymin, reaching an area only three miles (five kilometers) from the strategic bridge over the Narew River at Zegrze. The wider stakes are clear: Between August 1 and August 10, 1944 at the conclusion of the Belorussian strategic offensive operation near the town of Radzymin in the vicinity of Warsaw, part of which entailed a large tank battle at Wolomin.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam14.xml", "Debrecen", "The battle is already turning against you; survival now depends on discipline, not glory. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Cavalry-Mechanized Group Pliyev is in danger of being cut off at Nyiregyhaza, your Corps has been attached to the 6th Guards Tank Army and will attack north from Debrecen in order to relieve Cavalry Mechanized Group Pliyev. Holding Nyiregyhaza will cut off the escape route of the German 8th Army. The wider stakes are clear: The Debrecen operation saw Soviet forces advance anywhere from 60 to 120 miles further west into Hungary, leaving the 2nd and 3rd Ukrainian Fronts in position to renew the offensive towards Budapest. Keep the route open, rescue what can still be saved, and deny the enemy the encirclement it expects.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam15.xml", "Budapest Offensive", "The enemy has filled the approaches with strongpoints, but the city beyond them is the campaign's prize. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. On 29 October 1944, the Red Army started its offensive against the city of Budapest. More than 1,000,000 men split into two operating maneuver groups rushed towards the city. The wider stakes are clear: While this destroyed most of the German forces in the region, troops were rushed from the Western Front and, in March, the Germans launched the ill fated Operation Spring Awakening (Unternehmen Fruhlingserwachen) in the Lake Balaton area. Use artillery and infantry together, isolate strongpoints, and avoid wasting elite units in unsupported assaults.", [{'country': 4, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam16.xml", "East Prussian Offensive", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. The main thrust of the offensive will be conducted by the 3rd Belorussian Front under Chernyakhovsky. Your forces are tasked with driving westwards towards Konigsberg, against the defensive positions of Third Panzer Army and Fourth Army, the northern armies of General Georg-Hans Reinhardt's Army Group Center. The wider stakes are clear: The last elements were cleared from Pillau on April 25 in the Zemland offensive operation. Break the defence before reserves arrive, keep your spearheads supplied, and turn tactical success into an operational collapse.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam17.xml", "Stargard tank battle", "The road ahead is defended, yet a decisive blow here can unhinge the entire front. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. Operation Solstice (German: Unternehmen Sonnenwende), also known as Unternehmen Husarenritt or the 'Stargard tank battle', was a German armoured offensive operation on the Eastern Front, one of the last such operations. It was repulsed by the Red Army, but helped to convince the Soviet High Command to postpone the planned attack on Berlin. The wider stakes are clear: German forces failed to penetrate towards Kustrin and suffered major losses of heavy equipment in the subsequent retreat. Concentrate your best units, protect the flanks of the advance, and seize the decisive objectives before the enemy can rebuild a line.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam18.xml", "Seelow Heights", "The initiative is yours, but the enemy will not remain disorganized for long. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. In the early hours of 16 April, the offensive began with a massive bombardment by thousands of artillery pieces and Katyushas. Well before dawn, the 1st Belorussian Front attacked across the Oder and the 1st Ukrainian Front attacked across the Neisse. The wider stakes are clear: However, the Soviet forces led by Zhukov eventually broke through the defensive positions, having suffered about 30,000 casualties, while the Germans lost 12,000 personnel. Momentum is your greatest asset: pause too long and a breakthrough becomes another costly frontal battle.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["ruscam19.xml", "The Last Battle: Berlin", "A city is not captured in a single blow; it is taken district by district under smoke and fire. The Soviet counteroffensive is gathering force. On the walls of the houses we saw Goebbels' appeals, hurriedly scrawled in white paint: 'Every German will defend his capital. Steel pillboxes, barricades, mines, traps, suicide squads with grenades clutched in their hands all are swept aside before the tidal wave. The wider stakes are clear: At 02:41 on the morning of 7 May 1945, at the SHAEF headquarters, German Chief-of-Staff General Alfred Jodl signed the unconditional surrender documents for all German forces to the Allies. The city rewards combined arms and patience; reckless attacks will leave your best formations buried in rubble.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["Soviet Counter-Offensive Campaign (1942-1946)"],
["rcampx01.xml", "Operation Uranus", "Stalingrad is burning, but the German Sixth Army has finally pushed itself into a trap. As Zhukov, coordinate the blow that will close Operation Uranus: smash the Axis flanks, cut the roads across the Don and Chir, and prevent relief forces from reopening the corridor to Paulus. The Romanian armies are brittle, yet German armour and air power can still punish a careless advance. Break through quickly, preserve your mobile formations for exploitation, and turn the defence of Stalingrad into the encirclement that changes the course of the war.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx02.xml", "Operation Saturn", "The Stalingrad pocket is sealed, but the wider Axis front on the Don has not yet collapsed. Italian formations, fortified western approaches, and a strongly defended central airfield block the next stage of the counteroffensive. Strike before the enemy can recover from Operation Uranus, destroy the Italian Eighth Army’s cohesion, and open the road toward Millerovo and Rostov. A rapid victory will expand the encirclement and deny Manstein the forces he needs for a relief attempt. Use armour for depth, not merely for the first line, and keep the winter advance moving.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx03.xml", "The Road to Rostov", "The Chir and Don crossings are heavily guarded, and German aircraft are already moving east to reinforce the threatened sector. Your task is to rupture the river line, seize the bridges, and create the deployment space required for the advance on Rostov. The enemy expects the rivers to slow you long enough for reserves to arrive; prove that expectation fatal. Concentrate artillery on a narrow front, force the crossings under cover, and exploit immediately with mobile units before the defensive network can be rebuilt.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx04.xml", "Airstrike Rostov", "Rostov is the gateway to the Caucasus, but the assault cannot begin until several tactical deployment sites are secured around the city. Reconnaissance reports limited defenders and little air cover—an opportunity that will vanish as soon as the enemy understands your intention. Advance with speed, seize the staging areas intact, and protect the corridors through which the main army must follow. This is a preparation battle in which every turn saved matters: the better your opening position, the less costly the coming struggle for Rostov will be.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx05.xml", "Rostov", "Rostov has been reinforced by the Wiking Panzer Division, including heavy Tigers, anti-tank batteries, cavalry, and local air support. The enemy intends to turn the city into a shield for the Caucasus withdrawal and a fortress on the Don. Use reconnaissance to identify the heavy armour, isolate the strongest positions, and attack the city from more than one direction. A frontal rush will burn away your tank strength; combined arms and careful encirclement can instead trap the defenders and open the southern road toward the Crimea.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx06.xml", "Sevastopol", "Sevastopol stands behind coastal guns, prepared urban defences, and incoming airborne reinforcements. Soviet marines, naval forces, aircraft, and paratroopers have already secured footholds around the fortress, but the final assault must be coordinated before Axis help arrives across the Black Sea. Suppress the batteries, protect the landing zones, and break into the city without allowing the defenders to concentrate against a single approach. The capture of Sevastopol will restore a vital base and place the entire Crimean coast within reach.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx07.xml", "Northwest to Odessa", "The road north from Sevastopol appears lightly held, but scattered Axis units and reconnaissance aircraft can still delay the movement toward Odessa. Treat these skirmishes as an operational race: clear the route, preserve fuel and ammunition, and prevent isolated enemy groups from cutting your columns or reporting their strength. Your army must arrive at the next battlefield organised rather than exhausted. A clean pursuit will keep the Black Sea initiative in Soviet hands and ensure that the heavy guns waiting farther west face a concentrated army, not a string of vulnerable detachments.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx08.xml", "Odessa", "Odessa is protected by dense anti-tank positions, heavy artillery, Italian naval elements, and two formidable railway guns. The enemy has prepared the coastal approaches to punish armour and delay any direct assault, but Soviet naval gunfire and bomber support are becoming available. Neutralise the long-range batteries, secure the shoreline, and open safe lanes for infantry and tanks to enter the city. This is a combined-arms siege: victory depends on using sea, air, artillery, and ground forces as a single system rather than feeding units into the fortifications piecemeal.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx09.xml", "German Counterattack Kharkov", "Kursk has been liberated, but German forces are regrouping around Kharkov under experienced commanders and have shot down the aircraft sent to examine their positions. You must advance with incomplete intelligence against a city that has changed hands before and will be defended by armour, artillery, and mobile reserves. Probe carefully, secure the approaches, and avoid exposing your spearheads to a prepared counterstroke. Take Kharkov, break the enemy’s ability to stabilise the front, and clear the way toward the Dnieper operations that will follow.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx10.xml", "To Kiev - But First Kanev", "German and Romanian remnants are holding Kanev to protect the approaches to Kiev and the Dnieper crossings. The visible garrison appears small, but Luftwaffe activity has blinded reconnaissance along the river and hidden whatever reserves wait beyond the city limits. Seize the crossings, eliminate the holdouts, and establish a secure bridgehead before the main battle for Kiev begins. Speed is important, but a careless river assault could leave your formations divided on opposite banks. Take Kanev cleanly and give the armies converging on Kiev a firm southern anchor.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx11.xml", "Kiev", "The battle for Kiev is already under way. Konev, Malinovsky, and Vatutin are attacking from the north and centre while your force approaches from the south through uncertain terrain and hostile air cover. Your role is to reinforce the encirclement, seize the southern crossings, and prevent the garrison from escaping or receiving relief. Kiev is too large for a single thrust: isolate districts, coordinate armour with infantry, and keep supply routes across the river open. Liberate the city without allowing the battle to consume the army needed for the advance beyond Ukraine.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx12.xml", "Belgrade Liberation", "With Kiev secured, Romanian resistance around Belgrade threatens the flank and communications of the wider Soviet advance. Enemy tanks, anti-tank guns, and mixed Axis units defend the approaches, while damaged airfields must be captured before your own aviation can operate effectively. Clear the region, seize the bases, and eliminate the possibility of a counterattack from the south. This operation is less spectacular than Berlin, but strategically essential: leave an enemy force behind you and every supply column moving toward Poland will remain in danger.", [{'country': 13, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx13.xml", "Poland", "The armies driving through Poland are waiting for your formation on the south-eastern sector of the front. Luftwaffe patrols have destroyed reconnaissance aircraft, but airborne reinforcements are prepared to seize advanced positions and accelerate the junction. Break through the remaining German screen, protect the drop zones, and connect your force with the neighbouring Soviet armies before the enemy can defeat either element separately. Success will complete the concentration for the final advance to the Oder; delay will give Berlin precious time to fortify its approaches.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx14.xml", "The Road to Berlin", "The Oder line is the last great operational barrier before Berlin. Enemy troops are scattered around the approaches, city limits are heavily armed, and surprise detachments wait beyond the areas visible to reconnaissance. Secure the crossings, destroy isolated strongpoints, and bring your army into position before the Western Allies can reach the German capital first. The defenders are depleted but still dangerous, especially where anti-tank guns and urban terrain can halt Soviet armour. Open the road to Berlin and preserve enough strength for the battles inside the city.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx15.xml", "The Battle of Berlin", "Berlin is surrounded, but the Luftwaffe and dense anti-aircraft defences have forced Soviet reconnaissance out of the city. The enemy has converted streets, rail yards, government buildings, and hidden arsenals into a layered defensive system whose true strength remains uncertain. Drive into the capital, divide the garrison, and seize the crossings before the defenders can shift reserves between sectors. Expect ambushes, heavy anti-tank fire, and close urban combat. This is not yet the Reichstag assault—it is the battle to make that final objective reachable.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx16.xml", "The Fall of the Reichstag", "The Reichstag has become the last symbol and one of the strongest fortresses in Berlin. Its defenders possess more ammunition, anti-tank weapons, and heavy artillery than intelligence predicted, while barricades and firing positions have appeared overnight. Reduce the surrounding blocks, isolate the building, and bring infantry and engineers forward under concentrated fire support. Do not squander tanks against hidden guns in the streets. Take the Reichstag, raise the red banner over the centre of German power, and end the European war with a victory worthy of the losses that brought you here.", [{'country': 7, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx17.xml", "Berlin Standoff", "The guns have barely fallen silent when the alliance begins to fracture. Soviet engineers fortify the eastern sector of Berlin while American, British, and French troops face them across a tense line of demarcation. Orders are to hold ground and avoid opening fire—but an unexpected Allied attack turns occupation into a new battlefield. Stabilise the sector, protect the approaches to East Berlin, and decide whether this clash remains local or becomes the opening shot of another war. Every unit lost now will matter if negotiations fail completely.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx18.xml", "Conquer Europe?", "Victory over Germany has produced an impossible choice. In this alternate path, Soviet leaders form a new Pact of Steel with former German enemies and Italian forces in order to drive the Western Allies from Europe. British, American, and French armies are retreating toward Dunkirk while German formations secure the northern flank. Commit to the offensive, reorganise a coalition built from yesterday’s enemies, and strike before the evacuation ports can be fortified. The decision taken here abandons historical restraint and opens a campaign of continental conquest.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx19.xml", "Taking of Dunkirk", "The Western Allies are compressed around Dunkirk, but the port remains their gateway to the English Channel. Soviet, German, and Italian forces must break the siege perimeter, seize an airfield and deployment zone, and prevent another evacuation across the water. Naval and air support are available, yet transport capacity is limited and heavy artillery cannot all be moved forward at once. Secure the coast, destroy the remaining bridgehead, and establish the bases required for an invasion of Britain. Failure here will give the Allies time to rebuild behind the Channel.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx20.xml", "English Channel", "Operation Nexus carries the new coalition across the English Channel. British, American, and French forces contest the crossing while Soviet and allied transports struggle to deliver armour, artillery, and paratroopers to the southern coast. Capture an airfield immediately or enemy aircraft will turn the beaches and sea lanes into a graveyard. Then seize the deployment zone, widen the lodgement, and prevent the defenders from containing the invasion. The operation is a race between reinforcement and destruction: establish a functioning bridgehead before the Channel closes behind you.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx21.xml", "Annexation of South England", "The invasion has gained a foothold in southern England, and allied armies are pushing toward London from the north. Your force must annex the southern approaches, secure roads and airbases, and prepare the advance on Windsor. The countryside may appear open, but British reserves can use towns, rivers, and narrow routes to delay heavier formations. Keep the landing areas supplied, prevent local counterattacks from reaching the coast, and build a continuous front. A swift southern advance will close the first half of the ring around the British capital.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx22.xml", "Windsor 1946", "Windsor is heavily fortified and stands between your southern army and the encirclement of London. German units have reached the north-eastern outskirts while paratroopers and advance detachments hold scattered tactical positions inside the metropolitan area. Exploit identified gaps, secure the airborne landing zones, and break the Windsor defences before British reserves can seal the corridor. The city’s air and ground support remains strong, so every isolated spearhead risks destruction. Take Windsor, connect the encircling forces, and prepare for the final struggle for London.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx23.xml", "London Blitz", "Britain and France have capitulated, and the war crosses the Atlantic. A Soviet-German naval force, supported by submarines, destroyers, aircraft, and landing troops, approaches the Florida coast before American radar detects the deployment. Enemy destroyers and air units guard the objective, but no reinforcements are expected during the opening assault. Win control of the sea, suppress the coastal defence, and seize the first strategic point intact. This is the campaign’s most audacious leap: if the lodgement fails, the ocean will separate the invaders from every source of heavy reinforcement.", [{'country': 22, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx24.xml", "Onward to the USA", "The first American coastal position lies east of Florida, while other coalition armies strike farther north. Your air support will remain limited until an airbase is captured, leaving ships and landing forces exposed during the opening turns. Secure the tactical point, take the airfield, and expand the beachhead before American forces can coordinate a counterattack. Naval gunfire can open the way, but only ground units can hold what has been won. Establish the bridgehead that will carry the war from the Atlantic shore into the American interior.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx25.xml", "Florida Landing", "The Florida landing has succeeded, and the invasion front is moving north. Savannah is strongly fortified, but a captured airbase gives your army access to air and naval support while reinforcements approach from the coast. The city anchors the American southern defence and blocks the route toward Washington. Isolate its fortifications, protect the supply corridor to the beaches, and coordinate bombardment with a deliberate ground assault. Take Savannah before the defenders can turn it into a prolonged siege and allow the northern coalition armies to join the advance inland.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx26.xml", "Red Savannah", "Savannah has fallen and the road toward the American capital is opening. Coalition armies are driving south and west from the Atlantic while your force prepares the next stage of the offensive. American resistance is reorganising around key transport routes, industrial centres, and the approaches to Washington. Keep the columns moving, capture airfields and supply hubs, and prevent the defenders from forming a continuous line. This is the final operational advance of the campaign: every intact unit and every turn saved will strengthen the assault on the capital.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["rcampx27.xml", "Washington in Flames", "Washington is the final objective of the impossible war that began at Stalingrad and crossed two oceans. The American capital is defended by surviving regular forces, emergency formations, artillery, and whatever air support can still be assembled. Break the outer defensive ring, secure the Potomac crossings, and fight through the government district without allowing your supply line to collapse behind you. The battle is both military and symbolic: victory ends organised resistance and completes the alternate-history conquest. Commit every veteran formation carefully—there will be no campaign beyond Washington in which to replace them.", [{'country': 9, 'id': 1}], [{'country': 61, 'id': 0}], "eqp-adlerkorps" ],
["Standalone Historical Battles"],
["cubali01.xml", "Sierra Maestra 1958", "Sierra Maestra 1958<br><br>After one year of the first guerrilla actions agaisnt Batista, the power of the cuban rebels leaded by Castro is growing each day. Castro thoughts the land controled by the  M-26-7 movement had to be increased in the Sierra Maestra. However, he didn't know about the Batista intentions to launch a powerful strike on the Sierra, to clear the southern part of Cuba from rebels.<br><br>By Santiago Fuertes 2012 - The Latin Generals. <br>Special Thanks to JML & Paqueo for his tests on this scenario.<br><br>MAP: Sierra Maestra n\u00ba 468<br>EFILE: LG COLD WAR 1.65<br>SOUNDS: CUBA1 & CUBA2", [{"id": 0, "country": 107}], [{"id": 1, "country": 83}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["battle_cuito.xml", "Battle of Cuito Cuanavale (1987)", "Battle of Cuito Cuanavale<br><br>EFILE: OPEN LGCW1.5 or higher<br>MAP: CUITO<br>TYPE: Historical<br>SOUND: AFRICA<br><br>December, 1987<br><br>The FAPLA, the armed wing of the angolan MPLA, the people's party for the liberation of Angola, has launched a strike on the UNITA (the National Union for the Total Independence of Angola, supported by South Africa) positions near the village of Mavinga, in the South-Eastern Angola. However, the intervention of the South African Defense Force became too much for the FAPLA, and soon, the angolan communists found themselves into a desperate withdrawal to seek secure positions behind the Cuito river.<br><br>However, Castro has promised to the angolan movement to increase the current support they are receiving from Cuba. Indeed, a cuban general, Ochoa Sanchez, is managing the operations, and the cubans are preparing some more than sole advisors to be sent to the battlefield. Can the FAPLA/Cuba forces turn the tide?.<br><br>By Santiago Fuertes. 2009, Updated, September 2011<br>The Latin Generals.<br>http://gilestiel.nerim.net/lg/", [{"id": 0, "country": 245}], [{"id": 1, "country": 48}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["amilastc_sfb.xml", "Amin's Last Chance (1979)", "Amin's Last Chance<br><br>March, 1979<br><br>The forces of Uganda supported by airlifted reinforcements from Libya tries to delay the advance of Tanzanian and the rebels of Uganda towards Kampala. <br><br>Conditions of victory: <br><br>- To retain until end 4 hexes for BV <br>- To retain until end 3 hexes for V <br>- To retain until end 2 hexes for TV <br><br>The headquarters of Ugandan president Idi Amin must survive.<br><br>EFILE: Open LGCW 1.0 or higher<br>MAP: KAMPALA<br>TYPE: Historical<br><br>By Santiago Fuertes. 2010, updated September 2011<br>The Latin Generals.<br>http://gilestiel.nerim.net/lg/", [{"id": 1, "country": 297}], [{"id": 0, "country": 296}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["1954_dienbienphu.xml", "1954 Battle of Dien Bien Phu", "1954 Battle of Dien Bien Phu<br>\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af<br>General, you are ordered to launch the final assault on the french stronghold Dien Bien Phu. The french army is trapped in the valley and short of equipment, but still consits of some of their best Forreign Legion units and they even field some tanks, but that won't be enough to stop us!<br><br>Scenario Version: February 2020<br>Scenario Type: Historic<br>Player Country: Viet Minh<br>AI Version: 3.0<br>Player Turn Prestige 25pp/turn<br>Turns: 12 BV; 16 V; 20 TV<br>Scenario Designer: randowe<br><br>ORDERS:<br>\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af<br>Close in on the french strongholds and capture all VHs in 12/16/20 turns for a Brilliant Victory/Victory/Tactical Victory.", [{"id": 0, "country": 77}], [{"id": 1, "country": 6}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["khalkin1.xml", "Khalkhin Gol 1 - Japanese Attack (1939)", "Throughout June, there were continuing reports of Soviet and Mongolian activity on both sides of the river near Nomonhan, and small-scale attacks on isolated Manchukoan units. At the end of the month, the commander of the Japanese 23rd Infantry Division, Lt. Gen. Michitaro Komatsubara, was given permission to \"expel the invaders\". The Japanese plan was for a two-pronged assault. Three regiments plus part of a fourth, including three from the 23rd Division (the 71st and the 72nd Infantry Regiments, plus a battalion of the 64th Infantry Regiment) and the 26th Infantry Regiment under Colonel Shinichiro Sumi, borrowed from the 7th Infantry Division, would advance across the Khalkin Gol, destroy Soviet forces on Baintsagan Hill on the west bank, then make a left turn and advance south to the Kawatama Bridge. The second prong of the attack would be the task of the IJA 1st Tank Corps (1st TC) (Yasuoka Detachment), consisting of the 3rd and 4th Tank Regiments, plus a part of the 64th Infantry Regiment, a battalion from the 28th Infantry Regiment, detached from the 7th Infantry, 24th Engineer Regiment, and a battalion from the 13th Field Artillery Regiment, all under the overall command of Lieutenant General Yasuoka Masaomi. This force would attack Soviet troops on the east bank of the Khalkhyn Gol and north of the Holsten River. The two Japanese thrusts were intending to join together on the wings.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["khalkin2.xml", "Khalkhin Gol 2 - Zhukov's Strike (1939)", "Zhukov decided it was time to break the stalemate.  At 05:45 on 20 August 1939, Soviet artillery and 557 fighters and bombers attacked Japanese positions, the first fighter-bomber offensive in Soviet Air Force history.  Approximately 50,000 Soviet and Mongolian soldiers of the 57th Special Corps defended the east bank of the Khalkhyn Gol. Three infantry divisions and a tank brigade crossed the river, supported by massed artillery and the Soviet Air Force. Once the Japanese were pinned down by the attack of Soviet center units, Soviet armored units swept around the flanks and attacked the Japanese in the rear, achieving a classic double envelopment. When the Soviet wings linked up at Nomonhan village on 25 August, the Japanese 23rd Infantry Division was trapped. On 26 August, a Japanese counterattack to relieve the 23rd Division failed. On 27 August, the 23rd Division attempted to break out of the encirclement, but also failed. When the surrounded forces refused to surrender, they were again hit with artillery and air attacks. By 31 August, Japanese forces on the Mongolian side of the border were destroyed, leaving remnants of the 23rd Division on the Manchurian side. The Soviets had achieved their objective.", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-comww2" ],
["sparta.xml", "Spartacist Uprising - Berlin (1919)", "Spartakusaufstand - Berlin <br><br>January 5, 1919<br><br>General strike in Berlin. The newspaper district in the street \"Kochstra\u00dfe\" is occupied and roadblocks are erected. Negotiations between the government Ebert and the USDP fail - Communist Party under the leadership of Liebknecht calls for armed insurrection. This is the scenario in which you find yourself. <br><br>Revolutionary win the battle for Berlin and sparked such a conflagration? Or bring the brigade Reinhard from north, the \"Freikorps\" from Potsdam and the \"Garde-Kavallerie-Sch\u00fctzen-Division\" from south, the situation in Berlin under control?<br><br>Historically incorrect:<br>- The participation of \"Volksmariendivision\" (was in Berlin - but don't want to fight).<br>- the cavalry Fuerstenwalde and Freienwalde (fictitious forces to compensate).<br><br>20 Turns,<br><br>Scenario designed by M. Kessler", [{"id": 0, "country": 188}], [{"id": 1, "country": 161}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["madrid_36.xml", "Defence of Madrid (1936)", "November-December of 1936. After the coup d'etat of July, the Fascist columns have traveled from Africa and from the North of Spain to make a meeting in Madrid, overruning the capital. However the Rebels are too overconfident; the high morale of the citizens of Madrid and the newly created first Mixed Brigades of the People's Army will be a serious enemy to deal with.<br><br>Select your side and win the battle for Madrid!.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce" ],
["mallorca.xml", "Landing on Mallorca (1936)", "August, 1936. The captain Bayo commands an assault on the island of Mallorca. Could he and his men take the balearic island fron the nationals hans?.", [{"id": 1, "country": 225}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce" ],
["teruel.xml", "Battle of Teruel (1937)", "In the frozen Winter of 1937, the Spanish Nationalist had an important point to continue his offensive: the city of Teruel, as a 'gun aiming to the hearth of the Spanish Levante'. The Spanish Popular Army could not allow this, and an offensive to retake Teruel was planed and launched under temperatures around -28 degrees... <br>The Nationalist Colonel, Rey d'Haucourt surrendered his forces in Teruel, and the city was retaken, but the Rebel counteroffensive converted the battle in a little Spanish Stalingrad...", [{"id": 1, "country": 225}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce" ],
["ebro.xml", "Battle of the Ebro (1938)", "25 July 1938. After the disastrous winter of 1937 and spring of 1938 the Republic \u2014 widely written off as dead abroad \u2014 needed a feat of arms to lift the morale of its people and prove it was still alive.<br><br>With the rebel advance through the Levante unstoppable and driving on Valencia, seat of the Republican government, the Republican high command mounted an operation to cross the river Ebro and fall on the Nationalist rear.<br><br>Despite the crushing rebel superiority in aircraft and artillery \u2014 can the government forces hold the ground they take?", [{"id": 1, "country": 225}], [{"id": 0, "country": 226}], "eqp-gce" ],
["partisanen.xml", "Yugoslav Partisans - Operation Weiss (1943)", "partisan<br><br>04.02.1943<br><br>Partisans makes more and more trouble for the Germans troops. To beend the probelms the german send the mountain Jaeger Regiment. But they will do it?<br><br>Autor: RoadRunner<br><br>Konversion in OG: M. Kessler", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 239}], "eqp-pzliga" ],
["aran.xml", "Val d'Aran Invasion (1944)", "Aran Valley<br><br>In 1944, when the Axis powers were about to fall, some spanish communist exiles formerly part of the french Resistance, were sent to the Pyrenees to cross the spanish - french border and stablish a bridgehead for a possible Allied disembark in Spain, thus, taking down the Franco's government. The operation, supported by the spanish Communist Party ended in a complete failure, can you turn the tide?.<br><br>Autor: Santiago Fuertes   <br><br>Konversion in OG: M. Kessler", [{"id": 1, "country": 234}], [{"id": 0, "country": 91}], "eqp-pzliga" ],
["op_hooper.xml", "Operation Hooper - Cuito Cuanavale (1987)", "Operation Hooper<br><br>EFILE: OPEN LGCW 1.5 or higher<br>MAP: CUITO<br>TYPE: Historical<br>SOUND: WGP.<br><br>December, 1987<br><br>South Africa continues supporting the UNITA guerrillas agaisnt the FAPLA, the armed wing of the communist party of Angola, the MPLA, trying to eliminate the problematic communist goverment of Angola. The affair became into a serious problem near the northern Namibian's border, when the FAPLA began receiving big support from Cuba. Then, the angolans attacked the UNITA positions with 5 brigades heavily equipped with tanks and other weapons of soviet procedence, reaching the vicitinies of the town of Mavinga. Thus, the South African Defense Force sent full support to the UNITA to stop the offensive, and even, take the enemy base at Cuito Cuanavale.<br><br>By Santiago Fuertes. 2009<br>The Latin Generals.<br>http://gilestiel.nerim.net/lg/", [{"id": 0, "country": 245}], [{"id": 1, "country": 48}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["vkampala_sfb.xml", "Victory at Kampala (1979)", "Victory at Kampala<br><br>March, 1979<br><br>The Tanzanian People's Defensa Force supported by the Ugandan opposition invades Uganda with the aim of capturing Kampala and expelling from the power to Idi Amin.<br><br>EFILE: Open LGCW 1.0 or higher<br>MAP: KAMPALA<br>TYPE: Historical<br><br>By Santiago Fuertes. 2010 Updated, September 2011<br>The Latin Generals.<br>http://gilestiel.nerim.net/lg/", [{"id": 0, "country": 297}], [{"id": 1, "country": 296}], "eqp-olgcw" ],
["1920_perekop.xml", "1920 Siege of Perekop", "1920 Siege of Perekop<br>\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af<br>Comrade General, we are now in the position to attack the Isthmus of Perekop and northern Crimea, where Wrangel's White Army has entrenched themselves. Prepare for long and hard fighting! You will also command Makhno's Black Army in this operation.<br><br>Scenario Version: January 2021<br>Scenario Type: Historic<br>Player Countries: Red Russia, Black Army<br>AI Version: 3.0<br>Player Turn Prestige 20pp/turn<br>Turns: 16 BV; 20 V; 26 TV<br>Scenario Designer: randowe<br><br>ORDERS:<br>\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af\u00af<br>Break through the enemy defensive lines and attack the Isthmus of Perekop as well as northern Crimea and capture all VHs in 16/20/26 turns for a Brilliant Victory/Victory/Tactical Victory.", [{"id": 0, "country": 103, "support": [136]}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-atomic"],
["Greece: Resistance and Civil War (1940-1949)"],
["bn4s00.xml", "Battle of Pindus", "BATTLE OF PINDUS - 3 NOV 1940<br><br>Pindus Mountains, Epirus<br><br>In your defense sector an Italian Division tries to advance on the strategic mountain pass at the town of Metsovo and threatens to cut off our supply routes and to separate our troops in Epirus and in Macedonia. Stop the attack and chase away the Italian troops from the Pindus Mountains! Our Cavalry Division will try to surround the enemy on their right flank and encircle the Italians together with your troops.<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Vovousa, gets the chance of a Leader!", [{"id": 1, "country": 12}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s01.xml", "Battle of Korytsa", "BATTLE OF KORYTSA - 16 NOV 1940<br><br>Morava Mountains, Albania<br><br>The Italian attack could be stopped along the entire front! Now we will take the initiative and launch an offensive on the eastern flank of the front. Target of the attack is traffic point Korytsa in Albania. A victory will strengthen the morale of our troops and our nation in general.<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Korytsa gets the chance of gain experience!", [{"id": 1, "country": 12}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s02.xml", "Klisura Pass", "KLISURA PASS - 6 JAN 1941<br><br>Trebeshine Heights, Albania<br><br>After your victory at Korytsa we could penetrate deep into Albanian territory. However, we need the strategic important Klisura pass to consolidate our position. You will be the right one for this job. Occupy the Klisura Pass and the surrounding heights of Trebeshine mountain range! <br><br>GOAL Take all Allies VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the Klisura Pass, gets the chance of a Leader!", [{"id": 1, "country": 12}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s03.xml", "Italian Spring Offensive", "ITALIAN SPRING OFFENSIVE - 9 MAR 1941<br><br>Trebeshine Heights, Albania<br><br>In the last few weeks the Italians reinforced their army in Albania with fresh troops and we await the start of an offensive. Defend with your troops the Trebeshine Heights and if necessary recapture lost ground! <br><br>GOAL Hold after the tenth turn 10 VH, 9 VH or 8 VH for BV, V or TV!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 12}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s04.xml", "Retreat to Thessaloniki", "RETREAT TO THESSALONIKI - 8 APR 1941<br><br>South of Doiran Lake, Central Macedonia<br><br>As expected, the Germans invaded our country in support of their unsuccessful Allies, the Italians. German armored forces, through Yugoslavia bypassing the Metaxas Line, are on their way to Thessaloniki and threaten to encircle our East Macedonia Army. I fear that we are not able to stop the Germans here. Withdraw your troops immediately to Thessaloniki and try to establish a new defense line there. Use for your non-motorized units the railway line Kilkis-Thessaloniki to escape the rapid German forces!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 22 ground units via Exit Points or hold after the eighth turn 4 VH for BV! Hold after the eighth turn 3 VH or 2 VH for V or TV!<br><br>NOTE It is advisable to delay the deployment partly until the second turn, and then to send non-motorized units immediately via train on their journey. In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s05.xml", "Thessaloniki - Evacuation", "THESSALONIKI - EVACUATION - 9 APR 1941<br><br>Thessaloniki, Central Macedonia<br><br>Thessaloniki is not to hold - Evacuate your troops to Athens via sea immediately! The remains of the Krussia Detachment and the 19th Motorised Infantry Division try to kept clear your back as long as possible!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 9 ground units (in sea transport) via Exit Points or hold after the seventh turn 4 VH for BV! Hold after the seventh turn 3 VH or 2 VH for V or TV!<br><br>NOTE Due to the short time between the missions at HQ no new units can be recruited!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s06.xml", "Lake Kastoria", "LAKE KASTORIA - 15 APR 1941<br><br>Lake Kastoria, West Macedonia<br><br>As expected, the Germans invaded our country in support of their unsuccessful Allies, the Italians. Our East Macedonia Army capitulated already, our forces in Western Macedonia are destroyed and the Germans are close to Kozani. Thus our main forces in Albania threatens to cut off! We have no other choice but to immediate withdrawal from Albania. Advance with your troops immediately to Lake Kastoria and save our line of retreat!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 6 ground units via Exit Point or hold after the ninth turn 4 VH for BV! Hold after the ninth turn 3 VH or 2 VH for V or TV!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s07.xml", "Metsovo Pass", "METSOVO PASS - 19 APR 1941<br><br>South of Grevena, West Macedonia<br><br>After your breakthrough at Lake Kastoria we could not hold open the gap for long time and only a few troops could escaped. You have now the Germans before and behind! A German SS unit, passed Lake Kastoria before, is already on their way to Metsovo pass and there is now the opportunity to attack this force from behind! Prevent the blockade of the Metsovo pass and allow further comrades to escape!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE Due to the short time between the missions at HQ no new units can be recruited!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s08.xml", "Last Stand at Thermopylae", "LAST STAND AT THERMOPYLAE - 24 APR 1941<br><br>Levadia, Central Greece<br><br>The Empire forces have set up a defensive position at Thermopylae to cover the evacuation of their main forces. Hasten to meet them and take over their positions, so that these forces also have a chance to escape across the sea!<br><br>GOAL Hold after the tenth turn 7 VH, 6 VH or 4 VH for BV, V or TV!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s09.xml", "Crete - Invasion", "CRETE - INVASION - 20 MAY 1941<br><br>Chania, Crete<br><br>The crazy Germans actually try to conquer Crete from the air! Thwart this venture and destroy the German airborne troops!<br><br>Hold after the twelfth turn 6 VH, 5 VH or 4 VH for BV, V or TV!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn! Last chance to buy a tank for the next six scenarios! ;)", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s10.xml", "Crete - Evacuation", "CRETE - EVACUATION - 28 MAY 1941<br><br>Sphakia, Crete<br><br>The withdrawal from Crete, the evacuation to Egypt was ordered - the island is not to hold! Move to the south coast of the island and board the waiting vessels!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 12 ground units (in sea transport) via Exit Points!<br><br>NOTE Due to the short time between the missions at HQ no new units can be recruited!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s11.xml", "El Alamein", "EL ALAMEIN - 23 OCT 1942<br><br>Alam Naghil, south of El Alamein, Egypt<br><br>It is time to expel the Axis from Egypt! The offensive against the German-Italian positions at El Alamein has begun. Your troops have the task to attack the enemy positions east of Ruweisat Ridge and - if possible - to capture. The main attack will take place in the North and - in case of success -  force the entire German-Italian front to retreat!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE A fighter squadron, trained and equipped by our British Allies, is subject to your command. Congratulations!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s12.xml", "Crushing the Mutiny", "CRUSHING THE MUTINY - 24 APR 1944<br><br>At sea off Alexandria, Egypt<br><br>Bad news from Egypt! A pro-EAM (National Liberation Front of Greece) mutiny inside the Greek Navy and the first Greek Brigade is broke out. Your troops are shipped from Palestine to Alexandria and help to down the revolt!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s13.xml", "Foglia River", "FOGLIA RIVER - 2 SEP 1944<br><br>South of Foglia River , Italy<br><br>Welcome in Italy! The attack on the Gothic Line is under way! However, the German resistance is stronger than expected and parts of the British 8th Army must already be taken out of the front due to high losses and exhaustion. Your troops will replace these units. Perform a frontal assault against the German defense at the Foglia River and show our Allies friends to what Greeks are able!<br><br>GOAL Hold after the ninth turn 12 VH, 11 VH or 9 VH for BV, V or TV!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Morciano Di Romagna gets full replacements!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s14.xml", "Battle of Rimini", "BATTLE OF RIMINI - 15 SEP 1944<br><br>South of Conca River, Italy<br><br>The Germans retreated behind the Conca River and established a new defensive line there. Break through that line, advance on Rimini and free the city!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE A bomber squadron, trained and equipped by our British Allies, is subject to your command. Congratulations!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s15.xml", "Battle of Athens", "BATTLE OF ATHENS - 12 DEC 1944<br><br>Athens, Greece<br><br>In Athens the Communists are gone over to armed struggle! At present, we have insufficient forces stationed in Athens, but the British have pledged to fly in the 4th Indian Division from Italy immediately. Beat back the communists and clear Athens and the surrounding areas from the rebels!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s16.xml", "Battle of Konitsa", "BATTLE OF KONITSA - 25 DEC 1947<br><br>South of Konitsa, Epirus<br><br>The communist rebels have attacked the city Konitsa on the Greek-Albanian border! The garrison defended the town stubbornly and until now was able to fend off all attacks. Advance on Konitsa and expel the rebels!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s17.xml", "Battle of Vitsi", "BATTLE OF VITSI - 9 SEP 1948<br><br>South of Lake Kastoria, West Macedonia<br><br>Our last operation in the Grammos mountains was a bust! Most rebels escaped in the Vitsi region. Our job is now to prevent a renewed Redoubt in the Vitsi mountains and to destroy the escaped enemy forces. We plan a coordinated attack from the south and east to encircle the rebels. Your troops will lead the attack from the south and clean the area around the Lake Kastoria!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Dendrochori gets full replacements!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s18.xml", "Operation Torch", "OPERATION TORCH - 24 AUG 1949<br><br>East of  Mt Grammos, Pindus Mountains<br><br>We are on the verge of winning the war! The defeated rebels have been entrenched in the mountains at the Albania border and the General Staff has ordered a last major operation in order to complete our victory. The Americans have supplied us with modern dive bomber and they should help to destroy the strong fortifications. Chase off the remaining communist troops from their fortifications in the Grammos mountains!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 82}], [{"id": 0, "country": 39}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s19.xml", "Escape from Egypt", "ESCAPE FROM EGYPT - 8 MAY 1943<br><br>Military Prison Al-Qabbari, Alexandria<br><br>The renowned hero now only a public enemy! Jailed in the military prison of Al-Qabbari you are waiting for your trial because of communist propaganda and insubordination against the Middle East High Command and the Greek government in exile. However, your friends managed to organize your escape to Greece and to provide you with a getaway car. At the airport of Alexandria a plane is ready for take off and alternatively a vessel waiting for you located in the port of Al Muaddiyah. Reach one of these points without to be caught at the control points of the Brits! Friends on the Greek freighters SS Dimitrios Inglessis and SS Thrace monitor the airport and the port for you!<br><br>GOAL Retreat your MSU via Exit Point!", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s20.xml", "Punish the Traitors!", "PUNISH THE TRAITORS! - 10 OCT 1943<br><br>East of Kalabaka, Thessaly<br><br>Welcome to Greece, Commander! Experienced leaders like you we are needed urgently. The 13th ELAS Division is now under your command and your first task is a punishment operation against the traitorous EDES Bandits be making common cause with the Germans! Currently, the EDES control parts of the road Ioannina-Metsovo-Kalabaka. You will attack the EDES around Kalabaka and bring the area back under our control!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE If you do not like the composition of your new Core, you can sell units and acquire new ones with same experience. However,  the increased 35% chance for a leader get lost. New units start with a chance of 10%!<br><br>The unit occupying the town Spathades, gets the chance of a Leader!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s21.xml", "Battle of Agorelitsa", "BATTLE OF AGORELITSA - 17 JUL 1944<br><br>South of Korifasi, Peloponnese<br><br>You will carry out a strike against the German occupation forces on the western Peloponnese. Target of your attack is the 41st Fortress Division and the neutralization of the coastal artillery near Marathopoli. The Germans have some battle-hardened units in this area, so be careful!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The unit occupying the town Agorelitsa, gets the chance of a Leader!", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s22.xml", "Battle of Athens", "BATTLE OF ATHENS - 12 DEC 1944<br><br>Athens, Greece<br><br>After the withdrawal of the Germans from Greece, the royalists have returned to our country and think they can - with the help of the disgusting Brits - rob the fruits of our liberation struggle! They also not shy away from massacre peaceful protesters to keep themselves in power. Once again it's time to take up arms and to chase these parasites out of our country!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE The British will try to fly in reinforcements, so occupy as soon as possible all airfields!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s23.xml", "Battle of Konitsa", "BATTLE OF KONITSA - 25 DEC 1947<br><br>Konitsa, Epirus<br><br>Our struggle for a free Greece is now entering a decisive phase. Our political leadership has decided that we need a major city as capital for our government to gain further international validity for our fight. The choice has fallen on the city Konitsa at the Albanian border and the battle is already under way. But reinforcements are on the way to Konitsa to relieve the garrison. Fend off the attacks of the Athenian mercenary troops and bring the liberation of Konitsa to a successful end!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s24.xml", "First Battle of Grammos", "FIRST BATTLE OF GRAMMOS - 18 JUL 1948<br><br>Mt Grammos, Pindus Mountains<br><br>The battle for the Grammos mountains raged for nearly a month and the Athenian fascists send more and more mercenary troops into battle. We have no choice, we must abandon the Grammos mountains temporarily and dare the breakout! To achieve this, you will carry out a concentrated attack on the center of the enemy forces! Beat a breach in the enemy's ranks and lead our troops in Northeast direction to the Vitsi mountains!<br><br>GOAL Retreat 9 ground units via Exit Points!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s25.xml", "Battle of Vitsi", "BATTLE OF VITSI - 9 SEP 1948<br><br>Lake Kastoria, West Macedonia<br><br>It has not gone unnoticed that our main forces have retreated into the Vitsi mountains. With a new offensive the enemy wants us to deathblow here. But he underestimated our remaining strength and attack with only weak forces. After we have fool him with our withdraw he is now trapped! Destroy the enemy troops - a victory is urgently needed in order to maintain the morale of our forces!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!<br><br>NOTE In this mission the AI has the first turn!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["bn4s26.xml", "Aridaea", "ARIDAEA - 14 DEC 1948<br><br>East of Aridaea, West Macedonia<br><br>The liberation of Greek cities is still at the top of our priorities. Your Division will carry out an surprise attack across the Yugoslav border on Aridaea and free the city! If the resistance is broken here, the further advance on Veroea and Edessa is planned. Let's hope that you succeed and meet an unprepared enemy!<br><br>GOAL Capture all VH!", [{"id": 1, "country": 39}], [{"id": 0, "country": 82}], "eqp-lxf" ],
["Forward, Comrade! (1939-1945)"],
["forward0.xml", "Battle at the Chalchin Gol", "Battle at the Chalchin Gol<br>Welcome, Herr General. You are facing the 6. Japanese army. The Japanese have passed the Chalchin Gol. Your mission is to put the enemy over the river.<br>Your troops:<br>We have chosen some troops for you. You will have six different troops, each of them is of another class. And you are able to order more units in a recent scale.  Keep in mind that your decision can be important in coming battles.<br>Enemy troops: <br>The 6. Japanese army have only a few tanks and very few air support. The Japanese are worn out. They have no rail connection, so they are certainly not able to relieve their troops.<br>Sgn Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward1.xml", "Battle of Suomussalmi", "Battle of Suomussalmi<br>You surely know, that we are at war with Finland at the moment. Your mission is to break through the finish lines at Suomussalmi. <br>Your troops:<br>You have to solve this mission only with little help from auxiliary troops. <br>Enemy troops: <br>The Finish have only a few troops. Mainly infantry troops are awaiting you on your way to Suomussalmi.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward2.xml", "Pocket of Minsk", "Pocket of Minsk:<br>Comrade General, you surely know that the Germans have assaulted our country. Now, the situation is really delicate. While we are speaking, every moment German troops can fulfill the closing of the Minsker pocket. The Panzergruppe 2 and 3 have bypassed Minsk in the northern and southern and every moment they can team up near of Borissow to close the pocket. You have the permission to evacuate the pocket in need. But you should try to hold Minsk, the Minsker Airfield and Borissow as long as possible. <br>Your troops:<br>You will get help from the soviet Westfront. These troops have only few tank divisions but many artilleries and especially infantry divisions.<br> Enemy troops:<br>You are facing a large part of the Heeresgruppe Mitte. The Germans have contracted a lot of tanks, infantry, artillery, 8.8 PAK and bombers west of Minsk. Hoths Panzergruppe 3 is attacking from the north, Panzergruppe 2 under Guderian is attacking from the south. You will have contact with these troops soon, too. <br>Attention! Trying to hold Minsk can be really hard. The Germans are much more experienced then you. If you are a bad player you can evacuate Minsk and trying to hold Borissow and expect the enemy in the outback<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward3.xml", "Defense of Kishinev", "Defense of Kishinev<br>The Germans and their allies, the Rumanians, attacking Bessarabia. Stop the advance of the axis troops.<br>Your troops:<br>You have only your core troops. We cannot provide more troops, because they are all needed on other frontlines.<br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing the 11. German army in the north. Some parts of the Rumanian third and fourth army are attacking from southwest. The Rumanians are inexperienced. It could be a good idea, that you use your inexperienced troops against them.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward4.xml", "Battle of Odessa", "Battle of Odessa:<br>The Rumanian 4. Army has launched its attack on Odessa in the last days. They succeeded in pushing our troops back. Your mission is to launch a counterattack and put the Rumanians back to their starting position.<br>Your troops:<br>Again, you will nearly have your own troops to deal with your mission.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The Rumanian 4. Army is inexperienced. They have only a few tanks, but a lot of cavalry and infantry. We expect that some German troops will arrive in a few days to support the Rumanian attack.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward5.xml", "Pocket of Kiew", "Pocket of Kiev<br>Herr General, the situation is very awkward. Your troops are threatened by encirclement. Western of Kiev, the 6. Army is attacking your positions. From the north the Panzergruppe 2 will show up every moment in the back of your positions and they will join with the advance guard of the 17. Army. Hold Kiev and the surrounding regions as long as possible, so that we have the possibility to bind German troops.<br>Your troops:<br>Parts of the 37. Army are subordinate to your authority. These troops are wet behind the ears and do not have much tanks, but some artillery with big caliber.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The Germans proceed in the west with many tanks and infantry. The Panzergruppe 2 and the advance guard of the 17. Army are completely motorized and have mainly Panzer II and Panzer III tanks.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward6.xml", "Pocket of Brjansk", "Pocket of Brjansk<br>The situation at the Brjansker front is very grave. The XXIV. Motorized Army Corps could brake through your lines south of Brjansk. It may be expected that they will turn northwards and try to encircle your troops. Try to evacuate your troops slowly but do not miss to defend Brjansk and your other targets.<br>Your troops:<br>The 50. Army is reported to you. Altogether 50 troops will help you. They are still inexperienced, but they should be strong enough to slow the German advance a little bit. <br>Enemy troops:<br>The Germans have many tank divisions, infantry divisions and bomber squadrons. You should calculate with heavy attacks from the west and the south. The strongest German troops are deployed in the southwest. <br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward7.xml", "Tula Counterattack", "Tula Counterattack<br>Now it is time to take the initiative. You are facing the 2. Panzerarmee, which will attack every moment your lines south of Tula. Hold Tula and try to realize a counterattack if possible.<br>Your troops:<br>You have the command about the 49. and 50. Army. The troops are still inexperienced, but they were reinforced only just. <br>We are pleased to tell you, that we have decided to add a new recon unit to your troops.<br>Enemy troops:<br>Parts of the 2. Panzerarmee are under the required strength. There are not so much tanks and anti-tanks on the first front line, however the 2. Panzerarmee still have some tank divisions in reserve. Probably the Germans will march them off.<br>Please notice:<br>A brilliant victory, a normal victory and a tactical victory will lead to different scenarios. There will be no choice scenario. You should make a save game, if you want to play all scenarios.<br>A brilliant victory will give you the opportunity to end the war in the early 1942 by encircling the Heeresgruppe Mitte at Krasny Bor.<br>A normal victory will lead you to the normal progression of the campaign. <br>If you achieve only a tactical victory or a loss you have to defend Moskau first, before you can continue with the normal campaign path (Demyansk).<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward8.xml", "Closing the pocket", "Closing the pocket<br>After your success at Tula we could also break through the German lines north of Moscow. You are now in the near of Smolensk. The Germans had not tried to escape. I believe they have the order to stay in the pocket. Your troops should now deploy northeast and southeast of the city and attacking the last German troops which hold the last position, in which German troops could escape. Close the pocket! Hold in any case the connection to the troops east of you (both victory hexes), so the Germans could not escape. Otherwise there is a risk that your troops will be encircled. <br>Your troops:<br>We can provide only a few troops for your mission, because most of the soviet armies are needed to hold the pocket closed.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The Germans have left the city and have taken positions east of the town. The Germans in this area are really weak. However, the area of the bottleneck is surrounded with mine field and other blockings. We have reliable information that the Germans do big troop movements. They have removed troops from the Heeresgruppe S\u00fcd and Heeresgruppe Nord to relieve the pocket. Moreover, troops in the pocket try to meet these troops halfway. Be fast, because the enemy is outnumbered.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward9.xml", "Urban Warfare in Moskva", "Urban Warfare in Moscow<br>This is our last opportunity. The Germans have advanced to the western periphery of Moscow. Hold Moscow at any costs!<br>Your troops:<br>You have we command over a tank division, the Moscow garrison and several bunkers and pillboxes. We have tried to mine the way for the German divisions but we could not finish this.<br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing several tanks and infantry divisions. Moreover, you should calculate with heavy attacks from the German Luftwaffe.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward10.xml", "Demyansk Pocket", "Destroying the Demyansk Pocket<br>Comrade General, I have an easy mission for you. Since our offensive in the winter we could encircle the X. Army Corps near of Demyansk. Now we know that the Kampfgruppe Seydlitz is on her way to save the troops in the pocket. Stop the attack of Kampfgruppe Seydlitz and hold the pocket closen.<br>Your troops:<br>For this easy mission you will nearly only have your tank army. The deploy-hexes around the pocket are limited.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The X. Army corps has lost strength in the battles and have only a few divisions now. Kampfgruppe Seydlitz has an equal strength, but this troops are more dangerous. Do not miss to cut the Kampfgruppe Seydlitz off from the battlefield. They should arrive on our western flank in two days. Be aware of the German Luftwaffe. We have information that several bomber squadrons are in the combat area.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward11.xml", "Defense of Voronezh", "Defense of Voronezh<br>After our successes in the winter the Germans seems to have their troops reinforced. With their Hungarian allies they are starting a big offensive with the target Voronezh. Slow down the advance of the Germans, so we have enough time to prepare new positions. <br>Your troops:<br>You have command over the 40. and 13. Army. These troops are equipped with very new prototypes of SU tank destroyers. They could be useful for you.<br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing the 4. Panzerarmee and the 2. Army. Moreover, in the south the 2. Hungarian Army supports them. The Hungarians are not so experienced like the Germans. The Germans have also new assault guns with higher range than our tanks. Be aware of them! Oh, wait, we have just this moment obtained the information that the Germans have marched off more troops with good tanks and tank destroyers. They will arrive in the south of the battlefield in several days.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward12.xml", "Rzhew Meat Grinder", "Rzhew Meat Grinder<br>After our offensive in the winter there is still the German salient at Rzhew. We have decided to start a great attack on the salient with the target of destroying the defendsing German troops. Your troops should attack in the north at Rzhew, in the south at Sychewka and in the middle of the salient, break through the lines and destroy or capture the most forces.<br>Your troops:<br>You will have the command over the 30. Army. The Germans hold the only airfield in this area, but the 30. Army has a very experienced engineer troop, which has many experience in buliding airfields.<br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing the 9. German Army. The troops in the salient are still very strong. They have built a coherent front line and break through it could be very difficult but they have no reserves after the first front line. The area is also full of landmines and fortifications. Rzhew`s defenders are very powerfull, you may need a lot of higher range artillery to break through the lines at Rzhew. Be aware, that the reserve troops are deployed in Sychewka. There you have to calculate with heavy resistance, too.<br>Please notice:<br>You will gain 100 pp per turn.This money is for refits and you will be over the cap if you do not use it, so feel free to use it.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward13.xml", "Operation Uranus", "Operation Uranus<br>Be ready for Operation Uranus. Today our great offensive starts with the aim to encircling the 6. Army in Stalingrad. Your troops will attack from the south and the northwest the German and their allied troops. <br>Your troops:<br>You will have command over the 65. Army. This troops will attack the Romanian front in the northeast and will support your attack against the Italian und Hungarian troops in the southeast.<br>Enemy troops:<br>In the southwest the 4. Panzerarmee under command of Hermann Hoth is your opponent. In the north the 3. Romanian Army defends the front line. In the southeast Italian and Hungary troops hold the lines. The Romanian, Italian und Hungarian troops have under strength and are bad equipped. They have only a lit bit of ammunition. Although these troops are numerous, they should be no real opponent for your troops. The situation in the southwest looks different. The 4. Panzerarmee still has some tank divisions. There is also a tank troop equipped with the new very dangerous Tiger tank.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward14.xml", "Battle at the Myschkowa", "Battle at the Myschkowa<br>The fascists and their allied try to break up the pocket of Stalingrad. We could stop them at the Myschkowa. You should overrun the enemy troops and throw them back to their starting position. <br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this job.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The Army Group Hoth is on the other side of the Myschkowa river. We calculate with further reinforcements in the next days. Although this troops will mostly be Italians, Romanians and Hungarians.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward15.xml", "Blowed by backhand", "Blowed by backhand<br>Herr General, the victory is within one`s reach, or maybe not. The Germans have evacuated the area of Charkow and withdraw their troops. Your army should push forward into the empty area and follow the escaping Germans. Many of our generals believe that the Germans are already beaten and the war will soon be over. But I am not so optimistic. So, be careful. <br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this task.<br>Enemy troops:<br>Our recons reported nearly no enemies in the area.<br>Please notice:<br>If you can hold all VHs you will come to a choice scenario, in which you must decide which Army Group you want to face for the rest of the war. If you cannot hold all VHs you will first have to fend the German attack at Prokhorowka.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward16.xml", "Prokhorowka Tank Battle", "Prokhorowka Tank Battle<br>The Germans are attacking our lines at Prokhorowka. Resist all Germans attacks and lead a conterattack against Belgorod. <br>Your troops: <br>We knowed that the Germans we lead this offensive and we could prepare strong positions. You will have command over the 51th Tank Army. This troops are not so experienced but all refreshed to over strenght. The positions before your deployment positions are secured with landmines.<br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing the II. SS-Panzer Corps. You have to calculate with heavy tank attacks. The German Luftwaffe will support the attack of the tanks. So you need a strong air defense and fighters. <br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward18.xml", "Free Leningrad", "Free Leningrad<br>More then two years ago the Germans began with their blockade of Leningrad. The pitful population of the town had to feel the pinch of hunger. We want to stop the blockade and push the Germans back. In the south and in the central sovietunion the Germans are withdrawed. I am sure they will withdraw their troops, if we will be able to lauch a great attack on the 16th Army.<br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission, but we have allocated two divisions with bridging engineers to your troops, because the Germans have destroyed the bridges. <br>Enemy troops:<br>The 16th Army still have some strong troops, but the best of the Germans are fighting in the south and in the central. So the 16th Army has only a few tank divisions. Mostfull infantry divisions will be your opponent.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward19.xml", "Battle of Viipuri", "Battle of Viipuri<br>Due to the invasion of west allied troops in France the Germans have withdrawn many troops. Your next operation will be the attack in Karelia. Move forward and capture Viipuri. <br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission. <br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing several finish troops. However, you should expect that the Germans will help Finland with some German reinforcements. Nonetheless, the enemy troops should be no problem for you.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 38}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward20.xml", "Attack on Riga", "Attack on Riga<br>After our success in Karelia we now want to free the Baltic states. Your tank army have the mission to attack the Germans in Riga and throw them out of the city.<br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission. <br>Enemy troops:<br>The 16th army and the 18th Army defends the city. There are some serious tank divisions outside of the city. In Riga fanatic infantry divisions are deployed. They have support fire from several artillery divisions.<br>Please notice:<br>The next two scenarios will be with no-auto-refit. You will gain a lot of pp for refits. <br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward21.xml", "Courland Pocket", "Courland Pocket<br>We have started several trials to elimenate the trapped Germans in Courland, but all attempts were not successful. I think your men are more suitable for this mission. Attack on the front between Liepaja and Saldus, break through the German lines and take Pavilosta.<br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission.<br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing the 16th and 18th Army. These troops are worn out, but high experienced. They have only two serious tank troops. The way to the battlefield is blocked with Blockings, Bunkers and Mindfields.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward22.xml", "Manchurian Operation", "Manchurian Operation<br>The war in Europe is over. Now we had to keep our promise and built a second front against Japan in Asia. We could push forward and are now east of Changchun. Your troops should break through the lines of Japanese and Manchukuo troops in the east of the town and capture Changchun.<br>Your troops:<br>For this attack you will only have your tank army. We own no airfield in this area. So, you should have a can build unit for this mission in your troops.<br>Enemy troops: <br>You are facing two armies and some Manchukuo troops. These armies are bad equipped but they have entrenched themselves in the mountains east of Changchun. To break through the lines will take time.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 5}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward23.xml", "Smolensker Offensive", "Smolensker Offensive<br>Now it is time for our big offensive. You will attack the German Heeresgruppe Mitte at Yelnya. The Germans are well prepared for our attack, but I am sure you will be able to break through their lines.<br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The Heeresgruppe Mitte still have strong troops, but they have only few tanks. On the other side you have to calculate with strong fire of high-range artillery and the German Luftwaffe has strong bomber forces in this area. The areas behind the bridges are well prepared for your attack, but if you are breaken through the resistance will be smaller.", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward24.xml", "Operation Bagration", "Operation Bagration<br>Now the time four our great offensives is come. Several armies will join the attack in Belorussia. Your troops should take Vitebsk.  Take the town and push forward to the west.<br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission.<br>Enemy troops:<br>Vitebsk is secured by strong fortifications and the IX. Army Corps. Further south the VI. Army Corps hold the positions. The Germans have some good tanks and tank killers like Tiger II tanks and a division of Elefants. It could be a good idea to deploy your best troops in the south and push there forward and the rest can concentrate on Vitebsk.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward25.xml", "Battle of Silesia", "Battle of Silesia<br>Herr General, meanwhile our armies have arrived Poland. You should take Krakow, west of you which is hold by the 4th Tank Army.<br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The 4th tank army has far under strength, but they have some serious Panther and Tiger II tanks. The strongest resistance should be in the Krakow city areal.<br>Please remember:<br>The next scenario (and Berlin too) will be no-auto-refit scenarios.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward26.xml", "Fortress K\u00fcstrin", "Fortress K\u00fcstrin<br>Your troops have arrived the Oder at K\u00fcstrin. Take K\u00fcstrin, take positions along the river and build a bridgehead over the river at K\u00fcstrin. <br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission.<br>Enemy troops:<br>K\u00fcstrin is hold by a garrison. Behind the Oder some strong German troops will try to prevent that you can build a bridgehead. But altogether the enemy should be no problem for your troops.<br>Attention please:<br>A brilliant victory, a normal victory and a tactical victory will lead you into different paths. <br>If you win brilliant, you have to end the war with the battle in Berlin. This scenario will be no-auto-refit, too.<br>If you win normal the west allied have captured Berlin and you have to fight against them. In this path you have the help of German troops, which you can buy for extra pp.<br>If you win tactical the west allied have captured Berlin and you have to fight against them. The German armies in the east could flee into the west and will support the west allies.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward27.xml", "Battle of Berlin", "Battle of Berlin<br>Herr General, it is time for the last battle. Your troops have taken positions along the Oder. In this scenario you have several missions.<br>-\tTake Cottbus, Schwedt and Oranienburg<br>-\tCross the Oder at the Seelower Heights and defeat the 9th Army<br>-\tEncircle the rest of the 9th Army in the Pocket of Halbe <br>-\tDo not let the troops in the pocket flee<br>-\tTake Berlin<br>-\tStop the advance of the 12th Army and take Eberswalde at the Elbe<br>Your troops:<br>The 2nd Belorussian Front will assist your attack in the south and in the north. In the north the 2nd Belorussian Front should take Schwedt and fight against the 4th Tank Army. Remember, this is the last battle. You can use the massive pp for refitting if you need it.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The 9th Army, the 12th Army and the 4th Tank Army are high-experienced but worn out troops. They have some serious tank divisions with Tiger II and Panther tanks. In the areal of Berlin unexperienced Volkssturm and Landwehr troops are also common opponents. In Berlin rests of the 9th Army, police troops and Volkssturm troops defeats the city. They are supported by Waffen SS Battle Group Mohnke.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward28.xml", "Breakthrough at Dessau", "Breakthrough at Dessau<br>After some planning the general stuff has decided that we will attack the allied lines at Dessau. The allies have numerous troops at this front line, so, if we can break through their lines, the allies must withdraw their other troops.<br>Your troops:<br>Besides your tank army one army will support your attack. They are deployed west of your troops.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The enemy have several tank divisions. In the air you have to calculate with high resistance, too. The USAF and RAF have several air fleets in the area of Dessau. Several level-bomber squadrons will support the ground troops.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward29.xml", "Battle of East Friesland", "Battle of East Friesland<br>We could trap several armies in East Friesland. We have reliable information that the west allied plans to evacuate the troops through the harbors of Emden and Wilhelmshaven. Take Emden and Wilhelmshaven before the ships arrive and destroy most of the enemy's troops to prevent the possibilities of a counterattack.<br>Your troops: <br>Besides your tank army a little army will support you. This troops could be useful for the conquer of Emden.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The trapped opponents still have several dangerous tank divisions and plenty infantry. The air force will made problems to you, especially because you will have no airfield at the beginning of the battle. The next airfield is too far away. Be sure that you have troops that can build an airport.   <br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward30.xml", "Battle at the Ruhr", "Battle at the Ruhr<br>The majority of the war production for the west allied comes from the Ruhr area. If we will be able to capture the Ruhr area it will be more difficult for the allied to get supplies. Take the Ruhr area, D\u00fcsseldorf and build a bridgehead over the Rhine.<br>Your troops:<br>Besides your tank army several divisions will support your troops. Relating to your request we have given you more Flak units for this battle.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The enemies are not numerous. In the east of the Ruhr area the west allied have built a front which is saved by blockings, landmines and barbwire. More in the south the resistance seems to be not so hard.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward31.xml", "Battle in the Ardennes", "Battle in the Ardennes<br>In what the Germans failed once we now want to success. In the Ardennes the allied have build the last defensive line. If we can manage a breakthrough the way to Antwerpen will be free and the allied troops can no longer use the harbor of Antwerpen for reinforcements. <br>Your troops:<br>An army will support your attack. A unit of Josef Stalin tanks will assist you, too.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The allied troops are still numerous. Beware of assaults in the woody terrain. I remind you, that Josef Stalin tanks only have a few ammunitions and they are vulnerable in this terrain.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward32.xml", "Charge on Antwerpen", "Charge on Antwerpen<br>The victory is near. Your troops are standing in the near of Antwerpen. Your mission is to eliminate the last allied troops and occupy the harbor of Antwerpen to prevent further allied reinforcements.<br>Your troops:<br>The harbor of Antwerpen is secured by several ships. You will have command over a part of our fleet. Some bombers will assist you in this fight, too. The allied hold the only airfield in this area. It could be a good idea to build a new airfield at the start of the battle.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The defenders have abandoned the area south of Antwerpen and secured it with landmines and blockings. After this line the enemy front line is not so big. In the outback the allied still have some big tanks, like the Sherman Easy Eight type. In the harbor the allied unload unexperienced tank divisions at the moment.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward33.xml", "Breakthrough at Dessau", "Breakthrough at Dessau<br>After some planning the general stuff has decided that we will attack the allied lines at Dessau. The allies have numerous troops at this front line, so, if we can break through their lines, the allies must withdraw their other troops.<br>Your troops:<br>Besides your tank army one army will support your attack. They are deployed west of your troops.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The enemy have several tank divisions. In the air you have to calculate with high resistance, too. The USAF and RAF have several air fleets in the area of Dessau. Several level-bomber squadrons will support the ground troops.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward34.xml", "Battle of East Friesland", "Battle of East Friesland<br>We could trap several armies in East Friesland. We have reliable information that the west allied plans to evacuate the troops through the harbors of Emden and Wilhelmshaven. Take Emden and Wilhelmshaven before the ships arrive and destroy most of the enemy's troops to prevent the possibilities of a counterattack.<br>Your troops: <br>Besides your tank army a little army will support you. This troops could be useful for the conquer of Emden.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The trapped opponents still have several dangerous tank divisions and plenty infantry. The air force will made problems to you, especially because you will have no airfield at the beginning of the battle. The next airfield is too far away. Be sure that you have troops that can build an airport.   <br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward35.xml", "Battle at the Ruhr", "Battle at the Ruhr<br>The majority of the war production for the west allied comes from the Ruhr area. If we will be able to capture the Ruhr area it will be more difficult for the allied to get supplies. Take the Ruhr area, D\u00fcsseldorf and build a bridgehead over the Rhine.<br>Your troops:<br>Besides your tank army several divisions will support your troops. Relating to your request we have given you more Flak units for this battle.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The enemies are not numerous. In the east of the Ruhr area the west allied have built a front which is saved by blockings, landmines and barbwire. More in the south the resistance seems to be not so hard.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward36.xml", "Ardennenoffensive", "Battle in the Ardennes<br>In what the Germans failed once we now want to success. In the Ardennes the allied have build the last defensive line. If we can manage a breakthrough the way to Antwerpen will be free and the allied troops can no longer use the harbor of Antwerpen for reinforcements. <br>Your troops:<br>An army will support your attack. A unit of Josef Stalin tanks will assist you, too.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The allied troops are still numerous. Beware of assaults in the woody terrain. I remind you, that Josef Stalin tanks only have a few ammunitions and they are vulnerable in this terrain.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward37.xml", "Sturm auf Antwerpen", "Charge on Antwerpen<br>The victory is near. Your troops are standing in the near of Antwerpen. Your mission is to eliminate the last allied troops and occupy the harbor of Antwerpen to prevent further allied reinforcements.<br>Your troops:<br>The harbor of Antwerpen is secured by several ships. You will have command over a part of our fleet. Some bombers will assist you in this fight, too. The allied hold the only airfield in this area. It could be a good idea to build a new airfield at the start of the battle.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The defenders have abandoned the area south of Antwerpen and secured it with landmines and blockings. After this line the enemy front line is not so big. In the outback the allied still have some big tanks, like the Sherman Easy Eight type. In the harbor the allied unload unexperienced tank divisions at the moment.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 22}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward38.xml", "Kuban-Bridgehead", "Kuban-Bridgehead<br>Since many months the Germans has the bridgehead at the black sea. We could push them back, but all tries to destroy the Germans and their allied failed. We have reliable information that the Germans plans to evacuate the bridgehead preventing a cut off. We want attack before they can escape. Force an attack and destroy the German forces.<br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission. The Germans control all two airfields in this area. We have provided an engineer troop to your army. It should be able to build a little airfield in a few days.<br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing the 17th German Army. Also, there are several Romanian and Slovak troops. The Romanians and the Slovaks have only a low strength. The German troops has only a few tanks and only one fighter squadron. Maybe there will be no great fightback, but you have to be fast, too.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward39.xml", "Zhitomir Counterattack", "Zhitomir Counterattack<br>Unfortunately, I have to interrupt your vacation. While we have refitted your troops the situation near Zhitomir have changed in a serious way. The Germans have started a counterattack with five tank divisions after we have recaptured Kiev. Hold Zhitomir and stop every advance to Kiev.<br>Your troops:<br>Because of the refits not every of your unit had marched of simultaneously. In the Zhitomir area you will have only a few troops in the beginning. You can calculate with an arrive of your other troops in some days. The 94. Rifle Division defends Zhitomir. These troops will also be under your command.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The Germans are not numerous, but they have some serious tanks. Because of the near of the Germans to Zhitomir they may be able to lead a devastating attack onto your troops. So, be careful.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward40.xml", "Brody Cauldron", "Brody Cauldron<br>With your advance the encirclement of six German and Hungarian divisions is complete. We know that the Germans will try to break out of the pocket. You have to prevent that troops of the axis can escape over the river into the west and you have to destroy most of the enemies troops.<br>Your troops: <br>Some troops of the 1st Ukrainian Front will assist you by your mission.<br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing the XIII Army Corps. The enemy is under strenght and has only some seroius tanks. With a good front is should be easy to repel the breakout.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward41.xml", "Battle of Romania", "Battle of Romania<br>After we made peace with Finland, we want to urge Romania out of the war, because with the loss of the Romanian oilfield the Germans will not be able to perform big resistance. You have to break through the Axis lines at Jassy.<br>Your troops:<br>You only have the command about your tank army.<br>Enemy troops:<br>The Germans and Romanians have several divisions in this area. More precisely you are fighting against the Heeresgruppe S\u00fcdukraine which consists of the Army Group Wohler, the Army Group Dumitrescu and the 4th Romanian Army. The Germans have some heavy tanks and will be able to perform a hard counterattack if you are not able to perform a good first strike. The Romanians have suffered heavy losses in the war and their troops are quite under normal strength.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 13}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward42.xml", "Take Szekesferhervar!", "Take Szekesfehervar!<br>While the Germans try to break through our lines at the Lake Balaton in the west, your mission is to break through the German and Hungarian line at Szekesfehervar. With the capture of the town the way to Vienna will be open.<br>Your troops:<br>You will only have your tank army for this mission.<br>Enemy troops:<br>Your opponent is the Army Group Balck. The troops are battle-wearied, but they have some serious tanks and fighters. <br>!!!Please notice!!!: <br>The next two scenarios will be no-auto-refit. So, you should ensure that your troops are in acceptably conditions at the end of the battle.<br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["forward43.xml", "Battle of Prague", "Battle of Prague<br>Berlin is captured by our troops. Now we want to destroy the remaining German armies in Czechia and in Slovakia and free Prague. You have to broke through the German lines at Nagysallo and move north.<br>Your troops: <br>The 2nd Ukrainian Front will assist your attack on the German lines. Also, some Romanian, Czech and Polish troops will be under your command. Unfortunately, there is no airfield in this area. So, you have to build one, before your planes can start.<br>Enemy troops:<br>You are facing the 8th Army. These troops have lost much of their strength but they were supplied with some serious prototypes in the last days. The Germans have some new fighters in the area, but there is no airfield in the near, so, the fighters can support the German troops only a few days.  <br>Sgn. Major Heinz", [{"id": 1, "country": 7}], [{"id": 0, "country": 89}], "eqp-atomic" ],
["Sim Pobedishi! - The Red East (1918-1920)"],
["simpob_00.xml", "Until you find somebody: the Komuch offensive (I)", "By this sign: the Komuch offensive<br><br>June 8th, 1918<br><br>The men coming down the Volga have a banner with the old words on it - By this sign shalt thou conquer - and underneath the banner is a Committee of ex-deputies, a Czechoslovak corps that was supposed to be going home through Vladivostok, and the officers' druzhinas of every town between here and Chelyabinsk. They are going to write those words over everything they take. We shall see what they are worth by the autumn.<br><br>Samara fell this morning. The Czechoslovak battalions took the bridge over the Volga before the demolition party got to it, and the Committee of Members of the Constituent Assembly has declared itself the government of Russia in a building the garrison was holding at breakfast.<br><br>I command a detachment of the 1st Army. Between Samara and Kazan there is one railway, four towns on it, and nothing else. Hold them, and take the bridgehead back if it can be done.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Simbirsk (7,5), Melekess (21,7), Stavropol (20,19) and Syzran (8,26).<br>- Take Samara (30,23).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_01.xml", "Uncountable trophies: the Komuch offensive (II)", "Uncountable trophies: Kazan<br><br>August 4th, 1918<br><br>Kazan holds the gold.<br><br>Six hundred million roubles of the Imperial reserve were evacuated here for safety in 1915 and they are still in the bank vaults, and every man in Kappel's column knows it. That is why the attack is coming here and not somewhere sensible, and it is also why we cannot simply trade the city for space.<br><br>Kappel has perhaps three thousand men and the Serbian battalion and two gunboats. We have the 5th Army, which is three days old and has a staff that has never worked together. Hold the Kremlin, the academy and the river crossings. Bogorodskoye downstream is where their flotilla is basing.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold the Kazan Kremlin (27,3), the Military Academy (26,2), Vasilyevo (22,3), Verkhniy Uslan (23,4) and Karaishevo (33,17).<br>- Take Bogorodskoye (30,25).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_02.xml", "Harvest of sorrow: the end of the Komuch ", "Harvest of sorrow: the end of the Komuch<br><br>September 18th, 1918<br><br>The tide has turned and the Committee knows it before we do.<br><br>Kazan was retaken on the tenth, Simbirsk on the twelfth - Tukhachevsky's 1st Army took it in two days and sent Lenin a telegram about it while he was still in bed with a bullet in him. The People's Army is coming apart: the mobilised peasants will not fight for the Committee, and the Czechoslovaks have decided they are going home after all and would rather not die on the Volga first.<br><br>Samara and Syzran are the last of it. The Committee's staff and its treasury are already loading at Krotovka to go east to Ufa, and every column that gets out will be in the line against us again in the spring under Kolchak.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Samara (30,23) and Syzran (8,26).<br>- Hold Simbirsk (8,6).<br>- The enemy escapes instead if seven of his columns get out through Krotovka (41,23).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_03.xml", "At the gates of Europe: Ufa", "At the gates of Europe: Ufa<br><br>January 6th, 1919<br><br>There is a Supreme Ruler now.<br><br>Admiral Kolchak took power in Omsk in November by arresting the last of the Committee's ministers, and the Entente has recognised what he did by continuing to unload rifles at Vladivostok. He has a real staff, a real mobilisation and the whole of Siberia's railway.<br><br>His first stroke has come at Ufa in a Urals winter, against the 5th Army, which is holding a hundred and fifty versts with nine thousand men and no reserve worth the name. It is thirty degrees below and the ground cannot be dug.<br><br>Hold the city and the approaches. Iglino on the Chelyabinsk line is where their assault groups form.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Ufa (3,17), Cherkassy (11,2), Kumlekul (6,4) and Alatorka (21,18).<br>- Take Iglino (37,21).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_04.xml", "Breakthrough: the Spring Offensive", "Breakthrough: the spring offensive<br><br>March 1st, 1919<br><br>This is the one they have been building all winter.<br><br>Khanzhin's Western Army has come out of the thaw straight at the junction of our 5th and 1st Armies with a three-to-one superiority on the axis of attack, and behind it Gaida is driving on Vyatka to join hands with the interventionists at Archangel. If those two ever shake hands the northern half of the Republic is cut off.<br><br>We have five towns on the railway and not enough of anything. Hold them. Ufa, behind their front, is their railhead and their whole supply rests on it.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Hold Belebei (12,16), Tuymazy (8,7), Abdulino (8,22), Sterlitamak (32,22) and Meleuz (32,28).<br>- Take Ufa (33,4).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_05.xml", "Rush: the Spring Offensive", "Rush: the spring offensive<br><br>March 14th, 1919<br><br>They have not stopped, and now there is nothing behind us to stop them with.<br><br>Khanzhin is driving for the Volga and Samara and he is doing it with everything at once, on a front too wide for his own supply, because he has been told the Volga must be reached before the Southern Front's own offensive begins. Our task is to make him pay for every verst and to still be holding these towns when his momentum runs out.<br><br>There is no counterattack in these orders. There is a clock, and a line of towns, and the requirement that both still be ours when the clock stops.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold six objectives for a brilliant victory, five for a victory, four for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are Ufa (33,4), Tuymazy (8,7), Belebei (12,16), Abdulino (8,22), Sterlitamak (32,22) and Meleuz (32,28).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_06.xml", "Song of the cossacks: Orenburg", "Song of the Cossacks: Orenburg<br><br>April 17th, 1919<br><br>Orenburg has been under siege, on and off, for most of a year.<br><br>Dutov's Orenburg Cossacks want it because without it their Host has no capital and no junction; we hold it because it is the only rail link to Turkestan and to the Soviet republics beyond it. Cut that and Central Asia is on its own.<br><br>The garrison is the town: railwaymen, the Kirghiz and Tatar detachments, a workers' regiment, and the 1st Army's left flank. The relieving force is going to Buzuluk instead, because Frunze is about to attack, and I would rather he did.<br><br>Hold the ring. There is one gap in their line, north of the river, and it may be worth closing.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold five objectives for a brilliant victory, four for a victory, three for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are Orenburg (8,30), Sakmara (16,19), Seitovsky Posad (10,21), Nizhnie Chebenki (24,18) and Verkhnie Chebenki (29,18).<br>- Or take their crossing at (24,4).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_07.xml", "Clutching at straws: defense of Belebei", "Clutching at straws: Belebei<br><br>May 15th, 1919<br><br>Now we attack, and we attack quickly, because the whole point of this is that they should not have time to think.<br><br>Frunze's southern group has already broken the Western Army at Buguruslan and Bugulma. Khanzhin is trying to reform on the Belebei position with his Volga Corps, which is the old People's Army under a new name and is being asked to do the work of two corps.<br><br>The 25th Rifle Division under Chapayev goes in first. There is very little time: everything here depends on hitting the position before it becomes one.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Belebei (12,16), Tuymazy (8,7), Buzdyak (16,7) and Shafranovo (19,14) - four turns for a brilliant victory, seven for a victory, ten at the outside.<br>- Hold Abdulino (8,22).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_08.xml", "The tide turns: Chistopol", "The tide turns: Chistopol<br><br>May 26th, 1919<br><br>This is the point on which the whole summer turns, and I would rather it were somewhere with better roads.<br><br>North of us Gaida's Siberian Army is still pushing on Vyatka and has not yet understood that the army on its left has collapsed. If we take Bugulma and the Azanakayevo junction now, that whole northern group is fighting with a hole where its flank used to be and the Urals are open to us.<br><br>If we do not - if this attack fails and their reserves come south in time - then it is their offensive again, and it will be aimed at the Volga crossings, and I shall be fighting it in front of Kazan.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Bugulma (25,20) and Azanakayevo (28,17).<br>- Hold Chistopol (6,9), Naberezhnye Chelny (23,4) and Menzelinsk (28,4).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_10.xml", "We'll never leave again: Kazan", "We'll never leave again: Kazan<br><br>June 10th, 1919<br><br>Twice in one year is more than any city should be asked for.<br><br>Our attack in May was held and the counterstroke that followed it has carried them back onto the Volga. Kazan is again the front line: the Kremlin, the academy, the crossings, and behind them the road to Nizhny.<br><br>The front is being rebuilt around this city while we hold it. Every division that comes up the line arrives because we were still here when it started loading.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold six objectives for a brilliant victory, five for a victory, four for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are the Kazan Kremlin (27,3), the Military Academy (26,2), Vasilyevo (22,3), Zelenodolsk (14,1), Teteyevo (28,18), Bogorodskoye (30,25) and the crossing at (9,26).<br>- Or take Bolshiye Kabany (32,9) and Pelevo (36,13).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_11.xml", "Where it all began: Samara", "Where it all began: Samara<br><br>July 14th, 1919<br><br>A year and a month since the Czechoslovaks took this bridge, and here we are arguing over it again.<br><br>Their advance down the Volga has not been stopped so much as slowed, and the front headquarters is moving its staffs between three threatened directions by rail, which is what happens when a front has more axes than reserves. My group has been sent here.<br><br>Hold the crossings. Melekess and Krotovka, upstream and east, are their staging points; either would be worth taking off them.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold three objectives for a brilliant victory, two for a victory or a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are Samara (30,23), Simbirsk (7,5) and Syzran (8,26).<br>- Or take Melekess (21,7) and Krotovka (41,23).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_12.xml", "No mercy: Vyatka", "No mercy: Vyatka<br><br>October 20th, 1919<br><br>Gaida is gone - Kolchak dismissed him in the summer and he has since tried to overthrow his own government in Vladivostok - but the Siberian Army's northern drive has been picked up by someone else, and it still wants what it always wanted: Vyatka, and a junction with the interventionists coming down from Archangel.<br><br>If they meet, the Republic is cut in half along the Northern Dvina and everything north of Moscow is on the wrong side of the line.<br><br>Hold the three city sectors and Karavayevy. Vakhrushi is their forward railhead.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold four objectives for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are the three Vyatka sectors (27,10), (24,16), (22,18) and Karavayevy (11,18).<br>- Or take Vakhrushi (40,8).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_13.xml", "The Black Baron: Saratov", "The Black Baron: Saratov<br><br>November 13th, 1919<br><br>The Eastern Front now has a southern neighbour, and the neighbour has arrived.<br><br>Wrangel's Caucasus Army has come up the Volga from Tsaritsyn to shake hands with Kolchak's people, which is the one thing both White commands have wanted all year and have never managed to arrange. Our task is to see that they do not manage it here either.<br><br>Saratov is two sectors and a river frontage, with Atkarsk covering the railway west. Volsk upstream is where their two forces are trying to link.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold three objectives for a brilliant victory or a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are the two Saratov sectors (16,12), (19,13) and Atkarsk (3,3).<br>- Or take Volsk (37,1).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}, {"id": 2, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_14.xml", "Mousetrap: Ryazan", "Mousetrap: Ryazan<br><br>December 12th, 1919<br><br>Ryazan is not a front-line town. It is where the roads from the south and the east meet before Moscow, and that is why I am standing in it in December with a group made of other people's spare regiments.<br><br>Five objectives, a river, and a railway junction. If this line goes there is one more behind it and then there is Moscow.<br><br>Venev, on the Tula road, is where their forward group has come up. It is worth a great deal to us and probably not much to them yet.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold five objectives for a brilliant victory, four for a victory, three for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are Ryazan (34,5), Kolomna (4,4), Turlatovo (41,11), Plakhino (35,19) and Kashira (2,24).<br>- Or take Venev (6,36).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_15.xml", "As though nothing could fall: Klin", "As though nothing could fall: Klin<br><br>December 30th, 1919<br><br>There is nothing behind this one.<br><br>Klin is on the Petrograd railway sixty versts from Moscow. Everything the Republic has been able to scrape together in a fortnight is in the line here: the courses cadets, two workers' regiments from the Moscow factories, the internationalist battalion, and the regiments that have been retreating since Saratov and are being asked to stop today.<br><br>Five towns. Hold them until the clock runs out. Their forward staging area is south of us and if it can be taken, take it.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold five objectives for a brilliant victory, four for a victory, three for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are Klin (11,6), Woronino (19,3), Rogatschewo (29,7), Fedoroloka (27,16) and Solnogorsk (16,18).<br>- Or take their staging area at (19,28).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_16.xml", "Peace through strength: Zhitomir", "Peace through strength: Zhitomir<br><br>May 19th, 1920<br><br>During 1919 Poland was a formidable foe for the Red Army, that tried in vain to expand to the west only to be defeated by the brave Poles. I am convinced that, were it not for Poland, the Bolsheviks would have reached the borders of Germany, Hungary and other countries, where they would have instigated successful communist revolutions. Most people in Europe don't realise how much they owe to Poland, that acted as a barrier to the Soviet expansion. Personally, I respect and appreciate what the Poles did.<br><br>However, the respect that we had for the Polish army, and the fact that the Bolsheviks were our common enemies for many months, couldn't hide the mutual enmity that existed between us. We knew that, once the Red Army was finally destroyed, Poland would become our new main enemy, at least in the short term.<br><br>But I must be clear about this: in 1920 we didn't want a war with Poland. Kolchak was resigned to accept the demands of the League of Nations and to leave the Poles alone. It was them who, blinded by their victories against the Bolsheviks, believed that they could force us to leave Belarus and Ukraine, where they would support the establishment of independent republics that (of course!) would be allies of Poland and enemies of Russia.<br><br>And that was how, in April 1920, Poland invaded Ukraine. Naturally, that act of aggression against us was condemned by the League of Nations, whose delegates made us know that if Russia used an armed force against the Polish Army, only for defensive purposes, the League would support us. That was all that Kolchak wanted, and he immediately sent an army to Volinia, in western Ukraine, in order to stop the Polish invasion.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take all the VHs.", [{"id": 1, "country": 20}], [{"id": 0, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser" ],
["simpob_17.xml", "You've got to know when to walk away: farewell to Ufa", "Farewell to Ufa<br><br>May 29th, 1919<br><br>Across the Belaya, then.<br><br>The Western Army is broken and the town it has been supplying itself from all spring is on the far bank of a wide river with one bridge. Chapayev's 25th Division goes across on rafts and pontoons north of the city; the rest of the group goes for the Chishmy junction to cut the line out.<br><br>There is no reserve and no second attempt. Twelve turns is what the front headquarters has given us, and it has given the same twelve turns to their rearguard.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Ufa (33,4) and Chishmy (22,7) within twelve turns.<br>- Hold Buzdyak (16,7) and Sterlitamak (32,22).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_18.xml", "Cry for the Romanovs: Ekaterinburg", "Ekaterinburg<br><br>July 12th, 1919<br><br>A year and a week since the house on Voznesensky Lane, and we shall be the ones who have to find out what happened in it.<br><br>The 2nd and 3rd Armies have come over the northern Urals and Ekaterinburg is the prize: the junction of everything, the Verkh-Isetsk works, and the last real city before Siberia proper.<br><br>Their evacuation began before our guns were in range. Six marked columns of staff, treasury and archives are trying to get out on the Tyumen line, and what is in them will decide what anyone is able to prove about this year afterwards.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take Ekaterinburg (15,3).<br>- Hold Severskiy (6,19) and Davydova (34,21).<br>- The enemy escapes instead if six of his columns get out at (36,9).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_19.xml", "The bear against the red wolves: Chelyabinsk", "Chelyabinsk<br><br>July 25th, 1919<br><br>We took this city four days ago and now we have to keep it, which the enemy has evidently decided is a different question.<br><br>The 5th Army came through the passes and into Chelyabinsk on the twenty-fourth. Kolchak's staff has been planning exactly this: let the Reds into the town, close on both flanks from Miasskoye and the north, and destroy an army in a street it thinks it owns.<br><br>So they will come, and they will come at both shoulders at once. The city rose to help us take it - the railway workshops turned out three regiments in a week - and those men are in the line now.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold six objectives for a brilliant victory, five for a victory, four for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are Chelyabinsk (25,11), Argayash (14,4), Dolgoderevenskoye (22,6), Poletaevo (20,16), Chebarkul (7,17) and Yemanzhelinsk (23,22).<br>- Or take Miasskoye (32,7).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_20.xml", "Not dead yet: The Tobol offensive (I)", "Not dead yet: the Tobol (I)<br><br>September 1st, 1919<br><br>They are not finished, and the men who told the front headquarters they were finished should come and look at this.<br><br>Kolchak's armies have been reorganised behind the Tobol - Dieterichs has combed out the rear areas, the Siberian Cossacks have been mobilised wholesale, and they have counted correctly that our own divisions are down to half strength and six hundred versts from their railhead.<br><br>The blow has fallen on our left, where the Cossack cavalry has the open steppe. Hold the line of villages. Petropavlovsk behind their front is the objective everything else here is a step towards.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold four objectives for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are Makushino (4,4), Petukhovo (15,7), Mamlyutka (27,9) and Presnovka (4,18).<br>- Or take Petropavlovsk (38,12).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}, {"id": 2, "country": 191}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_22.xml", "Better to burn out: The Tobol offensive (II)", "Better to burn out: the Tobol (II)<br><br>September 25th, 1919<br><br>Their offensive is a month old and it is running on nothing.<br><br>Every mobilised recruit they put into the line this month has been taken from a village that is now sending its sons to the partisans instead. Their supply comes down one railway with the Siberian partisan detachments sitting on it. They have gained ground and lost the army that gained it.<br><br>We hold the Kurgan crossings and the Tobol bank. Their two forward groups east of the river are what is left of their striking power, and both are within our reach.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold four objectives for a brilliant victory, three for a victory, two for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are Kurgan (13,14), Chashinskiy (4,7), Vargashi (25,17) and the Tobol crossing (9,24).<br>- Or take both of their forward positions at (39,22) and (27,29).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}, {"id": 2, "country": 191}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_23.xml", "Darkness falling: Novonikolayevsk\r\n", "Darkness falling: Novonikolayevsk<br><br>December 7th, 1919<br><br>Omsk fell without a fight three weeks ago. Their government left it by train and their army left it on foot, and the two have not been in the same place since.<br><br>What is in front of us now is the Great Siberian Ice March: half a million people - the remains of three armies, their families, the typhus - moving east along one railway in December, with the Czechoslovak Legion holding the line for its own trains and letting nothing else past.<br><br>Novonikolayevsk is the bridge over the Ob. Take it and the whole column east of here is cut off from the whole column west of here.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- Take the two Novonikolayevsk sectors (29,20) and (28,23).<br>- Hold Kolyvan (21,3), Lokti (38,5), Pavino (19,24) and the Novonikolayevsk approach (32,24).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_24.xml", "Crying souls: The Ice March (I)\r\n", "Crying souls: Krasnoyarsk<br><br>January 4th, 1920<br><br>Krasnoyarsk has taken itself.<br><br>The garrison arrested its own commander on the last day of December and the town is held by a revolutionary committee, the railway workers and Shchetinkin's partisan army out of the Yenisei taiga. Our own leading divisions are still four days behind.<br><br>Kappel's column is coming down the line towards it - what is left of three armies, on foot, in forty degrees of frost, and they have to get through this town or round it. They have nothing to lose, which makes them dangerous in a way that a supplied army is not.<br><br>Hold the city and the approaches with what is here. The partisans know this country and we do not; they are allies and they are to be treated as allies.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold three objectives for a brilliant victory, two for a victory or a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are the two Krasnoyarsk sectors (20,11), (23,12) and Drokino (18,9).<br>- Or take Areyskoye (11,9).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["simpob_25.xml", "Once we were here: The Ice March (II)", "Once we were here: Irkutsk<br><br>January 27th, 1920<br><br>The last of it, and it is being decided in a town that changed sides by itself.<br><br>The Political Centre rose in Irkutsk at the end of December and handed the city, and the Supreme Ruler, to the Revolutionary Committee three weeks later; the Czechoslovaks gave him up at the station in exchange for a clear road to Vladivostok for their own trains. Kolchak is in the prison here. So is the gold, or what is left of it.<br><br>Coming at us out of the taiga is what survived the march: Kappel died of frostbite and pneumonia on the road and Voitsekhovsky has the column now, and he has demanded the city, the prisoner and a contribution. Semyonov's Cossacks are east of the lake. The Baikal ice is the only way past us.<br><br>Hold Irkutsk and Listvennichnoye. Take Khomutovo, where their column is forming.<br><br>Victory conditions:<br>- When the time runs out, hold three objectives for a brilliant victory, two for a victory, one for a tactical victory.<br>- The objectives are the two Irkutsk sectors (17,8), (20,10) and Listvennichnoye (29,23).<br>- Or take Khomutovo (18,3).<br>- The enemy escapes instead if one of his columns reaches the ice road at Bolshoye Goloustnoye (40,19).", [{"id": 0, "country": 103}], [{"id": 1, "country": 100}], "eqp-kaiser"],
["Korean War - Battles of 1950-51 (CC76)"],
["w92_kor01.xml", "DEFENSE OF SEOUL", "Good morning commander. I'm going to make a brief introduction of the present situation. The North Korean Peoples Army have crossed the 38th paralel, striking the ROK forces alongside the frontier. So, the situation is hopeless and some people including the president Truman are believing that this is the beginning of the 3rd  World War... The forces of the Republic of Korea with their outdated equipment and few soldiers are not able to stop the Soviet equiped North Korean forces which are now at the gates of the capital of South Korea; Seoul. It's sure that we won't be able to hold Seoul for too long, however we will need some time to make an organised retreat of the ROK forces.<br><br>Your task is; manage the ROK forces to avoid a quick victory of the NKPA forces over Seoul. Fortunately, a US task force will help you from the turn 5. (You will receive enough prestige to build your task force in the 5th turn). <br><br>Good luck commander!", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor02.xml", "KUM RIVER LINE", "The withdrawal continues commander, and the situation has not any sight to be changed for now. The North Korean forces have arrived to the North of the important city of Taejon, which is surrounded by the Kum river.<br><br>Your mission this time is again to get enough time to make a good retreat to the South. You should establish a defensive line on the South bank of the Kum river, to gain enough time to save as much units as possible. Taejon must not fall until the established time, otherwise the remain units in other parts will be surrounded and surely defeated.<br><br>Good Luck.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 8 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor03.xml", "PUSAN PERIMETER", "Please, sit down general... The NKPA forces have conquered the most of the Korean peninsula. Now, the U.N. forces are trying to resist in the Pusan Perimeter. This area is established around the important port of Pusan, the last capital of the Republic of Korea. Pusan must not fall at any costs!, otherwise, the Communists will be victorious and Korea entirely unified under the communist sign of North Korea.<br><br>Your task is to resist the North Korean strike, and then, stage a counterattack to break the enemy lines. Our 8th Army have received some reinforcements like some M26 Pershing tanks and other units which will be a great help to deal with the commies.<br><br>Good luck commander!.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor04.xml", "INCH'ON LANDING", "If this operation is not finally sucessful, surely Harry will claim for my head!! hehe. Well, you are the proper commander to land on Inch'on, the traditional port of Seoul. Yes, you are right, the plans are to free Seoul from the North Koreans while they are busy at the Pusan Perimeter. A success in Inch'on, will mean that the NKPA forces will be in a complete disarray.<br><br>Intelligence reports that the enemy forces are consisting of mainly rookie units of two divisions which are currently still in the making.<br><br>Your mission is; land at Inch'on and then drive to Seoul. Liberate the capital from the Communists.<br><br>Good Luck!!!.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 8 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor05.xml", "ADVANCE TO PYONGYANG", "Good morning, commander. The U.N. forces have completely turned the situation, now we are in front of the North Korean capital. The perimeter of Pyongyang it's defended only by a few enemy divisions, but beware!; the North Koreans still have many U.N. POWs in the nearly areas of Pyongyang, and they can execute them, so a fast action it's mandatory there. <br><br>Take Pyongyang as soon as possible, and free the prisoners taking the North Korean capital city from the commies. Also take care: the North Korean soldiers will act as guerrillas as soon as their units become into disarray.<br><br>Good luck.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 10 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor06.xml", "BATTLE OF THE CHONGCHON", "Warning!, a huge chinese force have crossed the Yalu river and it's falling over our positions in North Korea. Your troops in the vicitinies of the Chongchon river are in the way of the chinese army and will receive the assault of the main PLA (Peoples Liberation Army) strike, which is probably intended to free Pyongyang. The mountains will be a great help for us, althought the Chinese army is largely bigger than our troops deployed here.<br><br>Good Luck!.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 18 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor07.xml", "CHOSIN RESERVOIR", "Warning!, the Chinese are launching an incoming strike on our forward positons at the  Chosin Reservoir. We should expect again a human wave assault. Althought the enemy it's outnumbering our troops, we think the higher quality of your troops can stop the chinese hordes, under this horrible icy weather...<br><br>Good luck.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 8 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor08.xml", "HUNGNAM EVACUATION", "This is a really bad situation, a good part of our troops are near to be traped in North Korea, and the only choice for an evacuation, it's to reach the port of Hungnam. Your task is to drive your units quickly to the port of Hungnam. Try to stop the chinese forces as much as possible while our units are embarking in the port... other units are retrating in other points of Korea, and a quick retreat will allow the PLA forces to use their troops agaisnt the other places.<br><br>I will ask Harry for nuclear support agaisnt the chineses, while you are doing your job, commander.<br><br>Good luck.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 14 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor09.xml", "OPERATION THUNDERBOLT", "[General Mathew Ridgway speaking]<br><br>Please sit down commander. I'm the new C-I-C of the U.N. forces in Korea. As you know, Seoul it's back on the communist hands. We can't allow a situation such this, so we have planned an operation to liberate Seoul and turn the things into a more favorable scenario for us.<br><br>You should fix the chinese forces at the right or our lines, and make a fast advance to Seoul by the left. Take care, the enemy T-34 are still a menace to our Shermans, althought we have the support of some M26 tanks.<br><br>Your task is clear; liberate Seoul!.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor10.xml", "CHINESE SPRING OFFENSIVE", "Warning!, the PLA and the NKPA are launching a full scale operation agaisnt our lines!. Our troops are largely outnumbered by the communists, but we can count on the higher quality of our brave men to save Seoul from the communist menace again.<br><br>You should try to stop the communist onslaught, and then launch a counterattack to restore the lines. Seoul must not fall!!!.", [{"id": 0, "country": 25}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor11.xml", "SPRING OFFENSIVE 2ND STAGE", "The communist Spring offensive it's closely to be stopped at the Seoul area. However, the enemy offensive remains powerful Eastwards to Seoul. Take control over the situation and stop the communist assault also here.<br><br>Good luck!.<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 17 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
["w92_kor12.xml", "THE FALL OFFENSIVES", "Since the last Spring, the PLA keeps some good forward positions which we are going to clear of communist troops, this is really important because there are near to sign a truce with the enemy, and the peace talks will start soon. It's politicaly important to get as much territories as possible, because the conflict can be renewed in the future. The vicitinies of the Soyang reservoir are garrisoned by an important number of PLA troops. Also the NKPA has some units in the North.<br><br>Your task is to recapture the Soyang reservoir area and clear the coast of enemy elements. The navy is here to help you bombing the coastal positions.<br><br>Good luck, maybe we will be in home at Christmas...<br><br>NOTE: Deployment zone is limited to 17 hexes.", [{"id": 0, "country": 21}], [{"id": 1, "country": 9}], "eqp-cc76" ],
]
